{"id": "FRK-DEF", "kind": "def", "statement_nl": "The Fricke matrix W_N = [[0,-1],[N,0]] over R, and its lift frickeW to GL(2,R) for N>0.", "lean_name": "SocrateAI.ModularForms.frickeW", "lean_file": "Lean/SocrateAI/ModularForms/FrickeInvolution.lean", "status": "proved", "depends_on": [], "paper_claim": null}
{"id": "FRK-01", "kind": "math", "statement_nl": "W_N has determinant N > 0, hence lies in GL(2,R)+.", "lean_name": "SocrateAI.ModularForms.frickeW_mem_GLPos", "lean_file": "Lean/SocrateAI/ModularForms/FrickeInvolution.lean", "status": "proved", "depends_on": ["FRK-DEF"], "paper_claim": "GL2-WN-01"}
{"id": "FRK-02", "kind": "math", "statement_nl": "W_N squared equals -N times the identity matrix; since scalars act trivially on H, W_N is an involution of the upper half-plane.", "lean_name": "SocrateAI.ModularForms.frickeW_sq_coe", "lean_file": "Lean/SocrateAI/ModularForms/FrickeInvolution.lean", "status": "proved", "depends_on": ["FRK-DEF"], "paper_claim": "GL2-WN-02"}
{"id": "FRK-03", "kind": "math", "statement_nl": "For gamma in Gamma0(N), the lower-left entry c is divisible by N (extracted from the ZMod N membership condition).", "lean_name": "SocrateAI.ModularForms.gamma0_dvd_lower_left", "lean_file": "Lean/SocrateAI/ModularForms/FrickeInvolution.lean", "status": "proved", "depends_on": [], "paper_claim": null}
{"id": "FRK-04", "kind": "math", "statement_nl": "The Fricke conjugate [[d,-c/N],[-Nb,a]] is an SL(2,Z) element lying again in Gamma0(N): its determinant is ad-bc=1 and its lower-left entry -Nb vanishes mod N.", "lean_name": "SocrateAI.ModularForms.frickeConj_mem_Gamma0", "lean_file": "Lean/SocrateAI/ModularForms/FrickeInvolution.lean", "status": "proved", "depends_on": ["FRK-03"], "paper_claim": null}
{"id": "FRK-05", "kind": "math", "statement_nl": "Intertwining: W_N * gamma = frickeConj(gamma) * W_N in GL(2,R). Proved entrywise; avoids inverses entirely.", "lean_name": "SocrateAI.ModularForms.frickeW_intertwine", "lean_file": "Lean/SocrateAI/ModularForms/FrickeInvolution.lean", "status": "proved", "depends_on": ["FRK-DEF", "FRK-03"], "paper_claim": null}
{"id": "FRK-06", "kind": "math", "statement_nl": "Conjugation: W_N gamma W_N^{-1} = frickeConj(gamma), by the intertwining identity and one cancellation.", "lean_name": "SocrateAI.ModularForms.frickeW_conj_eq", "lean_file": "Lean/SocrateAI/ModularForms/FrickeInvolution.lean", "status": "proved", "depends_on": ["FRK-05"], "paper_claim": null}
{"id": "FRK-07", "kind": "math", "statement_nl": "Main theorem: W_N normalizes the image of Gamma0(N) in GL(2,R). This makes f |-> f|_k W_N an operator on forms for Gamma0(N).", "lean_name": "SocrateAI.ModularForms.frickeW_normalizes_Gamma0", "lean_file": "Lean/SocrateAI/ModularForms/FrickeInvolution.lean", "status": "proved", "depends_on": ["FRK-03", "FRK-04", "FRK-06"], "paper_claim": "GL2-WN-03"}
{"id": "FRK-08", "kind": "math", "statement_nl": "The slash action of W_N maps SlashInvariantForm (Gamma0 N) k to SlashInvariantForm (Gamma0 N) k: slash-invariance is preserved under the normalizer, via the intertwining identity and the slash cocycle.", "lean_name": "SocrateAI.ModularForms.slash_frickeW_invariant", "lean_file": "Lean/SocrateAI/ModularForms/FrickeSlash.lean", "status": "proved", "depends_on": ["FRK-07"], "paper_claim": null}
{"id": "FRK-09", "kind": "math", "statement_nl": "Transport of holomorphy (via MDifferentiable.slash) and boundedness-at-cusps (via OnePoint.IsBoundedAt.smul_iff plus cusp-set preservation from FRK-07) along W_N: the Fricke operator is well-defined on the bundled ModularForm (Gamma0GL N) k.", "lean_name": "SocrateAI.ModularForms.frickeModularOperator", "lean_file": "Lean/SocrateAI/ModularForms/FrickeModular.lean", "status": "proved", "depends_on": ["FRK-08"], "paper_claim": null}
{"id": "FRK-10", "kind": "math", "statement_nl": "Composite of the Fricke slash with itself is multiplication by the explicit scalar (-1)^k * N^(k-2): derived from W_N^2 = -N.I and Mathlib's slash normalisation |det g|^(k-1) * denom(g)^(-k), where for the scalar matrix c.I one has det = c^2 > 0 (so sigma = id), c.I acts trivially on H, and denom(c.I) = c. Consequently for even k the operator f |-> N^(1-k/2) * (f |[k] W_N) squares to the identity, giving the +1/-1 eigenspace decomposition. NOTE: the constant is N^(1-k/2) as a MULTIPLIER (equivalently divide by N^(k/2-1)); the earlier wording of this node did not fix the direction.", "lean_name": "SocrateAI.ModularForms.frickeW_sq_slash", "lean_file": "Lean/SocrateAI/ModularForms/FrickeComposite.lean", "status": "proved", "depends_on": ["FRK-09", "FRK-02"], "paper_claim": null}
