{"id": "F31-A1", "kind": "math", "statement_nl": "The weight k = (1/2) sum_delta r_delta, taken in ℚ so it is total; integrality is the separate predicate HasIntegralWeight ('sum r_delta is even'). Weight is additive in the exponent vector, and HasIntegralWeight holds exactly when etaQuotientWeight N r is the image of an integer (hasIntegralWeight_iff), so the predicate is not a vacuous label.", "lean_name": "SocrateAI.ModularForms.etaQuotientWeight_add", "lean_file": "Lean/SocrateAI/ModularForms/EtaQuotient.lean", "status": "proved", "depends_on": ["F31-A0"], "paper_claim": null}
{"id": "F31-A2", "kind": "def", "statement_nl": "Ligozat's cusp-order expression ord(N,r,d) = (N/24) sum_delta gcd(d,delta)^2 r_delta / (gcd(d,N/d) d delta). NAMING CORRECTION to the brief: the free parameter is the DENOMINATOR d of the cusp c/d (d | N, gcd(c,d)=1); the numerator never appears. This is a DEFINITION only - nothing here asserts it is an order of vanishing of anything (that needs the eta multiplier system on Gamma0(N), absent from Mathlib). Status 'proved' means: typechecks, axiom-guarded in FinalCheck.lean, footprint [propext, Classical.choice, Quot.sound], no sorryAx. Transcription fidelity is separately PROGRAM-CHECKED (evidence label A2, not A1) by kernel-decided #guards next to the definition: the known divisor of Delta = eta^24 at level 1, and the valence identity sum_cusps phi(gcd(d,N/d))*ord = k*psi(N)/12 at levels 2, 4, 6, 9. Levels 4 and 9 are the ones with gcd(d,N/d) != 1, so they pin down the factor a careless reading drops; level 9 also has a cusp of multiplicity phi(3)=2. Guards confirmed non-vacuous: a perturbed value fails to compile.", "lean_name": "SocrateAI.ModularForms.etaQuotientCuspOrder", "lean_file": "Lean/SocrateAI/ModularForms/EtaQuotient.lean", "status": "proved", "depends_on": ["F31-A0"], "paper_claim": null}
{"id": "F31-A3", "kind": "math", "statement_nl": "At the cusp infinity (denominator d = N) the cusp-order expression collapses to (1/24) sum_delta delta*r_delta, since gcd(N,delta)=delta for delta | N and gcd(N, N/N)=gcd(N,1)=1. Numerator form (etaQuotientCuspOrder_infty_num): 24*ord_infty = (sum_delta delta*r_delta : Z) cast to Q. This is the quantity in Ligozat's first congruence. PROVED for all N != 0 and all r : N -> Z; both theorems are axiom-guarded in FinalCheck.lean with footprint [propext, Classical.choice, Quot.sound], no sorryAx. SCOPE: this is a theorem ABOUT the transcribed definition F31-A2, i.e. an identity of rational numbers (A1). It does NOT assert that etaQuotientCuspOrder is an order of vanishing of an eta quotient - that reading still rests on F31-A2's program-checked (A2) transcription and on the absent eta multiplier system (see F32-OBSTRUCTED). Consistency: at N=9, r=rTest9 it returns (1*1+3*0+9*1)/24 = 5/12, the value the #guard block next to the definition already pins down.", "lean_name": "SocrateAI.ModularForms.etaQuotientCuspOrder_infty", "lean_file": "Lean/SocrateAI/ModularForms/EtaQuotient.lean", "status": "proved", "depends_on": ["F31-A2"], "paper_claim": null}
{"id": "F31-A4", "kind": "math", "statement_nl": "At the cusp 0 (denominator d = 1) the cusp-order expression collapses to (N/24) sum_delta r_delta/delta, since gcd(1,delta)=1 and gcd(1,N)=1.", "lean_name": "SocrateAI.ModularForms.etaQuotientCuspOrder_zero", "lean_file": "Lean/SocrateAI/ModularForms/EtaQuotient.lean", "status": "proved", "depends_on": ["F31-A2"], "paper_claim": null}
{"id": "F31-A5", "kind": "math", "statement_nl": "Rewriting of ord_0 as (1/24) sum_delta (N/delta)*r_delta, the quantity in Ligozat's SECOND congruence. PROVED from F31-A4 (etaQuotientCuspOrder_zero) by moving the constant N inside the sum: delta | N makes the natural-number division N/delta exact, so Nat.cast_div gives ((N/delta : N) : Q) = (N:Q)/(delta:Q), applied pointwise under Finset.sum_congr where membership in N.divisors is in hand (a global push_cast would be unsound: ((2/4 : N) : Q) = 0). Nat.sum_div_divisors is NOT needed on this route. Axiom footprint [propext, Classical.choice, Quot.sound], guarded in FinalCheck.lean. Consistency #guard at N=9: (9*1+3*0+1*1)/24 = 5/12, matching the A2 valence guard.", "lean_name": "SocrateAI.ModularForms.etaQuotientCuspOrder_zero_eq", "lean_file": "Lean/SocrateAI/ModularForms/EtaQuotient.lean", "status": "proved", "depends_on": ["F31-A4"], "paper_claim": null}
{"id": "F31-A6", "kind": "math", "statement_nl": "HEADLINE etaQuotientCuspOrder_add; the node also proves etaQuotientCuspOrder_smul and etaQuotientCuspOrder_zero_exp (same file, same footprint, all three guarded in FinalCheck.lean). The cusp-order expression is Z-linear in the exponent vector: additive (etaQuotientCuspOrder_add), homogeneous (etaQuotientCuspOrder_smul), and zero on the zero vector (etaQuotientCuspOrder_zero_exp). PROVED. This is what makes the order compositional: it is read off one eta-factor at a time, and Ligozat's holomorphy hypothesis becomes a system of LINEAR inequalities in r, the form in which it is actually solved. Proofs are mechanical: _add splits the summand by mul_add, pushes through the common denominator by add_div and uses Finset.sum_add_distrib; _smul pulls the scalar out of each summand (Pi.smul_apply, smul_eq_mul, Int.cast_mul, then ring in the field Q) and then out of the sum by Finset.mul_sum used right-to-left; _zero_exp is simp. NOTE: neither _add nor _smul needs any hypothesis on N or d - the identities hold termwise even where the denominator gcd(d, N/d)*d*delta vanishes, because x/0 = 0 in Q. Like its A3/A4/A5 siblings this is A1 for the identities of rational numbers it states and claims NOTHING about eta; it inherits the A2 transcription status of the definition for the reading 'this is an order of vanishing'. Axiom footprint [propext, Classical.choice, Quot.sound] for all three, guarded in FinalCheck.lean.", "lean_name": "SocrateAI.ModularForms.etaQuotientCuspOrder_add", "lean_file": "Lean/SocrateAI/ModularForms/EtaQuotient.lean", "status": "proved", "depends_on": ["F31-A2"], "paper_claim": null}
{"id": "F31-A7", "kind": "math", "statement_nl": "HEADLINE ligozatCongr1_iff; the node also proves ligozatCongr2_iff, the three predicates LigozatCongr1 / LigozatCongr2 / LigozatHolomorphic, the shared engine dvd24_iff_isInt_of_mul_eq and the cleared-denominator lemma etaQuotientCuspOrder_zero_num (same file, same footprint, all guarded in FinalCheck.lean). PROVED. Ligozat's three hypotheses are stated as predicates on (N, r) ALONE - no modular form, no eta, no upper half-plane occurs in any of them - and the two bridge lemmas identify each congruence with integrality of a cusp order: ligozatCongr1_iff says 24 | sum_delta delta*r_delta IFF etaQuotientCuspOrder N r N is the image of an integer, and ligozatCongr2_iff says 24 | sum_delta (N/delta)*r_delta IFF etaQuotientCuspOrder N r 1 is. Proof: both are one application of dvd24_iff_isInt_of_mul_eq, the arithmetic fact that a rational q with 24*q = (S : Q), S an integer, is itself an integer exactly when 24 | S (forward: mul_left_cancel_zero with (24 : Q) != 0; backward: injectivity of Int.cast via exact_mod_cast). The two instances are fed by etaQuotientCuspOrder_infty_num (A3) and by the new etaQuotientCuspOrder_zero_num (the A5 identity with denominators cleared). NOTE on the A5 numerator lemma: push_cast must NOT be used there - it fires Int.ofNat_div and rewrites ((N/delta : N) : Z) to the truncated integer quotient (N : Z)/(delta : Z), which no longer matches; the three cast lemmas Int.cast_sum, Int.cast_mul, Int.cast_natCast are named explicitly instead. SCOPE: these are equivalences between a divisibility in Z and an integrality in Q. They are A1 for exactly that, and inherit the A2 transcription status of etaQuotientCuspOrder for the reading 'this is an order of vanishing'. Neither is the assertion that the eta quotient is invariant under T or under W_N - those readings are F32-A6 and F32-A8, they require the eta multiplier system (absent from Mathlib), and nothing in EtaQuotient.lean claims them. Axiom footprint [propext, Classical.choice, Quot.sound] for all seven declarations, guarded in FinalCheck.lean.", "lean_name": "SocrateAI.ModularForms.ligozatCongr1_iff", "lean_file": "Lean/SocrateAI/ModularForms/EtaQuotient.lean", "status": "proved", "depends_on": ["F31-A3", "F31-A5"], "paper_claim": null}
{"id": "F31-A8", "kind": "math", "statement_nl": "HEADLINE dedekindPsi_mul; the node also proves dedekindPsi_prime_pow and numCusps_mul, and introduces the two definitions dedekindPsi and numCusps (same file, same footprint, all five guarded in FinalCheck.lean). PROVED. dedekindPsi N is the Dedekind psi function psi(N) = N * prod_{p|N} (1 + 1/p), written in the division-free form (prod_{p|N} (p+1)) * (N / prod_{p|N} p) so that it is a natural number; the N-division is exact because prod_{p|N} p divides N (Nat.prod_primeFactors_dvd). numCusps N is the divisor sum sum_{d|N} phi(gcd(d, N/d)). Three theorems: (1) dedekindPsi_mul, psi(mn) = psi(m) psi(n) for coprime m,n - proof is Nat.Coprime.primeFactors_mul to split the prime-factor set as a disjoint union, Finset.prod_union twice (once for the (p+1) product, once for the radical), and Nat.mul_div_mul_comm with Nat.prod_primeFactors_dvd to split the radical quotient, closed by mul_mul_mul_comm. NOTE the brief carried hypotheses m != 0 and n != 0: they are NOT needed (Nat.Coprime.primeFactors_mul and Nat.prod_primeFactors_dvd are unconditional, and Coprime 0 n already forces n = 1) and were DROPPED, which strengthens the statement. (2) dedekindPsi_prime_pow, psi(p^k) = p^(k-1) (p+1) for p prime and k >= 1, via Nat.primeFactors_pow_succ and Nat.Prime.primeFactors collapsing both products to a single factor. (3) numCusps_mul, multiplicativity of the cusp-count divisor sum on coprime arguments, proved by Finset.sum_nbij' along the divisor bijection d -> (gcd d m, gcd d n) with inverse (a,b) -> a*b; both round trips are Nat.Coprime.gcd_mul plus the core cancellation lemmas Nat.Coprime.gcd_mul_right_cancel / gcd_mul_left_cancel, and the summands match by a private auxiliary lemma that computes gcd(ab, (mn)/(ab)) = gcd(a, m/a) * gcd(b, n/b) and applies Nat.totient_mul. SCOPE - read this before citing the node: what is proved is ARITHMETIC ONLY. The classical readings 'psi(N) = [SL(2,Z) : Gamma0(N)]' and 'numCusps N is the number of cusps of Gamma0(N)' are NOT proved here and are nowhere claimed in the Lean file: Mathlib has no Gamma0(N) index formula and no cusp-count theorem (grep confirms), and no group theory occurs in this node. The two definitions are pinned numerically by eight kernel-decided #guards in EtaQuotient.lean: psi(1)=1, psi(5)=6, psi(8)=12, psi(12)=24, psi(4)*psi(3)=psi(12), numCusps 1 = 1, numCusps 12 = 6, numCusps 4 * numCusps 3 = numCusps 12. Axiom footprint [propext, Classical.choice, Quot.sound] for all five declarations, guarded in FinalCheck.lean.", "lean_name": "SocrateAI.ModularForms.dedekindPsi_mul", "lean_file": "Lean/SocrateAI/ModularForms/EtaQuotient.lean", "status": "proved", "depends_on": ["F31-A0"], "paper_claim": null}
{"id": "F31-A9", "kind": "math", "statement_nl": "HEADLINE sum_totient_gcd_sq_div. PROVED. The per-delta core identity of F3.1: for every N != 0 and every divisor delta of N, sum_{d|N} phi(gcd(d, N/d)) * gcd(d,delta)^2 / (gcd(d, N/d) * d) = delta * psi(N) / N, an identity in Q with psi = dedekindPsi from F31-A8. The node also proves the definition ligozatCuspSum (the left-hand side as a function of (N, delta)) and the three lemmas ligozatCuspSum_prime_pow, ligozatCuspSum_mul, ligozatCuspSum_eq; all five are guarded in FinalCheck.lean. PROOF: Nat.recOnPosPrimePosCoprime on N with delta universally quantified inside the motive. (a) N = 0 is vacuous because Nat.divisors 0 = empty. (b) Coprime step: both sides are multiplicative in the PAIR (N, delta) - ligozatCuspSum_mul reuses the divisor bijection d -> (gcd(d,m), gcd(d,n)) that already proves numCusps_mul (F31-A8), with the three gcds splitting by two new private lemmas gcd_mul_gcd_mul and gcd_div_mul_of_coprime (the second is a refactor of the existing private auxiliary of numCusps_mul, which now goes through it), and the right-hand side splits by dedekindPsi_mul. (c) Prime-power step: Nat.sum_divisors_prime_pow turns the divisor sum into a sum over range(k+1); each summand is put over the common denominator p^(k+1), the coefficient being p exactly at the two extreme divisors i in {0, k} (where min(i, k-i) = 0, so phi(p^0) = 1) and p - 1 in between (Nat.totient_prime_pow_succ); the resulting numerator sum splits at i = j into two geometric blocks p^k * sum_{i<j+1} p^i and p^(2j) * sum_{i<k-j} p^i (the second after reindexing by Finset.sum_range_reflect) and collapses by geom_sum_mul to p^(k+j) (p+1). SCOPE - read this before citing the node: what is proved is ARITHMETIC ONLY, an identity between rational numbers built from Nat.divisors, Nat.totient and Nat.gcd. The classical reading - that this is the valence identity for eta quotients summed over the cusps of Gamma0(N), each cusp denominator d occurring phi(gcd(d, N/d)) times - is a READING and is NOT proved here, for the same reason F31-A8's readings are not: Mathlib has no Gamma0(N) cusp theory and no eta multiplier system (grep confirms), and no modular form, no eta and no upper half-plane occurs anywhere in the proof. EVIDENCE for the statement itself, independent of the proof: a kernel-checked numeric instance at (N, delta) = (12, 4) in EtaQuotient.lean (both sides equal 8), plus a program check outside Lean over every N < 400 and every delta | N with zero mismatches (A2). New imports pulled into the file: Mathlib.Algebra.BigOperators.Field, Mathlib.Algebra.Ring.GeomSum, Mathlib.Data.Nat.Factorization.Induction, Mathlib.Tactic.LinearCombination. Axiom footprint [propext, Classical.choice, Quot.sound] for all five declarations, guarded in FinalCheck.lean.", "lean_name": "SocrateAI.ModularForms.sum_totient_gcd_sq_div", "lean_file": "Lean/SocrateAI/ModularForms/EtaQuotient.lean", "status": "proved", "depends_on": ["F31-A0", "F31-A8"], "paper_claim": null}
{"id": "F31-A10", "kind": "math", "statement_nl": "HEADLINE sum_etaQuotientCuspOrder. PROVED. THE VALENCE IDENTITY FOR ETA-QUOTIENTS, AS PURE ARITHMETIC: for every N != 0 and EVERY exponent vector r : N -> Z, sum_{d | N} phi(gcd(d, N/d)) * etaQuotientCuspOrder N r d = etaQuotientWeight N r * psi(N) / 12, an identity in Q with psi = dedekindPsi (F31-A8) and etaQuotientCuspOrder the Ligozat expression (F31-A2). No hypothesis on r: it holds for r violating both Ligozat congruences, and for r supported off N.divisors (the summation range ignores those values, by EtaExp.sum_divisors_congr). PROOF: three steps of bookkeeping on top of F31-A9. (a) Expand etaQuotientCuspOrder and regroup each summand so the delta-factor (N/24)(r_delta/delta) separates from the d-factor phi(gcd(d,N/d)) gcd(d,delta)^2 / (gcd(d,N/d) d) (Finset.mul_sum twice, then ring termwise). (b) Finset.sum_comm swaps the two divisor sums. (c) The inner d-sum is exactly sum_totient_gcd_sq_div (F31-A9), returning delta * psi(N) / N; delta and N then cancel legitimately because delta in N.divisors gives (delta : Q) != 0 and hN gives (N : Q) != 0 - this is the only use of hN - leaving sum_delta r_delta * psi(N) / 24 = etaQuotientWeight N r * psi(N) / 12. No new imports; no new Mathlib lemma beyond Finset.sum_comm, Finset.mul_sum, Finset.sum_congr, Finset.sum_div, Finset.sum_mul, div_self, Nat.pos_of_mem_divisors. SCOPE - read this before citing the node, because the name invites over-reading: what is proved is an IDENTITY OF RATIONAL NUMBERS about the transcribed definition F31-A2 and the arithmetic function F31-A8. It does NOT assert that etaQuotientCuspOrder is an order of vanishing of an eta quotient, that numCusps counts the cusps of Gamma0(N), or that dedekindPsi N = [SL(2,Z) : Gamma0(N)]; none of those three is proved anywhere in this development, and the last two cannot even be stated in Mathlib as it stands (no Gamma0(N) cusp theory, no index formula, no eta multiplier system - greps confirm). It is NOT the analytic valence theorem and contains no analysis, which is precisely why it is provable here while F32 is obstructed (F32-OBSTRUCTED). WHAT IT IS WORTH: it exhibits the numerical prediction the analytic valence theorem makes as a theorem of arithmetic, which is an independent check on A2's transcription - a cusp-order formula for weight-k forms on Gamma0(N) that failed this identity would be wrong. EVIDENCE for the statement itself, independent of the proof: kernel-decided #guards at N = 16 and N = 36 in EtaQuotient.lean, levels chosen because they have cusps of multiplicity phi(gcd(d, N/d)) = 2 (d = 4 at N = 16; d = 3, 6, 12 at N = 36), with each side of the identity additionally guarded separately so that a guard cannot pass by both sides being equally wrong; the N = 16 guard was confirmed non-vacuous by checking that deleting the phi(gcd(d, N/d)) multiplicity makes it fail to compile. Program-checked outside Lean on 4000 random (N, r), N <= 60, exponents in [-6,6], zero mismatches (A2). Axiom footprint [propext, Classical.choice, Quot.sound], no sorryAx, guarded in FinalCheck.lean.", "lean_name": "SocrateAI.ModularForms.sum_etaQuotientCuspOrder", "lean_file": "Lean/SocrateAI/ModularForms/EtaQuotient.lean", "status": "proved", "depends_on": ["F31-A0", "F31-A1", "F31-A2", "F31-A8", "F31-A9"], "paper_claim": null}
# --- F3.1-B0: build gate for the analytic (F3.2) layer. Not a theorem. ---
{"id": "F31-B0", "kind": "def", "statement_nl": "BUILD GATE, not a mathematical result. The Dedekind-eta analytic cone (Mathlib.NumberTheory.ModularForms.DedekindEta and .Discriminant, plus Analysis.Complex.Periodic, Analysis.Complex.UpperHalfPlane.Exp, Analysis.Calculus.LogDerivUniformlyOn, Analysis.Complex.SqrtDeriv and NumberTheory.ArithmeticFunction.Defs) is built and importable in this workspace. Verified by 'lake build' returning 'Build completed successfully (3398 jobs)' and by the FinalCheck guards, which run #print axioms on Mathlib's ModularForm.eta, eta_ne_zero, logDeriv_eta_eq_E2, eta_comp_eq_csqrt_I_inv, discriminant_T_invariant and discriminant_S_invariant. The lean_name is a verbatim re-export of Mathlib's S-transformation and is NOT a SocrateAI theorem; it exists so this gate node resolves and so that losing the .olean files fails the build instead of going stale.", "lean_name": "SocrateAI.ModularForms.etaAnalyticCone_available", "lean_file": "Lean/SocrateAI/FinalCheck.lean", "status": "proved", "depends_on": [], "paper_claim": null}
# --- F3.1-B1: the one analytic ingredient of F3.2-A1 that Mathlib never states. ---
{"id": "F31-B1", "kind": "math", "statement_nl": "The Dedekind-eta q-product factors are 1-periodic: ModularForm.eta_q n (z+1) = ModularForm.eta_q n z, for all n : Nat and ALL z : Complex (no upper-half-plane hypothesis is needed). Since eta_q n z = (qParam 1 z)^(n+1) and qParam 1 z = exp(2*pi*I*z/1), the entire content is that Complex.exp has period 2*pi*I (Complex.exp_periodic). VERIFIED ABSENT from Mathlib as a standalone lemma: Mathlib performs exactly this rewrite inline inside discriminant_T_invariant (Discriminant.lean:130, '<- exp_periodic (2*pi*I*z)') but never states it, so F3.2-A1 had nothing to cite when feeding tprod_congr. PLACEMENT DEVIATION: the brief named Lean/SocrateAI/ModularForms/EtaQuotient.lean; that file is the arithmetic layer whose import cone is deliberately Nat.divisors + Nat.totient only, and eta_q sits behind Mathlib.NumberTheory.ModularForms.DedekindEta, so the lemma is stated in EtaQuotientModularity.lean immediately above its only consumer, eta_T_transform. The statement itself is verbatim as scoped.", "lean_name": "SocrateAI.ModularForms.eta_q_add_one", "lean_file": "Lean/SocrateAI/ModularForms/EtaQuotientModularity.lean", "status": "proved", "depends_on": ["F31-B0"], "paper_claim": null}
# --- F3.1-B2: the eta T-transformation itself, standalone and hypothesis-free. ---
{"id": "F31-B2", "kind": "math", "statement_nl": "THE ETA T-TRANSFORMATION AS A STANDALONE THEOREM. PROVED. ModularForm.eta (z + 1) = Complex.exp (2 * pi * I / 24) * ModularForm.eta z, for EVERY z : Complex. The absence of a z in upperHalfPlaneSet hypothesis is deliberate and is SHARPER than the classical statement, not an oversight: ModularForm.eta is defined on all of C as qParam 24 z * tprod_n (1 - eta_q n z); the prefactor identity qParam 24 (z+1) = exp(2*pi*I/24) * qParam 24 z is pure Complex.exp_add on exp(2*pi*I*z/24); and the two tprod families are TERMWISE equal by F31-B1 (eta_q_add_one), so tprod_congr transports the product whether or not it is multipliable - off the upper half-plane both sides take the SAME junk value, so the identity survives there too. PROOF: three steps, no new machinery (LL-11) - simp only [Function.Periodic.qParam, <- Complex.exp_add] then congr 1; push_cast; ring for the prefactor; tprod_congr fed by eta_q_add_one for the product; simp only [ModularForm.eta] and ring. VERIFIED ABSENT from Mathlib at commit 905b95818e: greps for eta_T, eta_add_one, eta_periodic and eta_translate return no relevant hit. What Mathlib has is discriminant_T_invariant, which is the 24th POWER of this statement (Delta = eta^24) and therefore cannot be inverted to recover it - the 24th root of unity exp(2*pi*I/24) is exactly what dies when you raise to the 24th power, and it is exactly what Ligozat's first congruence 24 | sum_delta delta*r_delta constrains. LL-1 CROSS-CHECK, machine-checked, not prose: the companion theorem eta_pow_24_add_one raises the identity to the 24th power and derives eta(z+1)^24 = eta(z)^24, reproducing the CONTENT of Mathlib's discriminant_T_invariant from our theorem. A wrong constant (say pi*I/12 written as pi*I/24, or a stray sign) still elaborates in eta_add_one but fails there. Both theorems are additionally STATEMENT-PINNED by type ascriptions in FinalCheck.lean that fail to elaborate if a hypothesis is silently added or the constant moves. PLACEMENT DEVIATION, same as F31-B1: the brief named Lean/SocrateAI/ModularForms/EtaQuotient.lean; that file is the ARITHMETIC layer whose import cone is deliberately Nat.divisors + Nat.totient only, and ModularForm.eta sits behind Mathlib.NumberTheory.ModularForms.DedekindEta. Stating it there would force the whole eta analytic cone into the arithmetic file. It is stated in EtaQuotientModularity.lean immediately below eta_q_add_one instead. The STATEMENT is verbatim what was scoped. SCOPE - read this before citing the node: eta_add_one is a statement about eta under the SINGLE matrix T. It is NOT the eta multiplier system, NOT a statement about Gamma0(N), and NOT Ligozat's criterion. F32-A1 (eta_T_transform, the same identity written with exp(pi*I/12) and carrying an unused hz) is now a one-line corollary of this node - the tactic rw [eta_add_one]; congr 2; push_cast; ring was VERIFIED to close it and then reverted - but is DELIBERATELY LEFT AS A SORRY and still pinned as UNPROVED by the FinalCheck tripwire, so that flipping the F32-A1 node is its own commit with its own honesty-label update rather than a side effect of landing F31-B2 (LL-2, LL-7). Axiom footprint [propext, Classical.choice, Quot.sound] for both eta_add_one and eta_pow_24_add_one, no sorryAx, guarded in FinalCheck.lean.", "lean_name": "SocrateAI.ModularForms.eta_add_one", "lean_file": "Lean/SocrateAI/ModularForms/EtaQuotientModularity.lean", "status": "proved", "depends_on": ["F31-B0", "F31-B1"], "paper_claim": null}
# --- F3.1-B3: integer translations T^m; the eta T-transformation for all m in Z. ---
{"id": "F31-B3", "kind": "math", "statement_nl": "THE ETA TRANSLATION LAW FOR ARBITRARY INTEGER m. PROVED. ModularForm.eta (z + m) = Complex.exp (2*pi*I*m/24) * ModularForm.eta z, for EVERY m : Z and EVERY z : C. Needed downstream because Gamma0(N) contains every power T^m, not just T; the NEGATIVE half is not a formality, since T^(-1) is what appears when an element of Gamma0(N) is written as a word in T and V. Like F31-B2 the statement carries NO 'z in upperHalfPlaneSet' hypothesis, and for the same reason: eta is defined on all of C and the identity is transported termwise, so off the upper half-plane both sides take the SAME junk value. PROOF: Int.induction_on on m (case names zero/succ/pred in Lean 4.32.2, NOT hz/hp/hn), with F31-B2 (eta_add_one) as the single step in BOTH directions - upwards applied at z+i, downwards applied at z-i-1 and then INVERTED, which is legitimate because Complex.exp is nowhere zero, so mul_left_cancel_zero on Complex.exp_ne_zero applies. Exponentials recombine by Complex.exp_add; the 24th-power companion uses Complex.exp_int_mul then Complex.exp_two_pi_mul_I and _root_.one_zpow (the bare name one_zpow is AMBIGUOUS in this file's open namespaces - Matrix.one_zpow also matches). No new machinery, no new imports and no analytic input beyond B2 (LL-11). The node also proves the three cross-check theorems eta_sub_one, eta_add_two and eta_pow_24_add_int (same file, same footprint, all four guarded in FinalCheck.lean). LL-1 CROSS-CHECKS, machine-checked rather than prose - each states the classically correct value INDEPENDENTLY and derives it THROUGH eta_add_int, so a wrong constant fails there rather than elaborating silently: (a) m = 1 must reproduce eta_add_one on the nose (pinned by an ascription in FinalCheck.lean); (b) eta_sub_one, the m = -1 instance, which is the direction the induction proves by inversion, pinned with the constant written exp(-(2*pi*I)/24); (c) eta_add_two, the m = 2 instance with its right-hand side written as eta_add_one applied LITERALLY TWICE, which pins the SCALING in m - an exponent 2*pi*I*m/48, or 2*pi*I/24 with the m dropped, still elaborates in eta_add_int but fails this one; (d) eta_pow_24_add_int, the 24th power for every m, reproducing the content of Mathlib's discriminant_T_invariant along the whole translation subgroup. INDEPENDENT EVIDENCE outside Lean (A2): the q-product evaluated numerically at 5 points z of the upper half-plane and every m in [-4,4], max relative mismatch 5.9e-16, with three falsification controls (m/48, sign flip, m dropped) all producing residuals of order 0.3-1.1. STATEMENT PINS in FinalCheck.lean fail to elaborate if m is silently narrowed from Z to N - which would drop exactly the T^(-1) half the node exists for - if a z in upperHalfPlaneSet hypothesis is added, or if the constant moves. PLACEMENT DEVIATION, identical to F31-B1 and F31-B2 and for the same reason: the brief named Lean/SocrateAI/ModularForms/EtaQuotient.lean, but that file is the ARITHMETIC layer whose import cone is deliberately Nat.divisors + Nat.totient only, while ModularForm.eta sits behind Mathlib.NumberTheory.ModularForms.DedekindEta; stating it there would drag the entire eta analytic cone into the arithmetic file. It is stated in EtaQuotientModularity.lean immediately below eta_pow_24_add_one instead. The STATEMENT is verbatim what was scoped. VERIFIED ABSENT from Mathlib at commit 905b95818e: there is no standalone eta translation law of any kind (the greps recorded under F31-B2 for eta_T, eta_add_one, eta_periodic, eta_translate return no relevant hit), only discriminant_T_invariant, which is the 24th power and loses the 24th root of unity that Ligozat's first congruence 24 | sum_delta delta*r_delta constrains. SCOPE - read this before citing the node: eta_add_int is a statement about eta under the TRANSLATION SUBGROUP <T> alone. It is NOT the eta multiplier system, NOT a statement about Gamma0(N), and NOT Ligozat's criterion. F32-A1 (eta_T_transform) remains a sorry and is still pinned as UNPROVED by the FinalCheck tripwire; nothing in this node touches the F32 obstruction (F32-OBSTRUCTED). Axiom footprint [propext, Classical.choice, Quot.sound] for all four declarations, no sorryAx, guarded in FinalCheck.lean.", "lean_name": "SocrateAI.ModularForms.eta_add_int", "lean_file": "Lean/SocrateAI/ModularForms/EtaQuotientModularity.lean", "status": "proved", "depends_on": ["F31-B0", "F31-B2"], "paper_claim": null}
# --- F3.1-B4: LL-1 GUARD on B2 (not a new result); Delta = eta^24 must come back T-invariant. ---
{"id": "F31-B4", "kind": "math", "statement_nl": "LL-1 GUARD ON F31-B2, NOT A NEW RESULT. PROVED. Two theorems, both sorry-free. (1) discriminant_T_of_eta_add_one : for every z : UpperHalfPlane, ModularForm.discriminant (mk (z + 1)) = ModularForm.discriminant z, i.e. Delta(z+1) = Delta(z) on H, derived from F31-B2 (eta_add_one) ALONE via eta_pow_24_add_one. (2) discriminant_T_invariant_of_eta_add_one : Delta slash_12 ModularGroup.T = Delta - MATHLIB'S OWN STATEMENT ModularForm.discriminant_T_invariant, re-derived here WITHOUT citing Mathlib's lemma (the proof goes SL_slash_apply, modular_T_smul (T . z = (1:R) +v z), UpperHalfPlane.ext to identify (1:R) +v z with mk(z+1), then (1), then denom T z = 0*z+1 = 1 so the automorphy factor is trivial). WHY THE NODE EXISTS: eta_add_one is SELF-CONSISTENT. It was proved from the q-product by Complex.exp_add plus tprod_congr, and the prefactor step closes with 'congr 1; push_cast; ring' for WHATEVER exp argument the two sides actually have. Nothing INSIDE F31-B2 pins the constant 2*pi*I/24 against an external authority. Mathlib's discriminant_T_invariant is that authority: it is proved straight from discriminant_eq_q_prod with no reference to any eta-level T-transform. THE GUARD IS DELIBERATELY TWO-SIDED, and this is the substantive finding of the node: the 24th power ALONE IS NOT A SUFFICIENT GUARD. exp(2*pi*I/12) also has trivial 24th power ((e^{2 pi i/12})^24 = e^{4 pi i} = 1), so eta_pow_24_add_one - already guarded under F31-B2 - would SURVIVE a corruption of the constant from /24 to /12. Only landing on Mathlib's PROPOSITION rules that out, which is what theorem (2) does. The node therefore strengthens, rather than merely restates, the existing B2 guard. LOAD-BEARING VERIFICATION (run, output read, not asserted): with 'simp [ModularForm.discriminant]' and the appeal to eta_pow_24_add_one REMOVED, Lean reports 'unsolved goals ... eta (z + 1) ^ 24 = eta z ^ 24'. So F31-B2 really is what closes theorem (1); simp is not discharging the guard behind our backs. INDEPENDENT EVIDENCE outside Lean (A2): the q-product to 400 factors at 5 points of the upper half-plane gives max relative |Delta(z+1) - Delta(z)|/|Delta(z)| = 2.9e-15, with the falsification control (constant 2*pi*I/23, whose 24th power is NOT 1) producing residual 0.27. STATEMENT PINS in FinalCheck.lean: the SAME written-out proposition 'Delta slash_12 ModularGroup.T = Delta' is inhabited TWICE by ascription - once by Mathlib's discriminant_T_invariant and once by ours - so if either statement drifts, one ascription stops elaborating. PLACEMENT DEVIATION, identical to F31-B1/B2/B3 and for the same reason: the brief named Lean/SocrateAI/ModularForms/EtaQuotient.lean, but that file is the ARITHMETIC layer whose import cone is deliberately Nat.divisors + Nat.totient only, while ModularForm.discriminant sits behind Mathlib.NumberTheory.ModularForms.Discriminant. Stated in EtaQuotientModularity.lean immediately below eta_pow_24_add_one instead; the STATEMENT of theorem (1) is verbatim what was scoped. SCOPE - read before citing: NOTHING NEW IS CLAIMED. Theorem (2) is a re-proof of a Mathlib lemma, stated only so the re-proof is machine-checked to run through eta_add_one. Neither theorem says anything about the eta multiplier system, about Gamma0(N), or about Ligozat's criterion; F32-A1 (eta_T_transform) remains a sorry and is still pinned UNPROVED by the FinalCheck tripwire, and the F32 obstruction (F32-OBSTRUCTED) is untouched. Axiom footprint [propext, Classical.choice, Quot.sound] for BOTH declarations, no sorryAx, both guarded in FinalCheck.lean.", "lean_name": "SocrateAI.ModularForms.discriminant_T_of_eta_add_one", "lean_file": "Lean/SocrateAI/ModularForms/EtaQuotientModularity.lean", "status": "proved", "depends_on": ["F31-B0", "F31-B2"], "paper_claim": null}
{"id": "F32-A1", "kind": "math", "statement_nl": "PROVED. The eta T-transformation in the form F3.2 scoped it: for z in the OPEN upper half-plane (z in UpperHalfPlane.upperHalfPlaneSet), eta(z+1) = exp(pi*I/12) * eta(z). Lean: SocrateAI.ModularForms.eta_T_transform in Lean/SocrateAI/ModularForms/EtaQuotientModularity.lean. Axiom footprint [propext, Classical.choice, Quot.sound] - NO sorryAx - guarded by #guard_msgs in #print axioms in FinalCheck.lean, together with a longhand statement pin that fails to elaborate if the constant pi*I/12 drifts or the z-in-H hypothesis is dropped. HOW IT WAS PROVED, stated so the credit sits where the content is: this is a COROLLARY of F31-B2 (SocrateAI.ModularForms.eta_add_one), which proves the same identity with the constant written exp(2*pi*I/24) and with NO hypothesis on z, straight from the q-product (Complex.exp_add on the prefactor, eta_q_add_one under tprod_congr on the product). All that remains at this node is the numeral identity 2*pi*I/24 = pi*I/12, closed by 'rw [eta_add_one]; congr 2; ring'. The hypothesis hz : z in upperHalfPlaneSet is UNUSED and was kept deliberately, because it is verbatim the scoped signature and weakening a hypothesis is a change of statement; downstream work should cite F31-B2, the hypothesis-free form. VERIFIED ABSENT from Mathlib at commit 905b95818e (greps for eta_T, eta_add_one, eta_periodic, eta_translate return no relevant hit; Mathlib has only discriminant_T_invariant, the 24th power, which loses the root of unity). ALSO LANDED with this node, same file, same footprint, also guarded: SocrateAI.ModularForms.eta_T_transform_nat, the iterate eta(z + n) = exp(pi*I*n/12)*eta(z) for n : Nat, obtained by specialising F31-B3 (eta_add_int) at (n : Int) rather than by a fresh induction; it is the form the divisor-indexed product downstream consumes. It has no DAG node of its own. SCOPE, LOUDLY: this is eta under the SINGLE matrix T. It is NOT the eta multiplier system, NOT a statement about Gamma_0(N), and NOT Ligozat's criterion. Every other declaration in the F3.2 block (etaQuotient_pow_24, divisor_smul_comm, etaQuotient_pow24_slash, etaQuotient_multiplier, etaQuotient_T_transform, multiplier_T_eq_one, etaQuotient_fricke, multiplier_V_eq_one and the terminal multiplier_trivial_of_congr) is still a sorry, and F32-OBSTRUCTED is unchanged. The old inverted tripwire that asserted eta_T_transform depends on sorryAx has been replaced by a new inverted tripwire on multiplier_trivial_of_congr, so that the F3.2 terminal node cannot be reported as obtained on the strength of this node's clean footprint.", "lean_name": "eta_T_transform", "lean_file": "Lean/SocrateAI/ModularForms/EtaQuotientModularity.lean", "status": "proved", "depends_on": ["F31-B0", "F31-B2"], "paper_claim": null}
{"id": "F32-A2", "kind": "def", "statement_nl": "The eta quotient f(z) = prod_{delta | N} eta(delta*z)^{r_delta} as a finite product over divisors with integer (possibly negative) exponents, together with nonvanishing (etaQuotient_ne_zero, from eta_ne_zero) and holomorphy on the upper half-plane (differentiableAt_etaQuotient). PROVED (F3.2-A2), and the honest report is that this node's three deliverables were ALREADY LANDED sorry-free by the F3.1-B ladder that was built on top of this node's statement layer: the definitions etaQuotient (C-domain) and etaQuotientH (H-domain) in F3.1-B5, etaQuotient_ne_zero / etaQuotientH_ne_zero in F3.1-B7, and differentiableAt_etaQuotient / differentiableAt_etaQuotient_prod in F3.1-B8, with their side-condition lemmas natCast_mul_mem_upperHalfPlaneSet_of_mem, eta_natCast_mul_ne_zero_of_mem and differentiableAt_eta_natCast_mul. NO NEW PROOF WAS WRITTEN FOR THIS FLIP and no second copy of any declaration was created; depends_on has been widened to name B5/B7/B8, where the content actually is. What was added is the F32A2Pins section of FinalCheck.lean, which checks the one thing the B-ladder guards do not: that the landed declarations discharge the node AT THE SIGNATURE THE NODE WAS SCOPED IN. DEVIATION, STATED NOT GLOSSED: the node was scoped with the level a POSITIVE natural, def etaQuotient (N : PNat) (r : Nat -> Int) (z : C) := prod over (N:Nat).divisors of eta(delta*z)^(r delta). What is landed takes N : Nat. That is a GENERALISATION, not a weakening, and PINS 1-3 are the proof of it: each scoped PNat-statement is discharged by the landed Nat-form applied at (N : Nat), with no side condition and no repair term. The extra levels are degenerate rather than wrong - Nat.divisors 0 = empty, so etaQuotient 0 r z is the empty product 1, nonzero and constant, so both lemmas are TRUE there and merely vacuous (PIN 4 writes that value down). Nothing downstream leans on N = 0: every F3.2 modularity node carries 0 < N explicitly. WHAT WAS PROVED, IN ENGLISH (LL-1): for every level and every INTEGER exponent vector - positive, negative or mixed - the finite product over delta | N of eta(delta z)^(r delta) is a well-defined complex number, nonzero at every point of the OPEN upper half-plane, and complex-differentiable there. The analytic content is entirely Mathlib's (ModularForm.eta_ne_zero and ModularForm.differentiableAt_eta_of_mem_upperHalfPlaneSet, both verified present in Mathlib/NumberTheory/ModularForms/DedekindEta.lean); the work is Finset.prod_ne_zero_iff / DifferentiableAt.fun_finsetProd bookkeeping, zpow_ne_zero and DifferentiableAt.zpow (whose side condition 'f a != 0 OR 0 <= m' is discharged on the LEFT, which is why no sign hypothesis on r appears anywhere), and the 0 < delta side condition from Nat.pos_of_mem_divisors. PIN 5 is the r == -1 instance, where every factor is an inverse and DifferentiableAt.zpow's easy disjunct is false: a version of this node that secretly assumed 0 <= r delta - the version that would NOT support Ligozat's criterion, whose exponent vectors are genuinely mixed in sign - dies there. SCOPE - READ BEFORE CITING: a definition, non-vanishing, and differentiability at points of the OPEN upper half-plane, and nothing else. NOT holomorphy at or near a cusp (upperHalfPlaneSet is open and the cusps are not in it), NOT meromorphy on X_0(N), NOT any statement about Gamma0(N), the slash action, or the eta multiplier system. The Dedekind-sum obstruction recorded as F3.2-OBSTRUCTED is UNTOUCHED: the FinalCheck tripwire asserting that multiplier_trivial_of_congr still depends on sorryAx is unchanged and still passing, and all eleven remaining F3.2 sorries (etaQuotient_pow_24, divisor_smul_comm, etaQuotient_pow24_slash, etaQuotient_multiplier, T_mem_Gamma0, etaQuotient_T_transform, multiplier_T_eq_one, etaQuotient_fricke, matV_mem_Gamma0, multiplier_V_eq_one, multiplier_trivial_of_congr) are still sorries. AXIOM FOOTPRINT [propext, Classical.choice, Quot.sound] with NO sorryAx for all ten declarations (etaQuotient, etaQuotientH, etaQuotientH_apply, natCast_mul_mem_upperHalfPlaneSet_of_mem, eta_natCast_mul_ne_zero_of_mem, etaQuotient_ne_zero, etaQuotientH_ne_zero, differentiableAt_eta_natCast_mul, differentiableAt_etaQuotient, differentiableAt_etaQuotient_prod), each guarded by '#guard_msgs in #print axioms' in FinalCheck.lean. Final line of lake build: 'Build completed successfully (3476 jobs).'", "lean_name": "SocrateAI.ModularForms.etaQuotient", "lean_file": "Lean/SocrateAI/ModularForms/EtaQuotientModularity.lean", "status": "proved", "depends_on": ["F31-A0", "F32-A1", "F31-B5", "F31-B7", "F31-B8"], "paper_claim": null}
{"id": "F32-A3", "kind": "math", "statement_nl": "PROVED. The commutation identity delta*(gamma z) = gamma_delta*(delta z) for gamma in Gamma0(N) and delta | N, with gamma_delta = !![a, b*delta; c/delta, d] in SL(2,Z), and with equal automorphy denominators denom gamma_delta (delta z) = denom gamma z. Lean: SocrateAI.ModularForms.divisor_smul_comm in Lean/SocrateAI/ModularForms/EtaQuotientModularity.lean (block F3.2-A3). WHAT WAS PROVED, IN ENGLISH (LL-1): let delta | N with delta > 0 and let gamma = !![a,b;c,d] be in Gamma0(N), so N | c and hence delta | c. Put gamma_delta := !![a, b*delta; c/delta, d]. Then (i) det gamma_delta = a*d - (b*delta)*(c/delta) = a*d - b*c = 1, so gamma_delta is in SL(2,Z); (ii) for EVERY z in the upper half-plane, scaling by delta intertwines the two Moebius actions, delta*(gamma z) = gamma_delta*(delta z); (iii) the automorphy denominators agree ON THE NOSE, denom gamma_delta (delta z) = (c/delta)*(delta z) + d = c*z + d = denom gamma z. Conclusion (iii) is the point of the node: it is what will let F3.2-A4 collect the Delta-modularity factors across the divisors delta | N into a SINGLE power of denom gamma z. DECLARATIONS LANDED, all sorry-free, all with axiom footprint [propext, Classical.choice, Quot.sound] (NO sorryAx) and all guarded by '#guard_msgs in #print axioms' in FinalCheck.lean: divisorConjMat (the raw 2x2 integer matrix !![a, b*delta; c/delta, d], with c/delta INTEGER division), divisorConjMat_det, divisorConj (the same as an element of SL(2,Z)), the four entry simp lemmas divisorConj_zero_zero / _zero_one / _one_zero / _one_one, dvd_lower_left_of_mem_Gamma0 (delta | N and gamma in Gamma0(N) give delta | c), denom_divisorConj, divisor_smul_comm_explicit, and the existential form divisor_smul_comm that the node was scoped in. WHY THE EXPLICIT-WITNESS LEMMAS EXIST: divisor_smul_comm is an EXISTENTIAL, and an existential is only as informative as its witness. divisor_smul_comm_explicit and denom_divisorConj are stated with the witness named (divisorConj), and FinalCheck PIN 4 re-proves the node with the four entries of gamma' pinned to a, b*delta, c/delta, d, so a proof that satisfied the two equations with some other matrix - or that quietly used gamma itself - would fail there. PROOF INPUTS, all Mathlib (LL-11 - no new machinery): CongruenceSubgroup.Gamma0_mem plus ZMod.intCast_zmod_eq_zero_iff_dvd for N | c; Int.mul_ediv_cancel' for delta*(c/delta) = c; Matrix.det_fin_two_of and linear_combination for the determinant; UpperHalfPlane.coe_pos_real_smul, UpperHalfPlane.coe_specialLinearGroup_apply and ModularGroup.denom_apply for the two Moebius computations. NO ANALYSIS IS USED, and in particular UpperHalfPlane.denom_ne_zero is NOT used: the two Moebius quotients are rewritten to have a syntactically EQUAL denominator before anything is divided, so the proof never needs c*z + d != 0. DEVIATIONS FROM THE SCOPED SIGNATURE, STATED NOT GLOSSED, and each discharged by a FinalCheck pin. (1) The node was scoped with N : PNat and gamma an ELEMENT of Gamma0 N; the landed form takes N : Nat with gamma : SL(2,Z) plus a membership hypothesis, and carries an explicit hypothesis 0 < delta. That is not a hidden extra assumption: at a POSITIVE level, delta | N already forces 0 < delta, and PIN 1 proves it. (2) The node stated the first conclusion in C, as (delta:C) * (gamma z) = gamma' * (delta z); the landed form states it in H, as natScale delta hd0 . (gamma . z) = gamma' . (natScale delta hd0 . z). PIN 2 shows the scaled point really is multiplication by delta in C (((natScale delta hd0 . z : H) : C) = (delta:C) * (z:C)), and PIN 3 discharges the node AT THE VERBATIM SCOPED SIGNATURE - N : PNat, gamma : Gamma0 N, first conclusion in C - from the landed H-form. Nothing is weakened. FURTHER PINS: PIN 5 is the sanity check that gamma_1 = gamma at delta = 1; PIN 6 is a concrete computed instance, N = 4, delta = 2, gamma = !![1,0;4,1] in Gamma0(4), giving gamma_2 = !![1,0;2,1] - which is in Gamma0(2) and NOT in Gamma0(4), so the level really does drop by delta, exactly as the classical statement says. SCOPE - READ BEFORE CITING: this is matrix arithmetic on SL(2,Z) and the H-action. It says NOTHING about eta, about the eta quotient, about Delta, or about the eta multiplier system. It is a lemma FOR F3.2-A4, not a step of Ligozat's criterion. The Dedekind-sum obstruction F3.2-OBSTRUCTED is COMPLETELY UNTOUCHED: the inverted tripwire in FinalCheck.lean asserting that multiplier_trivial_of_congr depends on sorryAx is unchanged and still passing, and the F3.2 block of EtaQuotientModularity.lean still carries TEN sorries - etaQuotient_pow_24, etaQuotient_pow24_slash, etaQuotient_multiplier, T_mem_Gamma0, etaQuotient_T_transform, multiplier_T_eq_one, etaQuotient_fricke, matV_mem_Gamma0, multiplier_V_eq_one and multiplier_trivial_of_congr - every one of them downstream of this node, none implied by it. Final line of lake build: 'Build completed successfully (3476 jobs).'", "lean_name": "SocrateAI.ModularForms.divisor_smul_comm", "lean_file": "Lean/SocrateAI/ModularForms/EtaQuotientModularity.lean", "status": "proved", "depends_on": [], "paper_claim": null}
{"id": "F32-A4", "kind": "math", "statement_nl": "HEADLINE etaQuotient_pow24_slash. PROVED, sorry-free. STATEMENT, verbatim as landed: for every N : Nat with 0 < N, every exponent vector r : Nat -> Int and every gamma in Gamma0 N, ((etaQuotientH N r) ^ (24 : Nat)) slashed with weight (12 * sum over delta in N.divisors of r delta : Int) by (gamma : GL (Fin 2) R) equals (etaQuotientH N r) ^ (24 : Nat). IN ENGLISH (the LL-1 check): let f(tau) = prod_{delta | N} eta(delta tau)^{r_delta} with r an ARBITRARY integer exponent vector, mixed signs allowed. Then for every gamma = !![a,b;c,d] in Gamma0(N) and every tau in H, f(gamma tau)^24 = (c tau + d)^{12 * sum_delta r_delta} * f(tau)^24. NO congruence condition on r is assumed: neither 24 | sum delta r_delta nor 24 | sum (N/delta) r_delta appears in the statement or the proof. This is the step that DODGES the eta multiplier system and with it the Dedekind sums Mathlib does not have: passing to the 24th power replaces eta by Delta = eta^24, whose modularity is Mathlib's and is for the FULL modular group. PROOF, and the analytic input is entirely Mathlib's (LL-11). (1) eta_pow24_natScale_smul: apply SlashInvariantForm.slash_action_generators_SL2Z fed with ModularForm.discriminant_S_invariant and ModularForm.discriminant_T_invariant - i.e. Delta slashed by weight 12 is Delta, for EVERY gamma in SL(2,Z), verified present at Mathlib/NumberTheory/ModularForms/Discriminant.lean - at the CONJUGATED matrix gamma_delta = divisorConj h of F32-A3 and at the SCALED point delta*tau, then use F32-A3's divisor_smul_comm_explicit to rewrite delta*(gamma tau) as gamma_delta*(delta tau) and F32-A3's denom_divisorConj to identify the automorphy factor that comes back as denom gamma tau. Result: eta(delta*(gamma tau))^24 = (denom gamma tau)^12 * eta(delta tau)^24, with the ONLY hypothesis (delta : Int) | gamma 1 0 - no Gamma0(N) and no condition on r. (2) etaQuotientH_pow_24 rewrites f^24 as prod_delta (eta(delta tau)^24)^{r_delta}, i.e. as prod_delta Delta(delta tau)^{r_delta}, by Finset.prod_pow backwards plus the zpow helper zpow_pow24_comm ((x^m)^24 = (x^24)^m, unconditional in C, a CommGroupWithZero). (3) THE STRUCTURAL POINT, and it is the second half of F32-A3: the denom that comes back is denom gamma tau for EVERY delta | N, the SAME complex number, so prod_zpow_const collapses the delta-indexed automorphy factors into a single power ((denom gamma tau)^12)^{sum r_delta}, which pow_twelve_zpow rewrites as (denom gamma tau)^{12 * sum r_delta}. Had the denominators differed with delta, no single weight would exist and this node would be FALSE as stated. (4) The slash form is the pointwise form plus ModularForm.SL_slash / SL_slash_apply ((F slash_k gamma) tau = F(gamma tau) * denom gamma tau ^ (-k)) and one zpow_add0 cancellation, legal because UpperHalfPlane.denom_ne_zero. DECLARATIONS LANDED, all sorry-free, all with axiom footprint [propext, Classical.choice, Quot.sound] (NO sorryAx), each guarded by '#guard_msgs in #print axioms' in FinalCheck.lean section F32A4Pins: zpow_pow24_comm, prod_zpow_const, pow_twelve_zpow, etaQuotient_pow_24, coe_natScale_smul, eta_pow24_natScale_smul, etaQuotientH_pow_24, etaQuotientH_pow24_transform, etaQuotient_pow24_slash. TWO UNUSED HYPOTHESES, REPORTED NOT HIDDEN. etaQuotient_pow_24 carries hz : z in upperHalfPlaneSet and etaQuotient_pow24_slash carries hN : 0 < N; NEITHER IS CONSUMED, and both are renamed to _hz / _hN in the source with a comment saying so. The first is unused because zpow_mul is unconditional in C, so even the junk value at a zero base agrees on both sides; the second because at N = 0 the divisor set is empty, f is identically 1 and the weight is 0, so the statement is true but vacuous there. Both are KEPT because they are verbatim the scoped signatures, and weakening a hypothesis is a change of statement. This is a GENERALISATION, not a weakening. FOUR STATEMENT PINS (section F32A4Pins in FinalCheck.lean). PIN 1 is the scoped signature longhand - N : PNat, gamma an ELEMENT of Gamma0 N, the exponent vector the bare Nat -> Int rather than the EtaExp abbreviation, and the eta quotient written out as the product over Nat.divisors with ModularForm.eta fully qualified, so nothing hides behind our definitions. PIN 2 is the POINTWISE reading with the automorphy factor spelled c*tau + d instead of denom, which is the form a referee checks against the classical statement and where a transposition in the lower row of gamma would show up. PIN 3 pins the Delta-quotient identity against MATHLIB's object: f(tau)^24 = prod_{delta | N} ModularForm.discriminant(delta*tau)^{r_delta}, with Finset.attach only carrying the 0 < delta needed to form the point delta*tau : H. PIN 4 is the MATHLIB CROSS-CHECK RUN IN THE STRONG DIRECTION: at N = 1 and r identically 1 the eta quotient is eta itself, f^24 = Delta, the weight is 12*1 = 12 and Gamma0(1) = SL(2,Z), so this node REPROVES Mathlib's own 'Delta slashed by 12 equals Delta' for every gamma in SL(2,Z). A wrong weight normalisation, a wrong 24, or wrong divisor indexing dies there. NON-VACUITY CHECKED, not assumed: four perturbations fed the real proof term all fail to elaborate - (i) weight 6*sum r instead of 12*sum r (error: Type mismatch), (ii) f^12 instead of f^24 (error: deterministic timeout at isDefEq - it does not typecheck; the mismatch sits under Pi.pow so Lean burns heartbeats before reporting), (iii) weight 12*sum delta*r_delta, the F3.1 cusp-order sum, instead of 12*sum r_delta (error: Type mismatch), (iv) the pointwise law with denom^{-12 sum r} instead of denom^{+12 sum r} (error: Type mismatch). Recorded in scratch/A4perturb.lean, which keeps the failing forms as comments and the node itself as live code. SCOPE - READ BEFORE CITING. This is f^24, NOT f. It says NOTHING about the eta multiplier of f itself, NOTHING about Ligozat's two congruences, and NOTHING about any cusp: it is an identity on the OPEN upper half-plane. Extracting f from f^24 is F32-A5 (etaQuotient_multiplier) and is still a sorry. The Dedekind-sum obstruction F32-OBSTRUCTED is COMPLETELY UNTOUCHED: the inverted tripwire in FinalCheck.lean asserting that multiplier_trivial_of_congr depends on sorryAx is unchanged and still passing, and the F3.2 block of EtaQuotientModularity.lean still carries EIGHT sorry-carrying declarations - etaQuotient_multiplier, T_mem_Gamma0, etaQuotient_T_transform, multiplier_T_eq_one, etaQuotient_fricke, matV_mem_Gamma0, multiplier_V_eq_one and multiplier_trivial_of_congr - every one of them downstream of this node, none implied by it. Final line of lake build: 'Build completed successfully (3476 jobs).'", "lean_name": "SocrateAI.ModularForms.etaQuotient_pow24_slash", "lean_file": "Lean/SocrateAI/ModularForms/EtaQuotientModularity.lean", "status": "proved", "depends_on": ["F32-A2", "F32-A3"], "paper_claim": null}
{"id": "F32-A5", "kind": "math", "statement_nl": "HEADLINE etaQuotient_multiplier. PROVED, sorry-free. THE KEYSTONE, and the one soft step of the F3.2 ladder. STATEMENT, verbatim as landed: for every N : Nat with 0 < N (hypothesis NOT used - see below), every exponent vector r : Nat -> Int and every k : Int with sum over delta in N.divisors of r delta = 2 * k, there EXISTS a group homomorphism w : Gamma0 N ->* Cx such that (w gamma)^24 = 1 for every gamma, and for every gamma in Gamma0 N and every z : H, etaQuotientH N r ((gamma : SL(2,Z)) . z) = (w gamma : C) * (denom gamma z)^k * etaQuotientH N r z. NO congruence condition on r is assumed: neither 24 | sum delta*r_delta nor 24 | sum (N/delta)*r_delta appears in the statement or the proof. PROOF, and where its content comes from: by F32-A4 (etaQuotientH_pow24_transform, itself resting on Mathlib's full SL(2,Z) modularity of Delta) the ratio rho(gamma,z) = f(gamma z)/((denom gamma z)^k * f(z)) satisfies rho^24 = 1 - the exponents cancel EXACTLY because 12*(2k) = 24k, which is where the integrality of k is load-bearing. The ratio is well defined by F31-B7 (etaQuotientH_ne_zero) and continuous by F31-B8 (differentiableAt_etaQuotient); the 24th roots of unity are a finite, hence discrete, subset of C (finite_setOf_pow24_eq_one) and H is connected (Mathlib's ContractibleSpace H instance, UpperHalfPlane/Topology.lean:68), so rho is CONSTANT in z (eq_of_continuous_pow24_eq_one - the entire topological content, isolated as its own lemma). The homomorphism property is the automorphy cocycle denom_SL_mul (Mathlib's denom_cocycle transported along SpecialLinearGroup.mapGL R and coe_smul_of_det_pos), exact because k is an INTEGER. THE WITNESS IS NAMED, NOT CHOSEN: no Classical.choice is invoked to produce w. It is etaMultiplierHom r hk, with w(gamma) = f(gamma . i)/((denom gamma i)^k * f(i)) at the base point i : H; FinalCheck PIN 2 pins that by rfl. The node also lands, all sorry-free and all guarded in FinalCheck.lean: finite_setOf_pow24_eq_one, eq_of_continuous_pow24_eq_one, continuous_etaQuotientH, continuous_SL_smul, continuous_denom_SL, denom_SL_mul, etaMultiplierAux (+ _pow24, _const), etaMultiplierVal (+ _pow24, _ne_zero, _one, _mul), etaQuotientH_transform (the pointwise law F32-A6/A8 will specialise to T and V) and etaMultiplierHom. LL-1 EXTERNAL GUARD: etaMultiplierVal_level_one_24 - at N = 1, r = 24, k = 12 the eta quotient IS Mathlib's Delta, so the multiplier must be 1 on all of Gamma0(1) = SL(2,Z), and it is; etaQuotientH_level_one_24_transform runs the same check through the transformation law. A weight convention off by a factor 2, or a stray denom power absorbed into w, fails there. FinalCheck PIN 5 exhibits N = 2, r = (2,0), k = 1 - an exponent vector satisfying NEITHER of Ligozat's congruences - to pin the unconditionality as a sentence rather than as an absent hypothesis. UNUSED HYPOTHESIS, reported not hidden: hN : 0 < N is not consumed (the binder is written _hN). At N = 0 the divisor set is empty, f = 1, hk forces k = 0 and the statement holds with w = 1. SCOPE - READ BEFORE CITING: this is EXISTENCE of the multiplier plus its two structural properties (order divides 24; homomorphism in gamma). It does NOT evaluate w(gamma) for any general gamma, it is NOT Ligozat's criterion, it says nothing about the two congruences and nothing at any cusp. The Dedekind-sum obstruction F32-OBSTRUCTED is exactly the question of the VALUE of w(gamma), and it is untouched: the FinalCheck tripwire still certifies that multiplier_trivial_of_congr depends on sorryAx. Axiom footprint: [propext, Classical.choice, Quot.sound].", "lean_name": "SocrateAI.ModularForms.etaQuotient_multiplier", "lean_file": "Lean/SocrateAI/ModularForms/EtaQuotientModularity.lean", "status": "proved", "depends_on": ["F32-A2", "F32-A4"], "paper_claim": null}
{"id": "F32-A6", "kind": "math", "statement_nl": "HEADLINE multiplier_T_eq_one. PROVED, sorry-free. STATEMENT AS LANDED: for every N : Nat and every exponent vector r : Nat -> Int, if 24 divides sum_{delta | N} delta*r_delta (LigozatCongr1 N r, the F3.1-A7 predicate) then for every z : H, etaQuotientH N r (ModularGroup.T . z) = etaQuotientH N r z. WHAT WAS PROVED, IN ENGLISH (LL-1): let f(z) = prod_{delta | N} eta(delta*z)^{r_delta} with r an ARBITRARY integer exponent vector, mixed signs allowed. Then (a) f(z+1) = exp(pi*i*(sum_delta delta*r_delta)/12) * f(z) for every z, and (b) writing S = sum_delta delta*r_delta, the three statements '24 | S', 'f(Tz) = f(z) for all z in H' and 'w(T) = 1' are EQUIVALENT, where w : Gamma0(N) ->* Cx is the character produced by F32-A5. The middle and right forms coincide because denom T z = 1 (denom_T, proved not assumed), which is why multiplier_T_eq_one needs no weight hypothesis hk and no k at all while etaMultiplierVal_T_eq_one does. THE CONVERSE DIRECTION IS PROVED, and that is what makes the node's word 'exactly' a theorem rather than a gloss: ligozatCongr1_iff_T_invariant is an IFF - if f(Tz) = f(z) at even the single point z = i then exp(pi*i*S/12) = 1, so pi*i*S/12 = n*2*pi*i for some integer n (Complex.exp_eq_one_iff), and cancelling the nonzero pi*i gives S = 24n. DECLARATIONS LANDED, all sorry-free, all with axiom footprint [propext, Classical.choice, Quot.sound] (NO sorryAx), each guarded by '#guard_msgs in #print axioms' in FinalCheck.lean: T_mem_Gamma0, etaQuotient_T_transform, coe_T_smul, etaQuotientH_T_smul, multiplier_T_eq_one, denom_T, etaMultiplierVal_T_eq_one, etaMultiplierHom_T_eq_one, ligozatCongr1_iff_T_invariant, etaQuotient_T_transform_level_one_pin, etaQuotient_T_transform_level_two_pin, ligozatCongr1_level_one_24, discriminant_T_via_multiplier, eta_not_T_invariant. PROOF INPUTS, all already in the library or in Mathlib (LL-11 - no new machinery, no Dedekind sums): F31-B3 (eta_add_int, eta(z+m) = exp(2*pi*i*m/24)*eta(z) for INTEGER m, proved from the q-product) applied factorwise at the point delta*z and the integer delta, since (delta:C)*(z+1) = delta*z + delta; then mul_zpow, Complex.exp_int_mul backwards to turn (exp c)^{r_delta} into exp(r_delta*c), Finset.prod_mul_distrib and Complex.exp_sum to collect, and Finset.mul_sum / Finset.sum_div for the exponent. Membership T in Gamma0(N) is Gamma0_mem plus ModularGroup.coe_T (lower-left entry 0, so the congruence holds for EVERY N). The H-action is Mathlib's UpperHalfPlane.modular_T_smul. denom T z = 1 is ModularGroup.denom_apply plus coe_T. UNUSED HYPOTHESIS, REPORTED NOT HIDDEN: etaQuotient_T_transform carries _hz : z in upperHalfPlaneSet and does NOT consume it - eta_add_int holds on all of C and every other step is zpow/exp algebra valid at any base. The binder is renamed to _hz with a comment; the hypothesis is KEPT because it is verbatim the scoped signature and weakening a hypothesis is a change of statement. FinalCheck PIN 2 pins the statement WITH the hypothesis. FIVE STATEMENT PINS (section F32A6Pins in FinalCheck.lean). PIN 1 is the SCOPED SIGNATURE in the node's own words: N : PNat, the hypothesis written as the CONGRUENCE ((sum delta*r_delta : Z) : ZMod 24) = 0 rather than as a divisibility, and the conclusion w <T, T_mem_Gamma0 N> = 1 for the BUNDLED character etaMultiplierHom of F32-A5 - a proof that only established 1-periodicity without connecting it to w would not satisfy it. PIN 2 is the transformation law longhand, no SocrateAI definition on either side, the product over Nat.divisors with ModularForm.eta fully qualified and the constant written with Real.pi and Complex.I. PIN 3 is the IFF longhand. PIN 4 is denom T z = 1 written as c*z + d with the entries of T. PIN 5 is NON-VACUITY as a sentence: eta itself is NOT 1-periodic (at N = 1, r = 1 the congruence is 24 | 1, false), so a version of this node whose conclusion held for every r dies there. TWO FURTHER LL-1 GUARDS IN THE SOURCE FILE: etaQuotient_T_transform_level_two_pin fixes N = 2, f(z) = eta(2z) and demands the constant exp(2*pi*i/12), so a transcription that summed r_delta instead of delta*r_delta fails; and discriminant_T_via_multiplier proves Delta(z+1) = Delta(z) by this node's route, next to an example proving the same statement from MATHLIB's full-level modularity of Delta through denom_T - two independent proofs of one statement, which disagree if our constant exp(pi*i*24/12) is not 1. SCOPE - READ BEFORE CITING: this is the multiplier at the SINGLE generator T, plus the exact arithmetic condition for it to be trivial. It is NOT Ligozat's criterion. Nothing here evaluates w at any gamma outside <T>, nothing here is about the Fricke conjugate V (F32-A8) or about any cusp, and the reduction of Gamma0(N) to T, V and -I remains the named obstruction F32-OBSTRUCTED. The inverted tripwire in FinalCheck.lean asserting that multiplier_trivial_of_congr depends on sorryAx is unchanged and still passing, and the F3.2 block of EtaQuotientModularity.lean still carries FOUR sorries - etaQuotient_fricke, matV_mem_Gamma0, multiplier_V_eq_one and multiplier_trivial_of_congr. Final line of lake build: 'Build completed successfully (3476 jobs).'", "lean_name": "SocrateAI.ModularForms.multiplier_T_eq_one", "lean_file": "Lean/SocrateAI/ModularForms/EtaQuotientModularity.lean", "status": "proved", "depends_on": ["F32-A1", "F32-A2", "F32-A5", "F31-A7", "F31-B3", "F31-B7"], "paper_claim": null}
{"id": "F32-A7", "kind": "math", "statement_nl": "HEADLINE etaQuotient_fricke. PROVED, sorry-free. STATEMENT, verbatim as landed: for every N : Nat with 0 < N, every exponent vector r : Nat -> Int, every k : Int with sum over delta in N.divisors of r delta = 2*k, and every z : C with z in upperHalfPlaneSet, etaQuotient N r (-(1/((N:C)*z))) = I^(-k) * (N:C)^k * ((Real.sqrt (prod over delta in N.divisors of (delta:R)^(r delta)) : R) : C)^{-1} * z^k * etaQuotient N (fun delta => r (N/delta)) z. WHAT WAS PROVED, IN ENGLISH (LL-1): let f(z) = prod_{delta | N} eta(delta z)^{r_delta} with r an ARBITRARY integer exponent vector, mixed signs allowed, and suppose the weight sum is EVEN, sum_delta r_delta = 2k with k an integer. Then on the open upper half-plane the Fricke involution z -> -1/(Nz) sends f to its DUAL quotient f*(z) = prod_{delta | N} eta(delta z)^{r_{N/delta}} - the exponent vector reversed along the divisor involution delta -> N/delta - times the explicit constant i^{-k} * N^k * s^{-1/2} * z^k, where s = prod_{delta | N} delta^{r_delta} is a POSITIVE REAL and s^{-1/2} is (Real.sqrt s)^{-1}. NO congruence condition on r is assumed: neither 24 | sum delta*r_delta nor 24 | sum (N/delta)*r_delta appears in the statement or in the proof. PROOF INPUTS, and the analytic content is entirely Mathlib's (LL-11 - no new machinery, no Dedekind sums). The single analytic input is ModularForm.eta_comp_eq_csqrt_I_inv (eta(-1/w) = (sqrt I)^{-1} * sqrt w * eta w on upperHalfPlaneSet, verified present at Mathlib/NumberTheory/ModularForms/Discriminant.lean); it is USED, not reproved. Everything else is the bookkeeping the node was scoped around, and that bookkeeping is the work: (1) eta_fricke_factor turns delta*(-1/(Nz)) into -1/((N/delta)z) by the divisor identity delta*(N/delta) = N and then applies the Mathlib S-transform at the point (N/delta)*z, which lies in upperHalfPlaneSet because N/delta is a POSITIVE natural; (2) csqrt_ofReal_mul is THE BRANCH STEP: sqrt(m*z) = sqrt(m)*sqrt(z) for m a positive REAL and any z != 0. That identity is FALSE for a general complex scalar - it is exactly where the cut would be crossed - and it holds here because Complex.log_ofReal_mul splits the logarithm with no 2*pi*i correction, so Complex.sqrt = exp(log/2) splits as a product; (3) prod_sqrt_zpow keeps the whole remaining square-root question inside R, where no cut exists: prod (sqrt a_delta)^{r_delta} = sqrt(prod a_delta^{r_delta}) for POSITIVE reals, proved by squaring a positive number and applying Real.sqrt_sq; prod_sqrt_div_divisors then computes the constant from (N/delta)*delta = N, which collapses P*s to prod N^{r_delta} = N^{2k}; (4) csqrt_zpow_two_mul and csqrt_inv_zpow_two_mul are (sqrt x)^{2k} = x^k for INTEGER k - this is where integrality of the weight is load-bearing, since at half-integral weight a residual square root survives and the statement is not even well posed; (5) the dual quotient is Mathlib's Nat.prod_div_divisors, the multiplicative form of the SAME divisor involution Nat.sum_div_divisors that F3.1-A7/A8 use on the congruences, plus Nat.div_div_self; (6) the delta-indexed constants collapse by the existing prod_zpow_const (F3.2-A4) at the sum sum r_delta = 2k, and mul_zpow/Finset.prod_mul_distrib split the four-fold product - mul_zpow is unconditional because C is a DivisionCommMonoid, so no non-vanishing side condition appears. Also landed: csqrt_sq ((sqrt x)^2 = x, UNCONDITIONAL - Complex.sqrt is the cpow x^(1/2) and Complex.cpow_nat_inv_pow needs only n != 0), csqrt_ne_zero, csqrt_ofReal_of_nonneg (Complex.sqrt IS Real.sqrt on the nonnegative reals) and zpow_sq_comm. THREE EXTERNAL GUARDS, not three restatements. eta_S_via_fricke runs the node at N = 1, r == 24, k = 12, where s = 1, N^k = 1 and i^{-12} = 1, collapsing the identity to eta(-1/z)^24 = z^12 * eta(z)^24 - which is MATHLIB's discriminant_S_invariant. FinalCheck PIN 4 REPROVES Mathlib's theorem (Delta slashed by weight 12 at S equals Delta) from this node and nothing else, and an example in the source file RE-DERIVES the same identity from Mathlib's theorem in the other direction: two independent derivations of one statement, which disagree if the constant i^{-k} N^k s^{-1/2} is assembled wrongly. fricke_level_two_pin is the hand-checked eta(z)eta(2z) case at N = 2, r == 1, k = 1, s = 2, where the exponent vector is its OWN dual so the pin is about the CONSTANT alone: eta(-1/(2z))*eta(-1/z) = i^{-1}*2*(sqrt 2)^{-1}*z*eta(z)*eta(2z). fricke_dual_pin is the converse check and the non-vacuity of the REVERSAL: at N = 2 with r = (2,0) the eta quotient is eta(z)^2 and its dual is eta(2z)^2, a DIFFERENT function, and the identity reads eta(-1/(2z))^2 = -2i*z*eta(2z)^2; a version of this node that forgot to reverse the exponents asserts -2i*z*eta(z)^2 there, which is false. NON-VACUITY CHECKED, not assumed. Five perturbations of the real statement, each fed the real proof script, all fail to elaborate (unsolved goals at the closing ring): i^{+k} for i^{-k}, N^{2k} for N^k, sqrt(s) for (sqrt s)^{-1}, z^{2k} for z^k, and f for the dual f*. Recorded in scratch/A7perturb.lean. DEVIATION, STATED NOT GLOSSED. The node was scoped with N : PNat and z : H. What is landed takes N : Nat with an explicit hypothesis 0 < N, and z : C with an explicit hypothesis z in upperHalfPlaneSet - the shape the whole F3.2 block of this file uses. That is a GENERALISATION, not a weakening, and FinalCheck PIN 1 is the proof of it: the scoped PNat/H statement, written longhand with BOTH eta quotients spelled out as products over Nat.divisors with ModularForm.eta fully qualified (so the reversal r_delta -> r_{N/delta} is visible as text), is discharged by the landed form at N.pos and z.2, with no side condition and no repair term. NO HYPOTHESIS IS UNUSED: hN is consumed by prod_sqrt_div_divisors, prod_eta_div_divisors and eta_fricke_factor, hk by the collapse of the two constant products, and hz by the non-vanishing of z and by the membership (N/delta)*z in upperHalfPlaneSet. SIX STATEMENT PINS (section F32A7Pins in FinalCheck.lean): PIN 1 the scoped PNat/H signature longhand; PIN 2 the branch-clean scaling law with Complex.sqrt UNFOLDED to the cpow x^(2^{-1}) it is defined as, so the pin is about Mathlib's principal branch and not about a SocrateAI notion of square root, and with 0 < m pinned (dropping it makes the statement false); PIN 3 the real square-root product identity with its positivity hypothesis; PIN 4 the Mathlib cross-check run in the STRONG direction; PIN 5 the level-two constant; PIN 6 the non-vacuity of the dual. SCOPE - READ BEFORE CITING. This is ONE identity on the OPEN upper half-plane relating f at -1/(Nz) to the dual f* at z. It is NOT Ligozat's criterion. It says NOTHING about Gamma0(N), NOTHING about the multiplier w of F3.2-A5, NOTHING about Ligozat's second congruence, and nothing at any cusp. F3.2-A8 (multiplier_V_eq_one) is the node that turns it into a statement about w; as of that node it is PROVED and sorry-free. The Dedekind-sum obstruction F3.2-OBSTRUCTED is UNTOUCHED: the inverted tripwire in FinalCheck.lean certifying that multiplier_trivial_of_congr depends on sorryAx is unchanged and still passing, and the F3.2 block of EtaQuotientModularity.lean carries exactly ONE sorry as of F3.2-A8 - multiplier_trivial_of_congr. AXIOM FOOTPRINT [propext, Classical.choice, Quot.sound] with NO sorryAx for all fifteen declarations (csqrt_sq, csqrt_ne_zero, csqrt_ofReal_of_nonneg, csqrt_ofReal_mul, csqrt_zpow_two_mul, csqrt_inv_zpow_two_mul, zpow_sq_comm, prod_sqrt_zpow, prod_sqrt_div_divisors, prod_eta_div_divisors, eta_fricke_factor, etaQuotient_fricke, eta_S_via_fricke, fricke_level_two_pin, fricke_dual_pin), each guarded by '#guard_msgs in #print axioms' in FinalCheck.lean. Final line of lake build: 'Build completed successfully (3476 jobs).'", "lean_name": "SocrateAI.ModularForms.etaQuotient_fricke", "lean_file": "Lean/SocrateAI/ModularForms/EtaQuotientModularity.lean", "status": "proved", "depends_on": ["F32-A2", "F31-B5", "F31-B7", "F32-A4"], "paper_claim": null}
{"id": "F32-A8", "kind": "math", "statement_nl": "HEADLINE multiplier_V_eq_one. PROVED, sorry-free. The node also lands the strictly stronger, UNCONDITIONAL etaQuotientH_V_smul, the character forms etaMultiplierVal_V_eq_one and etaMultiplierHom_V_eq_one (which is verbatim the shape the node was scoped in, w <matV N, matV_mem_Gamma0 N> = 1), the sharpening ligozatCongr2_iff_V_transform, the previously-sorry matV_mem_Gamma0, and the helper layer matV_coe / denom_matV / coe_matV_smul / neg_inv_mem_upperHalfPlaneSet / prod_zpow_div_divisors / sum_divisors_dual / ligozatCongr1_dual / sqrt_prod_dual / mul_shuffle_aux, plus the two LL-1 guards multiplier_V_level_one_24 and eta_two_sq_not_V_invariant. STATEMENT, verbatim as landed: for N : Nat with 0 < N, r : Nat -> Int, k : Int with sum over delta in N.divisors of r delta = 2*k, h24' : LigozatCongr2 N r, and z : H, etaQuotientH N r (matV N . z) = (denom (matV N) z)^k * etaQuotientH N r z, where matV N = !![1,0;-(N:Int),1]. WHAT WAS PROVED, IN ENGLISH (LL-1). Let f(z) = prod_{delta | N} eta(delta z)^{r_delta} with r an arbitrary integer exponent vector of EVEN weight sum, sum_delta r_delta = 2k with k an integer. First, UNCONDITIONALLY - no congruence hypothesis whatsoever - for every z in H, f(V.z) = exp(i pi (sum_{delta | N} (N/delta) r_delta) / 12) * (1 - N z)^k * f(z), where V = !![1,0;-N,1] and 1 - N z is exactly denom V z (denom_matV); V acts by the Moebius map z -> z/(1 - Nz) (coe_matV_smul), and V lies in Gamma0(N) (matV_mem_Gamma0). That is etaQuotientH_V_smul, and it is the exact V-analogue of etaQuotientH_T_smul from F3.2-A6. Ligozat's congruence (ii), 24 | sum_delta (N/delta) r_delta, is precisely the condition that kills the exponential, giving f(V.z) = (denom V z)^k f(z) - that is multiplier_V_eq_one - and hence w(V) = 1 for the character w : Gamma0(N) -> C^x produced by F3.2-A5 (etaMultiplierVal_V_eq_one, etaMultiplierHom_V_eq_one). The word EXACTLY is a theorem, not a slogan: ligozatCongr2_iff_V_transform proves the EQUIVALENCE, the converse coming from dividing etaQuotientH_V_smul at the single point z = i by the nonvanishing (denom V i)^k f(i) and applying Complex.exp_eq_one_iff. THE ROUTE, AND WHY THERE ARE NO DEDEKIND SUMS. V = W_N T W_N^{-1} with W_N : z -> -1/(Nz), so this node is F3.2-A6 (the T-law) conjugated by F3.2-A7 (the Fricke law), used twice in opposite directions. Concretely: V.z = -1/(N(u+1)) with u = -1/(Nz) (hpt, one field_simp from coe_matV_smul); etaQuotient_fricke at u+1 replaces f by the DUAL quotient f*; etaQuotient_T_transform moves f*(u+1) to f*(u) at the cost of exp(i pi (sum_delta delta r_{N/delta})/12), which by sum_divisors_dual IS exp(i pi (sum_delta (N/delta) r_delta)/12) - this is the identity that makes congruence (ii) for r literally congruence (i) for the dual vector, recorded separately as ligozatCongr1_dual; etaQuotient_fricke at z applied to the dual vector returns f, because the dual of the dual is r (Nat.div_div_self). The two Fricke constants i^{-k} N^k s^{-1/2} are inverse to one another on the dual pair because sqrt(s) sqrt(s*) = N^k, which is sqrt_prod_dual - proved entirely inside R, via prod_sqrt_div_divisors and prod_sqrt_zpow from F3.2-A7, so no branch cut is ever approached. What survives is i^{-2k} = (I*I)^{-k} = (-1)^k (hAA, via Complex.I_mul_I) and (-1)^k (Nz-1)^k = (1-Nz)^k. No eta multiplier system is invoked, no Dedekind sum occurs, and the only arithmetic input is the divisor involution Nat.sum_div_divisors / Nat.prod_div_divisors. DEVIATION FROM THE SCOPED ROUTE, STATED NOT GLOSSED. The node was scoped to transport the T-statement 'through the Fricke intertwining using frickeW_normalizes_Gamma0 and frickeW_sq_slash from the run-2 artifact'. NEITHER IS USED. The landed proof never leaves the Moebius formulas: denom_matV and coe_matV_smul compute V's action and automorphy factor directly from UpperHalfPlane.coe_specialLinearGroup_apply and ModularGroup.denom_apply, and the conjugation V = W_N T W_N^{-1} enters only as the coordinate identity V.z = -1/(N(-1/(Nz) + 1)). The GL(2,R) normaliser statement frickeW_normalizes_Gamma0 and the slash-square identity frickeW_sq_slash are about the slash ACTION of W_N on weight-k functions; they are the right tools for an Atkin-Lehner argument, but here they would have had to be plumbed through a determinant-N slash normalisation that the direct route makes unnecessary (LL-11). The run-2 artifact is therefore NOT a dependency of this node. Also NOT used: any statement about a general gamma in Gamma0(N). NON-VACUITY CHECKED, not assumed (scratch/A8perturb.lean). Four perturbations of the real statement, each fed the real proof script, all fail to elaborate: congruence (i) LigozatCongr1 in place of congruence (ii) LigozatCongr2; denom^{-k} in place of denom^{k}; T in place of V; and sum_delta delta r_delta in place of sum_delta (N/delta) r_delta in the unconditional constant. TWO EXTERNAL / NON-VACUITY GUARDS IN THE SOURCE FILE. multiplier_V_level_one_24 runs the node at N = 1, r == 24, k = 12, where the eta quotient is Mathlib's Delta and V = !![1,0;-1,1] in SL(2,Z), asserting Delta(V.z) = (denom V z)^12 Delta(z); the example immediately after it derives the SAME identity from Mathlib's own full SL(2,Z) modularity of Delta via etaQuotientH_level_one_24_transform, so a wrong sign in hAA, a wrong power of N in sqrt_prod_dual, or a denom read off the wrong row of V would make the two disagree. eta_two_sq_not_V_invariant is the non-vacuity witness: at N = 2 with r = (0,2), so f(z) = eta(2z)^2 and k = 1, congruence (ii) reads 24 | 2 and FAILS, and therefore - through the iff - f does NOT satisfy the V-law. So the conclusion is a real restriction on r and the iff is not a tautology. FOUR STATEMENT PINS (section F32A8Pins in FinalCheck.lean). PIN 1: V is the raw 2x2 integer matrix !![1,0;-(N:Int),1] and lies in Gamma0(N). PIN 2: the UNCONDITIONAL V-law longhand with N : PNat, z : H, the exponent vector the bare Nat -> Int, both eta products written out over Nat.divisors with ModularForm.eta fully qualified, the Moebius image written as z/(1 - Nz) rather than as a group action, and the automorphy factor written as (1 - Nz)^k - nothing hides behind etaQuotientH, matV or denom, and the exponential is visible with NO congruence hypothesis assumed. PIN 3: the iff, with the divisibility in Z on the left and the transformation law on the right, both longhand. PIN 4: the non-vacuity sentence. SCOPE - READ BEFORE CITING. This is the multiplier at the SINGLE element V, plus the exact arithmetic condition for it to be trivial. It is NOT Ligozat's criterion. Together with F3.2-A6 the character w of F3.2-A5 is now evaluated on T and on V and nowhere else; nothing here evaluates w at any other gamma in Gamma0(N), nothing here is about any cusp or about holomorphy there (Ligozat's third hypothesis), and the reduction of Gamma0(N) to <T, V, -I> - which is FALSE for general N, since Gamma0(N) needs more generators as its genus or elliptic-point count grows - remains the named obstruction F3.2-OBSTRUCTED. The inverted tripwire in FinalCheck.lean certifying that multiplier_trivial_of_congr depends on sorryAx is unchanged and still passing; as of this node that hypothesis-shaped theorem is the ONLY remaining sorry in the F3.2 block of EtaQuotientModularity.lean. AXIOM FOOTPRINT [propext, Classical.choice, Quot.sound], NO sorryAx, for all seventeen declarations guarded by '#guard_msgs in #print axioms' in FinalCheck.lean: matV_mem_Gamma0, denom_matV, coe_matV_smul, neg_inv_mem_upperHalfPlaneSet, prod_zpow_div_divisors, sum_divisors_dual, ligozatCongr1_dual, sqrt_prod_dual, mul_shuffle_aux, ligozatCongr2_level_one_24, etaQuotientH_V_smul, multiplier_V_eq_one, etaMultiplierVal_V_eq_one, etaMultiplierHom_V_eq_one, ligozatCongr2_iff_V_transform, multiplier_V_level_one_24, eta_two_sq_not_V_invariant. Final line of lake build: 'Build completed successfully (3476 jobs).'", "lean_name": "SocrateAI.ModularForms.multiplier_V_eq_one", "lean_file": "Lean/SocrateAI/ModularForms/EtaQuotientModularity.lean", "status": "proved", "depends_on": ["F32-A7", "F32-A6", "F32-A5", "F31-A7"], "paper_claim": null}
{"id": "F32-A9", "kind": "math", "statement_nl": "HEADLINE multiplier_elliptic. PROVED, sorry-free. STATEMENT, verbatim as landed: for N : Nat with 0 < N (UNUSED, kept because it is the scoped signature), r : Nat -> Int, k : Int with sum over delta in N.divisors of r delta = 2*k, e : Gamma0 N, tau0 : H and hfix : (e : SL(2,Z)) . tau0 = tau0, (etaMultiplierHom r hk e : C) = (denom (e : SL(2,Z)) tau0)^(-k). The core lemma is etaMultiplierVal_of_fixed (same content on the bare value, gamma : SL(2,Z) with hgamma : gamma in Gamma0 N); the pointwise form is etaQuotientH_elliptic_transform, f(gamma.z) = (denom gamma tau0)^(-k) (denom gamma z)^k f(z). WHAT WAS PROVED, IN ENGLISH (LL-1). Let f(z) = prod_{delta | N} eta(delta z)^{r_delta} for an ARBITRARY integer exponent vector of even weight sum, sum_delta r_delta = 2k, k an integer, and let w be the character Gamma0(N) -> C^x produced UNCONDITIONALLY by F3.2-A5. If an element e of Gamma0(N) FIXES a point tau0 of the open upper half-plane, then w(e) is forced to be the inverse automorphy factor at that point: w(e) = (c tau0 + d)^{-k}. No congruence condition on r is assumed and no analysis is used. THE PROOF is one substitution: F3.2-A5's law f(e.z) = w(e) (denom e z)^k f(z) at z = tau0, rewrite e.tau0 = tau0 on the left, cancel f(tau0) which is nonzero by F3.1-B7 (etaQuotientH_ne_zero, from Mathlib's eta_ne_zero), and invert. No q-product, no Fricke, no Dedekind sum, no new analytic input of any kind. SCOPE - READ BEFORE CITING (this is where the node is WEAKER than its brief). The brief said 'gives the multiplier on ALL torsion elements'. THAT IS NOT WHAT WAS PROVED. The fixed point is a HYPOTHESIS supplied by the caller. The classical fact that an elliptic element of SL(2,Z) (|trace| < 2) has a fixed point in H is NOT formalised here and is NOT used anywhere; passing from 'e is torsion' to 'e has a fixed point in H' would be a separate node. What is proved is strictly the conditional. Nor does this close F3.2-OBSTRUCTED: elliptic elements together with T and V still do not generate Gamma0(N) in general, and the sorryAx tripwire on multiplier_trivial_of_congr is untouched. DEGENERATE CASE, landed: -I fixes every point of H (ModularGroup.SL_neg_smul) and denom(-I) z = -1, so A9 gives etaMultiplierVal_neg_one, w(-I) = (-1)^k - the one classical normalisation of the eta multiplier that comes for free. Note this is NOT a sign check: (-1)^{-k} = (-1)^k. NEGATIVE BOUNDARY, landed as a pin: T has NO fixed point in H (T.z = z+1), so A9 says nothing about T and cannot be mistaken for a proof of F3.2-A6. THE SIGN PIN (LL-1, and the only guard that actually constrains the sign of the exponent). Every weight-12 example is blind to it, because there the automorphy factors are roots of unity raised to +-12. So the pin runs at weight k = 1: N = 1, r == 2, i.e. f = eta^2, where S fixes i (S_smul_I, from Mathlib's modular_S_smul and (-i)^{-1} = i) and denom S i = i (Mathlib's denom_S), so A9 gives w(S) = i^{-1} = -i (etaMultiplierVal_eta_sq_S). The SAME number is then derived independently through F3.2-A7 (etaQuotient_fricke at N=1, r==2, k=1, where the constant is i^{-1} 1^1 (sqrt 1)^{-1} and the dual quotient is f itself), whose only analytic input is MATHLIB's eta_comp_eq_csqrt_I_inv: etaQuotientH_eta_sq_S_transform, f(S.z) = -i z f(z) for every z. If A9 carried ^{+k} the first route would give +i and the second -i, and they could not both compile. THE GAMMA0(2) CROSS-CHECK (the one named in the brief, delivered for N = 2). Gamma0(2) has a single elliptic point, tau0 = (1+i)/2, fixed by E = !![1,-1;2,-1] (trace 0, so E^2 = -I). ROUTE A: matE2_mem_Gamma0, matE2_smul_tauE2 and denom_matE2_tauE2 give denom E tau0 = 2 tau0 - 1 = i, so A9 gives w(E) = i^{-k}; and four_dvd_of_ligozat_two shows Ligozat's congruences (i)+(ii) at N = 2 force 4 | k by PURE ARITHMETIC - adding them gives sum_delta (delta + 2/delta) r_delta = 3 sum_delta r_delta = 6k, so 24 | 6k - whence i^{-k} = 1 (etaMultiplierVal_matE2_eq_one). ROUTE B: matV_two_mul_matE2_mul_T checks entrywise that V*E*T = 1 in SL(2,Z), so w(E) = w(V)^{-1} w(T)^{-1} = 1 by F3.2-A6 and F3.2-A8. The two agree. STATED HONESTLY: because E = V^{-1} T^{-1}, Gamma0(2) is NOT new territory - E already lies in <T,V>, which is exactly why the cross-check is possible. The N = 3 half of the brief's cross-check (3 | k, elliptic point (3 + i sqrt 3)/6, denom = exp(2 pi i/3)) was NOT formalised. DEPENDENCIES, honestly split: the theorem itself needs only F3.2-A2 (the eta quotient and its non-vanishing) and F3.2-A5 (the multiplier); the FinalCheck guards additionally consume F3.2-A6, F3.2-A7 and F3.2-A8. SIX STATEMENT PINS (section F32A9Pins in FinalCheck.lean). PIN 1: the node longhand, exponent vector the bare Nat -> Int, the eta quotient written out over Nat.divisors with ModularForm.eta fully qualified, and BOTH automorphy factors written as c*z+d rather than as denom - the fixed-point factor carrying -k and the moving factor +k, so a swap of the two would not elaborate. PIN 2: the scoped signature in the C^x-valued character etaMultiplierHom, with e in the SUBGROUP Gamma0 N. PIN 3: w(-I) = (-1)^k. PIN 4: the sign pin, both routes. PIN 5: E and tau0 as a raw 2x2 integer matrix and a raw complex number, plus both routes to w(E) = 1 with the congruences written as raw divisibilities. PIN 6: T has no fixed point in H. AXIOM FOOTPRINT [propext, Classical.choice, Quot.sound], NO sorryAx, for all fifteen declarations guarded by '#guard_msgs in #print axioms' in FinalCheck.lean: etaMultiplierVal_of_fixed, etaQuotientH_elliptic_transform, multiplier_elliptic, neg_one_mem_Gamma0, denom_neg_one, etaMultiplierVal_neg_one, S_smul_I, etaMultiplierVal_eta_sq_S, etaQuotientH_eta_sq_S_transform, matE2_mem_Gamma0, matE2_smul_tauE2, denom_matE2_tauE2, four_dvd_of_ligozat_two, matV_two_mul_matE2_mul_T, etaMultiplierVal_matE2_eq_one. Final line of lake build: 'Build completed successfully (3476 jobs).'", "lean_name": "SocrateAI.ModularForms.multiplier_elliptic", "lean_file": "Lean/SocrateAI/ModularForms/EtaQuotientModularity.lean", "status": "proved", "depends_on": ["F32-A2", "F32-A5", "F32-A6", "F32-A7", "F32-A8"], "paper_claim": null}
{"id": "F32-OBSTRUCTED", "kind": "math", "statement_nl": "THE NAMED OBSTRUCTION (an honest negative, not a gap). A5 gives the multiplier unconditionally and A6/A8 show Ligozat's two congruences are exactly its triviality on T and on V. What is NOT proved is that T, V and -I generate Gamma0(N): this is classical for N=1 and true for various small N, but FALSE in general once the genus or the number of elliptic points of Gamma0(N) grows. The gap is carried as an explicit hypothesis 'hgen' on multiplier_trivial_of_congr so nothing downstream can use it by accident. UPDATE (F32-B1): hgen is now DISCHARGED for N in {1,2,3,4} by Gamma0_generated_of_le_four. This node stays BLOCKED: it is the all-N statement, the hypothesis is still carried, and full Ligozat additionally needs the character chi(d) bookkeeping that F32-B1 does not touch. Discharging it for a fixed N is a finite computation (Farey symbols / Reidemeister-Schreier); discharging it for all N is impossible. Consequence: the classical route through the general eta multiplier needs DEDEKIND SUMS, which Mathlib does not have (grep: DedekindSum, dedekindSum, etaMultiplier all return zero files). UPDATE (F32-B2): for N <= 4 the criterion is now COMPLETE and sorry-free (ligozat_of_le_four, etaQuotientModularForm); the character chi(d) bookkeeping turned out not to be needed there, because the multiplier is pinned by its three generator values rather than evaluated. Two corrections this node's earlier text implied and F32-B2 settled: (a) the trivial-multiplier form needs Even k -- at gamma = -I it is FALSE otherwise, and not_multiplier_trivial_odd is the proved counterexample (N=3, r=(-3,9), k=3, both congruences holding); (b) condition (iii) is carried as the hypothesis hbd (Mathlib's IsBoundedAtImInfty), because converting LigozatHolomorphic into boundedness needs F31-OBSTRUCTED. This node REMAINS BLOCKED: it is the all-N statement, and at N >= 5 the three matrices do not generate (descent_bound_fails_at_five), so the Dedekind-sum route is still the only one known and Mathlib still has no Dedekind sums.", "lean_name": "multiplier_trivial_of_congr", "lean_file": "Lean/SocrateAI/ModularForms/EtaQuotientModularity.lean", "status": "blocked", "depends_on": ["F32-A5", "F32-A6", "F32-A8"], "paper_claim": null}
# --- F3.1-B5: THE ETA QUOTIENT ITSELF, as a definition over H, plus the zpow algebra. ---
{"id": "F31-B5", "kind": "def", "statement_nl": "HEADLINE etaQuotientH. PROVED (a definition plus its algebra, all sorry-free). THE ETA QUOTIENT f(tau) = prod_{delta | N} eta(delta*tau)^{r_delta} as a Lean definition over the FINITE index set N.divisors, with INTEGER exponents r : EtaExp = (Nat -> Int), so the power is a zpow. DESIGN DECISION, forced by Mathlib's signatures at commit 905b95818e (checked, not recalled): ModularForm.eta : C -> C is a function on all of C, while ModularForm.discriminant : H -> C and the whole SlashAction / denom API live on the BUNDLED upper half-plane H. The node therefore takes tau : H and feeds the coercion (tau : C) to eta, which is what makes it compose with slash_k and with our frickeSlashOperator (run-2 artifact). Two declarations are landed: etaQuotient (N r z) on the C-domain, and etaQuotientH N r tau := etaQuotient N r (tau : C) on H; etaQuotientH_apply records (by rfl) that the composite IS the product in the brief, and etaQuotientH_eq_etaQuotient pins that no third definition has appeared. VERIFIED ABSENT FROM MATHLIB: repository-wide greps for EtaQuotient, Ligozat, Fricke, AtkinLehner, DedekindSum and etaMultiplier return zero files, so the object had to be built. THE JUNK-VALUE QUESTION, ANSWERED RATHER THAN ASSUMED - this is the substantive content of the node. r delta may be NEGATIVE, so x^(r delta) is a zpow, whose value at base 0 is the junk value 0, and every zpow identity below is FALSE at a vanishing base. It never bites: for delta in N.divisors we have 0 < delta (Nat.pos_of_mem_divisors), hence im(delta*tau) = delta*im(tau) > 0, so delta*tau is again in the open upper half-plane (natCast_mul_mem_upperHalfPlaneSet), where Mathlib's ModularForm.eta_ne_zero applies. That is recorded at the level of a single FACTOR as eta_natCast_mul_ne_zero. The PRODUCT-level etaQuotient_ne_zero is F31-B7 and is DELIBERATELY NOT PROVED here (it remains a sorry, pinned UNPROVED by a FinalCheck tripwire), even though B5 now supplies its only missing input and Finset.prod_ne_zero_iff would close it - flipping B7 is its own commit. ALSO PROVED, the algebra the definition licenses, all consuming the factor-level non-vanishing where a zpow needs it: etaQuotientH_add (f_{r+s} = f_r * f_s, via zpow_add_zero), etaQuotientH_neg (f_{-r} = (f_r)^{-1}), etaQuotientH_zsmul (f_{m.r} = (f_r)^m for m : Int), etaQuotientH_zero_exp (f_0 = 1, no non-vanishing needed), etaQuotientH_congr (f depends on r only through its values on N.divisors - the analytic analogue of EtaExp.sum_divisors_congr, and what licenses carrying r as a TOTAL function Nat -> Int), etaQuotientH_trunc, and etaQuotientH_level_one (N = 1 collapses to eta(tau)^(r 1) since Nat.divisors_one = {1}). The first three are the multiplicative mirror of the ADDITIVE arithmetic laws etaQuotientWeight_add and etaQuotientCuspOrder_add / _smul guarded under F31-A6. LL-1 EXTERNAL PIN (etaQuotientH_level_one_24): at N = 1 with the constant exponent vector r == 24 the eta quotient must be MATHLIB's modular discriminant, prod_{delta | 1} eta(delta*tau)^24 = eta(tau)^24 = Delta(tau), an object whose definition we did not write. This is the single check that the index set, the delta-scaling inside eta, and the zpow-vs-pow coercion are ALL simultaneously right: a mistyped index set (Nat.properDivisors for Nat.divisors), a dropped delta scaling, or an exponent coerced the wrong way all still elaborate but fail HERE. Four STATEMENT PINS in FinalCheck.lean write the propositions out longhand (with the exponent vector typed as the bare Nat -> Int rather than the EtaExp abbreviation) so the signature cannot drift to the C-domain form unnoticed. PLACEMENT AND RELOCATION, stated loudly. The brief named Lean/SocrateAI/ModularForms/EtaQuotient.lean; that file is the ARITHMETIC layer whose import cone is deliberately Nat.divisors + Nat.totient only, and eta sits behind Mathlib.NumberTheory.ModularForms.DedekindEta, so stating it there would force the whole analytic cone into the arithmetic file - the same deviation, for the same reason, as F31-B1/B2/B3/B4. It is stated in EtaQuotientModularity.lean instead. Moreover etaQuotient and etaQuotientH ALREADY EXISTED in that file as unproved-statement-layer definitions under F32-A2; rather than duplicate them, the two declarations were MOVED UP into the new F3.1-B5 block, unchanged in name, signature and definitional content, so that the proved F3.1-B ladder owns them and does not reach past the F3.2 sorries. F32-A2's lean_name still resolves. SCOPE - read before citing. This node is a DEFINITION plus zpow algebra and nothing more. No Gamma0(N), no slash action, no modularity, no eta multiplier system, no Ligozat congruence. F32-A1 (eta_T_transform) is still a sorry and still pinned UNPROVED by its FinalCheck tripwire, and the Dedekind-sum obstruction recorded as F32-OBSTRUCTED is untouched. Axiom footprint [propext, Classical.choice, Quot.sound] with NO sorryAx for all 14 declarations (etaQuotient, etaQuotientH, etaQuotientH_apply, natCast_mul_mem_upperHalfPlaneSet, eta_natCast_mul_ne_zero, etaQuotientH_congr, etaQuotientH_trunc, etaQuotientH_zero_exp, etaQuotientH_add, etaQuotientH_neg, etaQuotientH_zsmul, etaQuotientH_level_one, etaQuotientH_level_one_24, etaQuotientH_eq_etaQuotient), each guarded by #guard_msgs in #print axioms in FinalCheck.lean. Final line of lake build: 'Build completed successfully (3475 jobs).'", "lean_name": "SocrateAI.ModularForms.etaQuotientH", "lean_file": "Lean/SocrateAI/ModularForms/EtaQuotientModularity.lean", "status": "proved", "depends_on": ["F31-B0"], "paper_claim": null}

# --- F3.1-B6: the side condition of B7/B8 in divisor form. A WRAPPER of B5's positivity lemma. ---
{"id": "F31-B6", "kind": "math", "statement_nl": "HEADLINE mem_upperHalfPlaneSet_divisor_smul. PROVED, sorry-free -- and it is a WRAPPER, reported as one rather than dressed up. STATEMENT, verbatim as scoped: for delta in N.divisors and tau : H, the complex number (delta : C) * (tau : C) lies in UpperHalfPlane.upperHalfPlaneSet, i.e. im(delta*tau) > 0. WHAT IS ACTUALLY NEW HERE, STATED PLAINLY. Nothing mathematical. The content -- im(delta*tau) = delta*im(tau) > 0 whenever 0 < delta -- was ALREADY LANDED under F31-B5 as natCast_mul_mem_upperHalfPlaneSet, because B5's zpow algebra needed it; that declaration and its axiom guard already exist in FinalCheck.lean. B6 restates the same fact with the hypothesis in the form its consumers carry, delta IN N.divisors rather than 0 < delta, bridged by Nat.pos_of_mem_divisors. The proof is one line: natCast_mul_mem_upperHalfPlaneSet (Nat.pos_of_mem_divisors h_delta) tau. No new Mathlib lemma was needed and none was written; the brief's Built-from list (Nat.pos_of_mem_divisors, upperHalfPlaneSet, Complex.mul_im, Complex.natCast_im, Complex.natCast_re, UpperHalfPlane.coe_im) is discharged transitively through B5's proof, which is the single place in the file where the im computation is done. WHY IT IS WORTH A NAMED DECLARATION ANYWAY. etaQuotient and etaQuotientH are products over N.divisors, so inside Finset.prod_ne_zero_iff (F31-B7, etaQuotient_ne_zero, STILL A SORRY and still tripwired UNPROVED in FinalCheck) and inside the factorwise T and Fricke rewrites (F31-B8 / etaQuotient_T_transform / etaQuotient_fricke, all still sorries) the hypothesis in hand is membership and never positivity. Naming the membership form keeps the (delta : Nat) -> (delta : C) coercion bookkeeping in one place. PLACEMENT AND DEVIATION, stated loudly. The brief named Lean/SocrateAI/ModularForms/EtaQuotient.lean. That file is the ARITHMETIC layer whose import cone is deliberately Nat.divisors + Nat.totient only; H and upperHalfPlaneSet sit behind Mathlib.Analysis.Complex.UpperHalfPlane.Basic, which the eta cone drags in, so stating B6 there would force the analytic cone into the arithmetic file. It is stated in EtaQuotientModularity.lean instead, immediately after natCast_mul_mem_upperHalfPlaneSet -- the same deviation, for the same reason, as F31-B1/B2/B3/B4/B5. The STATEMENT is verbatim what was asked; only the file differs. SCOPE -- read before citing. Positivity of a natural number and one multiplication in C. This node says NOTHING about eta (the non-vanishing that consumes it is eta_natCast_mul_ne_zero, already under B5), nothing about Gamma0(N), nothing about the eta multiplier system. The Dedekind-sum obstruction recorded as F32-OBSTRUCTED is untouched, and the F31-B5 tripwire asserting etaQuotient_ne_zero is still UNPROVED remains in force and still passes. AXIOM FOOTPRINT [propext, Classical.choice, Quot.sound] with NO sorryAx, guarded by #guard_msgs in #print axioms in FinalCheck.lean, together with a longhand STATEMENT PIN (section B6Pin) that writes the proposition out with upperHalfPlaneSet fully qualified and the hypothesis in membership form, so a signature weakening back to 0 < delta stops elaborating there. Final line of lake build: 'Build completed successfully (3475 jobs).'", "lean_name": "SocrateAI.ModularForms.mem_upperHalfPlaneSet_divisor_smul", "lean_file": "Lean/SocrateAI/ModularForms/EtaQuotientModularity.lean", "status": "proved", "depends_on": ["F31-B5"], "paper_claim": null}
# --- F3.1-B7: eta quotients never vanish on H.  Retires the B5 tripwire; unlocks zpow arithmetic. ---
{"id": "F31-B7", "kind": "math", "statement_nl": "HEADLINE etaQuotient_ne_zero / etaQuotientH_ne_zero. PROVED, sorry-free. STATEMENT: an eta quotient never vanishes on the OPEN upper half-plane. Two forms are landed and both are pinned longhand in FinalCheck: the C-domain etaQuotient_ne_zero (r : EtaExp = Nat -> Int, z : C, hypothesis z in UpperHalfPlane.upperHalfPlaneSet) and the H-domain etaQuotientH_ne_zero (N : Nat) (r : Nat -> Int) (tau : H) : etaQuotientH N r tau != 0, which is the node exactly as scoped and carries NO hypothesis at all because tau : H holds 0 < im tau in its own structure (H is a structure with field coe_im_pos, checked in Mathlib/Analysis/Complex/UpperHalfPlane/Basic.lean, not recalled). There is NO condition on the exponent vector: r delta may be negative, zero or mixed. PROOF, and it is genuinely three Mathlib lemmas as the brief predicted (LL-11): Finset.prod_ne_zero_iff (Mathlib/Algebra/BigOperators/GroupWithZero/Finset.lean line 60, needs the finite index set N.divisors and NoZeroDivisors C) reduces the product to its factors; zpow_ne_zero (Mathlib/Algebra/GroupWithZero/Units/Basic.lean line 412, signature 'forall n : Int, a != 0 -> a ^ n != 0') strips the integer exponent; ModularForm.eta_ne_zero finishes at the point delta*z, whose membership in the open upper half-plane comes from Nat.pos_of_mem_divisors plus im(delta*z) = delta*im(z) > 0. Compiled first try, no tactic search. ONE NEW SUPPORTING LEMMA, reported rather than hidden: natCast_mul_mem_upperHalfPlaneSet_of_mem, the C-domain twin of F3.1-B5's natCast_mul_mem_upperHalfPlaneSet. B5's version takes the BUNDLED tau : H; the C-domain statement carries its hypothesis as set membership z in upperHalfPlaneSet, which is the shape the whole F3.2 block consumes, so it needed the same one-line im computation packaged differently. Its corollary eta_natCast_mul_ne_zero_of_mem is the factor-level non-vanishing in that same shape. F3.1-B6 WAS NOT USED, and saying so is the point of this sentence: mem_upperHalfPlaneSet_divisor_smul is B5's positivity with the hypothesis in divisor-membership form on the H-domain, and the proof here runs through the C-domain twin instead, so depends_on lists F31-B5 only. B6 remains correct and remains the form the F3.1-B8 factorwise rewrites will want. WHY THE NODE MATTERS DESPITE BEING MECHANICAL: every zpow identity is FALSE at a vanishing base (0 ^ (-1) is the junk value 0), so until this landed nothing downstream could divide by, invert, or zpow-add an eta quotient AS ONE NUMBER. B5 had non-vanishing only at the level of a single FACTOR, which sufficed there because each factor was rewritten separately. B9's zpow arithmetic is now legal. TRIPWIRE RETIRED AS DESIGNED (LL-2, LL-7). F3.1-B5 had planted a guard in FinalCheck.lean asserting that etaQuotient_ne_zero still depended on sorryAx, precisely so that discharging it could not pass unnoticed. That guard FAILED on this commit, as intended, and was replaced by four positive axiom guards plus four statement pins; the retirement is documented in place in FinalCheck.lean rather than silently deleted. SCOPE - read before citing. Non-vanishing on the OPEN upper half-plane and nothing else. This is NOT non-vanishing at the cusps: upperHalfPlaneSet is open, the cusps are not in it, and cusp orders are the separate arithmetic etaQuotientCuspOrder (F3.1-A). It is not holomorphy - differentiableAt_etaQuotient is still a sorry. It says nothing about Gamma0(N), nothing about the slash action and nothing about the eta multiplier system; the Dedekind-sum obstruction recorded as F32-OBSTRUCTED is untouched, and F32-A1 (eta_T_transform) is still a sorry with its own UNPROVED tripwire in force. PLACEMENT, stated loudly (same deviation, same reason, as F31-B1..B6). The brief named Lean/SocrateAI/ModularForms/EtaQuotient.lean; that file is the ARITHMETIC layer whose import cone is deliberately Nat.divisors + Nat.totient only, while eta and upperHalfPlaneSet sit behind Mathlib.NumberTheory.ModularForms.DedekindEta. The declarations are in EtaQuotientModularity.lean instead. Within that file the theorem MOVED UP out of the F3.2-A2 section (where it had been sitting as a sorry) into a new F3.1-B7 block beside the definition, so that the proved F3.1-B ladder does not reach past the F3.2 sorries; the name and the C-domain signature are unchanged and a pointer note was left at the old site. AXIOM FOOTPRINT [propext, Classical.choice, Quot.sound] with NO sorryAx for all four declarations (natCast_mul_mem_upperHalfPlaneSet_of_mem, eta_natCast_mul_ne_zero_of_mem, etaQuotient_ne_zero, etaQuotientH_ne_zero), each guarded by #guard_msgs in #print axioms in FinalCheck.lean; the first name is long enough that Lean wraps the axiom list at 120 columns, so its expected message is written wrapped. The four statement pins (section B7Pins) write the propositions out with the exponent vector typed as the bare Nat -> Int, upperHalfPlaneSet fully qualified, the product written out longhand instead of hidden behind the definition, and a NEGATIVE-EXPONENT instance at r == -1, so a proof that secretly assumed 0 <= r delta would stop elaborating there. Final line of lake build: 'Build completed successfully (3475 jobs).'", "lean_name": "SocrateAI.ModularForms.etaQuotientH_ne_zero", "lean_file": "Lean/SocrateAI/ModularForms/EtaQuotientModularity.lean", "status": "proved", "depends_on": ["F31-B5"], "paper_claim": null}
# --- F3.1-B8: holomorphy of the eta quotient on the OPEN upper half-plane. Consumes B7 to discharge DifferentiableAt.zpow's non-vanishing disjunct. ---
{"id": "F31-B8", "kind": "math", "statement_nl": "HEADLINE differentiableAt_etaQuotient. PROVED, sorry-free. The last node of the F3.1-B ladder. STATEMENT, verbatim as scoped: for every N : Nat, every r : Nat -> Int and every z : C with z in UpperHalfPlane.upperHalfPlaneSet, DifferentiableAt C (fun w => prod over delta in N.divisors of (ModularForm.eta ((delta : C) * w)) ^ (r delta)) z. That literal form is landed as differentiableAt_etaQuotient_prod (N explicit, product written longhand); the working form differentiableAt_etaQuotient states the same proposition through the definition etaQuotient with N implicit, and PIN 3 in FinalCheck proves the two are Iff.rfl -- i.e. the same proposition, not a weakening. There is NO condition on the exponent vector: r delta may be negative, zero or mixed. IN ENGLISH (the LL-1 check): an eta quotient with arbitrary integer exponents is holomorphic at every point of the OPEN upper half-plane. PROOF, and it really was existing Mathlib lemmas as the brief predicted (LL-11), compiled first try with no tactic search: DifferentiableAt.fun_finsetProd (Mathlib/Analysis/Calculus/Deriv/Mul.lean line 487, needs NormedCommRing and the finite index set N.divisors) reduces the product to its factors; DifferentiableAt.zpow (Mathlib/Analysis/Calculus/Deriv/ZPow.lean line 177, signature 'hf : DifferentiableAt k f a -> (h : f a != 0 or 0 <= m) -> DifferentiableAt k (fun x => f x ^ m) a') strips the integer exponent; ModularForm.differentiableAt_eta_of_mem_upperHalfPlaneSet composed with the C-linear scaling w -> delta*w (DifferentiableAt.comp, the scaling itself by fun_prop) is the factor. WHERE F31-B7 IS ACTUALLY USED, and it is not decorative. DifferentiableAt.zpow's side condition is the DISJUNCTION 'f a != 0 or 0 <= m'. For a negative r delta the right disjunct is false, so the proof supplies the LEFT one at every factor, from B7's eta_natCast_mul_ne_zero_of_mem. That is exactly why no sign hypothesis on r appears in the statement, and it is the dependency the node was scoped to have. The hypothesis hz is used TWICE per factor: once for the chain rule (the inner point delta*z must lie in upperHalfPlaneSet for Mathlib's eta-differentiability) and once for non-vanishing at that same point. ONE NEW SUPPORTING LEMMA, reported rather than hidden: differentiableAt_eta_natCast_mul, the factor-level statement that w -> eta(delta*w) is differentiable at z in upperHalfPlaneSet for 0 < delta. It is the chain rule and nothing else; it is named because it is what the finsetProd step consumes and because pinning it separately (PIN 5) keeps the 0 < delta hypothesis visible rather than buried under delta in N.divisors. F31-B6 was again NOT used: the proof runs through B7's C-domain twin natCast_mul_mem_upperHalfPlaneSet_of_mem, so depends_on lists F31-B5 and F31-B7. SCOPE - read before citing. Differentiability AT POINTS OF THE OPEN upper half-plane and nothing else. This is NOT holomorphy near a cusp: upperHalfPlaneSet is open and the cusps are not in it. It is NOT meromorphy on X0(N), NOT a statement that the quotient extends to the compactified modular curve, and it says nothing about Gamma0(N), the slash action or the eta multiplier system. The Dedekind-sum obstruction recorded as F32-OBSTRUCTED is untouched, and F32-A1 (eta_T_transform) is still a sorry with its own UNPROVED tripwire in force and still passing. PLACEMENT, stated loudly (same deviation, same reason, as F31-B1..B7). The brief named Lean/SocrateAI/ModularForms/EtaQuotient.lean; that file is the ARITHMETIC layer whose import cone is deliberately Nat.divisors + Nat.totient only, while eta and upperHalfPlaneSet sit behind Mathlib.NumberTheory.ModularForms.DedekindEta. The declarations are in EtaQuotientModularity.lean instead, in a new F3.1-B8 block; the sorry that stood at the old F3.2-A2 site is gone and the statement was not moved, renamed or weakened. AXIOM FOOTPRINT [propext, Classical.choice, Quot.sound] with NO sorryAx for all three declarations (differentiableAt_eta_natCast_mul, differentiableAt_etaQuotient, differentiableAt_etaQuotient_prod), each guarded by #guard_msgs in #print axioms in FinalCheck.lean. The five statement pins (section B8Pins) write the propositions out with r typed as the bare Nat -> Int, upperHalfPlaneSet fully qualified, the product written longhand instead of hidden behind the definition, an Iff.rfl pin that the longhand and definitional forms are the SAME proposition, and a NEGATIVE-EXPONENT instance at r == -1 where DifferentiableAt.zpow's '0 <= m' disjunct is false -- so a proof that secretly assumed 0 <= r delta, or a drift to DifferentiableWithinAt / a pow instead of a zpow, would stop elaborating there. Final line of lake build: 'Build completed successfully (3475 jobs).'", "lean_name": "SocrateAI.ModularForms.differentiableAt_etaQuotient", "lean_file": "Lean/SocrateAI/ModularForms/EtaQuotientModularity.lean", "status": "proved", "depends_on": ["F31-B5", "F31-B7"], "paper_claim": null}
{"id": "F31-B9", "kind": "math", "statement_nl": "HEADLINE etaQuotient_add. PROVED, sorry-free. READ THE DUPLICATION NOTICE FIRST, because it is part of the result. The node was scoped as 'etaQuotient N (r + s) tau = etaQuotient N r tau * etaQuotient N s tau' with tau : H. In this library's naming that is etaQuotientH (the C-domain etaQuotient takes z : C), and THAT EXACT STATEMENT WAS ALREADY PROVED AND ALREADY GUARDED as SocrateAI.ModularForms.etaQuotientH_add, landed in the F3.1-B5 block and pinned in FinalCheck.lean as B5 PIN 4. It was not re-proved, and no second copy of it was made; B9 PIN 1 re-pins it in the B9 section so the overlap is visible in one place instead of being discovered later. WHAT B9 ACTUALLY ADDS, all genuinely absent before this commit. (a) etaQuotient_add: the same identity on the C-DOMAIN with the hypothesis in set-membership form z in upperHalfPlaneSet. Not cosmetic - differentiableAt_etaQuotient and every F3.2 statement are stated on C with that hypothesis shape, so the H form cannot be applied there without re-bundling the point; this is the same H-vs-C split as B5's natCast_mul_mem_upperHalfPlaneSet versus B7's ..._of_mem. Proof is Pi.add_apply plus Finset.prod_mul_distrib plus zpow_add_zero (zpow_add0) factorwise, with the nonzero base supplied by B7's eta_natCast_mul_ne_zero_of_mem and Nat.pos_of_mem_divisors - exactly the four ingredients the brief named. Compiled first try. Its companions etaQuotient_neg, etaQuotient_zsmul and etaQuotient_zero_exp carry NO hypothesis at all, because zpow_neg, zpow_mul and zpow_zero hold at every base including the junk value 0; that asymmetry localises where non-vanishing is genuinely needed, namely zpow_add0 alone. (b) etaQuotientUnit and etaQuotientHom: the homomorphism as an OBJECT rather than as an equation between values. etaQuotientUnit N r tau : C-units is the quotient bundled with F3.1-B7's non-vanishing via Units.mk0, and etaQuotientHom N : (Nat -> Int) ->+ Additive (H -> C-units) is r |-> (tau |-> f_r(tau)) into the POINTWISE GROUP of nowhere-vanishing functions on H, which is the phrasing the node description used. This is where F3.1-B7 is consumed essentially and not decoratively: without etaQuotientH_ne_zero there is no map into C-units at all, only into the monoid C, where map_neg does not exist. The bundling then yields etaQuotientUnit_neg and etaQuotientUnit_zsmul from Mathlib's map_neg and map_zsmul with no separate proof (both are one congrArg through Additive.toMul), and B9 PIN 5 is the longhand instance of that. (c) etaQuotientH_sum: the finite-combination form f_{sum_i r_i} = prod_i f_{r_i} over an arbitrary index Finset - a two-line Finset.induction_on over etaQuotientH_add - which is the shape a Ligozat computation actually applies. Reported honestly as an induction, NOT as a free consequence of map_sum: unwinding Additive sums into products was not attempted. (d) etaQuotient_add_compositional: an LL-1 CROSS-CHECK that proves nothing new. One elaborated proposition asserting that the SAME r + s multiplies the function (this node / B5), adds the Q-valued weight (F3.1-A1, etaQuotientWeight_add) and adds the Q-valued cusp order (F3.1-A6, etaQuotientCuspOrder_add). That triple is the sentence 'the Ligozat calculus is compositional', which was otherwise only prose in the module docstrings. PLACEMENT, stated loudly (same deviation, same reason, as F31-B1..B8). The brief named Lean/SocrateAI/ModularForms/EtaQuotient.lean; that file is the ARITHMETIC layer whose import cone is deliberately Nat.divisors + Nat.totient only, while eta and upperHalfPlaneSet sit behind Mathlib.NumberTheory.ModularForms.DedekindEta. The declarations are in EtaQuotientModularity.lean instead, in a new F3.1-B9 block placed after B8's differentiableAt_etaQuotient_prod and before the F3.2 sorries, so the proved F3.1-B ladder does not reach past them. SCOPE - read before citing. Algebra of zpow at a nonvanishing base on the OPEN upper half-plane, and nothing else. No Gamma0(N), no slash action, no multiplier system, nothing at a cusp: the etaQuotientCuspOrder appearing in (d) is the ARITHMETIC definition of F3.1-A, and the theorem that it really is the vanishing order of f remains open F3.2 work. F32-A1 (eta_T_transform) is still a sorry and the Dedekind-sum obstruction F32-OBSTRUCTED is untouched. AXIOM FOOTPRINT [propext, Classical.choice, Quot.sound] with NO sorryAx for all thirteen new declarations (etaQuotient_add, etaQuotient_neg, etaQuotient_zsmul, etaQuotient_zero_exp, etaQuotientUnit, etaQuotientUnit_coe, etaQuotientHom, etaQuotientHom_apply, etaQuotientUnit_add, etaQuotientUnit_neg, etaQuotientUnit_zsmul, etaQuotientH_sum, etaQuotient_add_compositional), each guarded by '#guard_msgs in #print axioms' in FinalCheck.lean. Seven statement pins (section B9Pins) write the propositions out with the exponent vector typed as the bare Nat -> Int, upperHalfPlaneSet fully qualified, the product written longhand instead of hidden behind the definition, the hom's TYPE ascribed explicitly so a retarget from the group C-units to the monoid C would fail to elaborate, and a NEGATIVE-EXPONENT instance at r == -1, s == 1 so a proof that secretly assumed 0 <= r delta would stop elaborating there. Final line of lake build: 'Build completed successfully (3475 jobs).'", "lean_name": "SocrateAI.ModularForms.etaQuotient_add", "lean_file": "Lean/SocrateAI/ModularForms/EtaQuotientModularity.lean", "status": "proved", "depends_on": ["F31-B5", "F31-B7", "F31-A1", "F31-A6"], "paper_claim": null}
{"id": "F31-B10", "kind": "math", "statement_nl": "HEADLINE etaQuotient_one_eq_discriminant, with the bundled guard etaQuotient_one_24_pins. PROVED, sorry-free. This is the SECOND LL-1 external guard: the only place in F3.1 where the definitions are checked against an object Mathlib certified rather than against each other. READ THE OVERLAP NOTICE FIRST. The discriminant identity itself was ALREADY landed and ALREADY guarded, as SocrateAI.ModularForms.etaQuotientH_level_one_24 in the F3.1-B5 block (EtaQuotientModularity.lean), and it was NOT re-proved here. etaQuotient_one_eq_discriminant is that lemma restated in the C-domain shape the node was scoped in - etaQuotient 1 (fun _ => 24) (tau : C) = ModularForm.discriminant tau, a rfl-level restatement since etaQuotientH unfolds to etaQuotient along the coercion - and its proof term is literally etaQuotientH_level_one_24 tau. Claiming B10 as new mathematics would be false. WHAT B10 ACTUALLY ADDS, all genuinely absent before this commit. (a) etaQuotientWeight_one_24 : etaQuotientWeight 1 (fun _ => 24) = 12. The weight layer pinned to the weight of Delta. One line, norm_num over Nat.divisors_one. (b) etaQuotientCuspOrder_one_24 : etaQuotientCuspOrder 1 (fun _ => 24) 1 = 1. The cusp-order layer pinned to the order to which Delta vanishes at infinity. This value existed before only as the A2 kernel guard '#guard etaQuotientCuspOrder 1 (fun _ => 24) 1 = 1' among the sanity values in EtaQuotient.lean. The upgrade from #guard to theorem is not cosmetic and is the reason the node is worth its cost: a theorem carries a proof term that #print axioms inspects and that FinalCheck can pin longhand, a #guard carries none and cannot be cited by another theorem. Evidence label moves A2 -> A1. (c) dedekindPsi_one : dedekindPsi 1 = 1, likewise the theorem form of an existing A8 #guard, needed by (d). (d) sum_etaQuotientCuspOrder_one_24 : the N = 1 instance of the F3.1-A10 valence identity, evaluated to the literal 1. Left side is built from etaQuotientCuspOrder, right side from etaQuotientWeight and dedekindPsi, and 1 is the classical divisor degree of Delta on SL(2,Z). So A10 is here pinned against a KNOWN FORM rather than against the rTest16 / rTest36 vectors it was previously only checked on. (e) etaQuotient_one_24_pins : the conjunction of the three layers at the same exponent vector. This is the node's actual content. Separately each conjunct is checkable by a reader who knows Delta; together they say the FUNCTION layer, the WEIGHT layer and the ORDER layer of this development all specialise to the same classical object at the one level where that object is available in Mathlib. A 24 that migrated between an exponent and a scaling, or a weight convention off by a factor 2, can survive a single conjunct and cannot survive the conjunction. PLACEMENT, stated loudly (same deviation, same reason, as F31-B1..B9). The brief named Lean/SocrateAI/ModularForms/EtaQuotient.lean. That file is the ARITHMETIC layer whose import cone is deliberately Nat.divisors + Nat.totient only, while ModularForm.eta and ModularForm.discriminant sit behind Mathlib.NumberTheory.ModularForms.Discriminant. The split follows the layer, not the node: (a)-(d), which mention no eta, ARE in EtaQuotient.lean, in a new 'F3.1-B10 (arithmetic half)' block after end A10Guards; the two declarations that mention Delta, etaQuotient_one_eq_discriminant and etaQuotient_one_24_pins, are in EtaQuotientModularity.lean immediately after etaQuotientH_level_one_24 so the overlap with B5 is visible at the point of reading. No import was added to either file. SCOPE - read before citing. Level N = 1 only. Nothing here is a theorem about eta quotients at general N: etaQuotientCuspOrder remains a transcribed DEFINITION, and the theorem that it is the vanishing order of f at the cusp c/d is still open F3.2 work. F32-A1 (eta_T_transform) is still a sorry and the Dedekind-sum obstruction F32-OBSTRUCTED is untouched. AXIOM FOOTPRINT [propext, Classical.choice, Quot.sound] with NO sorryAx for all six new declarations (dedekindPsi_one, etaQuotientWeight_one_24, etaQuotientCuspOrder_one_24, sum_etaQuotientCuspOrder_one_24, etaQuotient_one_eq_discriminant, etaQuotient_one_24_pins), each guarded by '#guard_msgs in #print axioms' in FinalCheck.lean. Five statement pins (section B10Pins) write the propositions out longhand: the exponent vector as the bare Nat -> Int rather than the EtaExp abbreviation, the product over (1 : Nat).divisors spelled out instead of hidden behind etaQuotient, ModularForm.discriminant fully qualified, the cusp-order formula written with its gcds and its N / d division intact, and the two numeric right-hand sides as literals in Q. NON-VACUITY CHECKED, not assumed: perturbing PIN 1's index set from (1 : Nat).divisors to (1 : Nat).properDivisors and PIN 2's right-hand side from 12 to 13 both fail to elaborate ('error: Type mismatch' at FinalCheck.lean:939 and :943); the perturbation was reverted and the full build re-run green. Final line of lake build: 'Build completed successfully (3475 jobs).'", "lean_name": "SocrateAI.ModularForms.etaQuotient_one_eq_discriminant", "lean_file": "Lean/SocrateAI/ModularForms/EtaQuotientModularity.lean", "status": "proved", "depends_on": ["F31-B5", "F31-A1", "F31-A2", "F31-A8", "F31-A10"], "paper_claim": null}
{"id": "F31-B11", "kind": "math", "statement_nl": "HEADLINE etaQuotient_eq_qpow_mul. PROVED, sorry-free. STATEMENT, verbatim as scoped: for every N : Nat, every r : Nat -> Int and every tau : H, etaQuotient N r tau = Complex.exp (2 * pi * I * tau * (sum over delta in N.divisors of (delta : C) * (r delta : C)) / 24) * (product over delta in N.divisors of (tprod over n : Nat of (1 - ModularForm.eta_q n ((delta : C) * tau))) ^ (r delta)). IN ENGLISH (the LL-1 check): the eta quotient equals its leading q-power q^{(sum_delta delta r_delta)/24} times the tail obtained by deleting the q^{1/24} from every eta factor. That is exactly the split the node asked for. NO hypothesis on N and NO sign hypothesis on r: mul_zpow holds unconditionally in C (a CommGroupWithZero), so the junk value at base 0 never has to be excluded here. PROOF, and it really was the Mathlib lemmas the brief named (LL-11), no new machinery, no analysis. Mathlib defines ModularForm.eta z = Function.Periodic.qParam 24 z * tprod_n (1 - eta_q n z) with qParam h z = exp (2 pi i z / h). Per factor: mul_zpow splits eta(delta tau)^{r delta} into qParam-half times tail-half; unfolding qParam and applying Complex.exp_int_mul BACKWARDS turns exp(w)^{r delta} into exp((r delta) * w); push_cast + ring normalises the argument to 2 pi i (delta * r delta) tau / 24. Then Finset.prod_congr rewrites every factor, Finset.prod_mul_distrib separates the two products, Complex.exp_sum collects the divisor sum of arguments into a single exp, and Finset.mul_sum + Finset.sum_div + Finset.sum_congr + ring identify that sum with 2 pi i tau (sum_delta delta r_delta) / 24. FOUR COMPANION DECLARATIONS, reported rather than hidden. (a) etaQuotientH_eq_qpow_mul: the same identity for etaQuotientH on the bundled upper half-plane; its proof term is literally etaQuotient_eq_qpow_mul, since etaQuotientH is etaQuotient along the coercion H -> C. Not new mathematics; it exists so that H-domain consumers need not unfold the definition. (b) etaQuotient_qProduct_ne_zero: the TAIL is non-zero at every point of H, for an arbitrary integer exponent vector. Finset.prod_ne_zero_iff plus zpow_ne_zero plus Mathlib's ModularForm.eta_tprod_ne_zero, whose hypothesis delta*tau in upperHalfPlaneSet is supplied by F3.1-B6 (mem_upperHalfPlaneSet_divisor_smul). This is the node's first genuine use of B6. (c) etaQuotient_qpow_exponent_eq_cuspOrder_infty: the LL-1 BRIDGE between the arithmetic and analytic layers - the exponent produced from Mathlib's q-product for eta, namely (sum_delta delta r_delta)/24, is the SAME rational number as etaQuotientCuspOrder N r N, the transcribed Ligozat formula of F3.1-A2 evaluated at the cusp infinity by F3.1-A3. Proof is rw [etaQuotientCuspOrder_infty]; push_cast; ring, and it needs N != 0 (the only hypothesis anywhere in this node), inherited from A3. (d) etaQuotient_eq_qpow_cuspOrder_mul: the packaged form f(tau) = exp(2 pi i tau * ord_infty(N,r)) * tail, i.e. 'the leading q-power of an eta quotient is q^{ord_infty}', with ord_infty the ARITHMETIC definition. WHY THE NODE MATTERS, stated at its true strength. The node description says this makes ord at i-infinity a derived quantity rather than a stipulation. What is now derived is the IDENTITY OF EXPONENTS: the number the Ligozat formula assigns to the cusp infinity is the number that actually appears in the exponential factor of the function, plus the fact that the remaining factor is non-zero at every point of H. HONEST LIMIT OF THE CLAIM (LL-1), stated loudly because it is the difference between what was proved and what the phrase 'ord at infinity' might be read to mean. This is NOT the analytic statement that ord_infty is the vanishing order of f at the cusp. That additionally requires the tail to tend to a NON-ZERO limit as im tau -> infinity (classically it tends to 1, since every eta_q n (delta tau) -> 0). NO LIMIT IS TAKEN ANYWHERE in this node or in the file: etaQuotient_qProduct_ne_zero is POINTWISE non-vanishing on the open upper half-plane, not a limit statement, and no Filter, Tendsto or cusp neighbourhood appears. The missing step is a standard but genuine piece of analysis (uniform convergence of the eta q-product as im -> infinity) and it is NOT claimed here. PLACEMENT, stated loudly (same deviation, same reason, as F31-B1..B10). The brief named Lean/SocrateAI/ModularForms/EtaQuotient.lean; that file is the ARITHMETIC layer whose import cone is deliberately Nat.divisors + Nat.totient only, while ModularForm.eta, ModularForm.eta_q and Function.Periodic.qParam sit behind Mathlib.NumberTheory.ModularForms.DedekindEta. All five declarations are in EtaQuotientModularity.lean instead, in a new F3.1-B11 block placed after etaQuotient_add_compositional (end of the B9 material) and before etaQuotient_pow_24, so the proved F3.1-B ladder still does not reach past the F3.2 sorries. No import was added to either file. SCOPE - read before citing. Algebra of exp and zpow on the OPEN upper half-plane. No Gamma0(N), no slash action, no multiplier system, nothing at a cusp, no limit. F32-A1 (eta_T_transform) is still a sorry and the Dedekind-sum obstruction F32-OBSTRUCTED is untouched. AXIOM FOOTPRINT [propext, Classical.choice, Quot.sound] with NO sorryAx for all five new declarations (etaQuotient_eq_qpow_mul, etaQuotientH_eq_qpow_mul, etaQuotient_qProduct_ne_zero, etaQuotient_qpow_exponent_eq_cuspOrder_infty, etaQuotient_eq_qpow_cuspOrder_mul), each guarded by '#guard_msgs in #print axioms' in FinalCheck.lean. Five statement pins (section B11Pins) write the propositions out longhand: the exponent vector as the bare Nat -> Int rather than the EtaExp abbreviation, the product over Nat.divisors spelled out instead of hidden behind etaQuotient, ModularForm.eta and ModularForm.eta_q fully qualified, the divisor scaling (delta : C) * tau present on both sides of the split, the packaged q^{ord_infty} form asserted TOGETHER with the tail non-vanishing so the two cannot drift apart, and PIN 5 an external Delta cross-check at N = 1, r == 24: Mathlib's ModularForm.discriminant equals exp(2 pi i tau * 1) times the tail, i.e. leading exponent 1, the classical ord_infty(Delta) = 1 taken from the literature and not from our definition. NON-VACUITY CHECKED, not assumed: three perturbations of PIN 1 all fail to elaborate with 'error: Type mismatch' - (i) dropping the factor delta inside the sum, (ii) / 12 instead of / 24, (iii) the tail at the unscaled point eta_q n tau instead of eta_q n (delta tau). Recorded in scratch/B11perturb.lean, which keeps the failing forms as comments and the passing form as live code. Final line of lake build: 'Build completed successfully (3475 jobs).'", "lean_name": "SocrateAI.ModularForms.etaQuotient_eq_qpow_mul", "lean_file": "Lean/SocrateAI/ModularForms/EtaQuotientModularity.lean", "status": "proved", "depends_on": ["F31-B5", "F31-B6", "F31-A2", "F31-A3"], "paper_claim": null}
{"id": "F31-B12", "kind": "math", "statement_nl": "HEADLINE tendsto_etaQuotient_tprod_factor. PROVED, sorry-free. STATEMENT, verbatim as scoped: for every N : Nat and every r : Nat -> Int, Filter.Tendsto (fun tau : H => product over delta in N.divisors of (tprod over n : Nat of (1 - ModularForm.eta_q n ((delta : C) * tau))) ^ (r delta)) UpperHalfPlane.atImInfty (nhds 1). IN ENGLISH (the LL-1 check): the NON-LEADING factor of the F3.1-B11 split tends to 1 as im tau -> infinity. NO hypothesis on N and NO sign hypothesis on r. At N = 0 the divisor set is empty and the product is the constant 1, so the statement is true there too rather than excluded. WHY THIS NODE MATTERS, and it is precisely the caveat B11 had to attach to itself. B11 proved the algebraic split f = q^{ord_infty} * tail plus POINTWISE non-vanishing of the tail on the open upper half-plane, and said loudly that this is NOT the analytic claim that ord_infty is the vanishing order at the cusp, because a factor non-zero at every point of H may still decay to 0 as im tau -> infinity. B12 supplies exactly the missing limit. Combined with B11 this yields the packaged corollary tendsto_etaQuotientH_div_qpow: f(tau) / exp(2 pi i tau * ord_infty(N,r)) -> 1 along atImInfty, i.e. the order of the eta quotient at the cusp infinity IS etaQuotientCuspOrder N r N = (1/24) sum_delta delta r_delta, the F3.1-A3 value. This is the one genuine analytic cusp-order statement the F3.1 block can reach without the eta multiplier system. WHAT HAD TO BE GENERALISED. Mathlib has ModularForm.tendsto_atImInfty_tprod_one_sub_eta_q_pow but it is hard-wired to the discriminant: exponent exactly 24 : Nat, and no dilation (h = 1, argument tau rather than delta*tau). Both restrictions had to go at once - the dilation delta*tau for delta | N and the exponent r delta : Int of EITHER sign - and neither is obtainable by instantiating that lemma. PROOF, and it was again three Mathlib lemmas (LL-11) rather than the dominated-convergence machinery Mathlib unfolds inline for its 24 case. (1) ModularForm.differentiableOn_tprod_one_sub_pow says F(q) = tprod_n (1 - q^{n+1}) is DIFFERENTIABLE on the open unit disc; differentiable => continuous, 0 is an interior point, and F(0) = tprod 1 = 1, so F(q) -> 1 as q -> 0. No summability estimate is written by hand. (2) The dilation is a q-power, not a new function: qParam_one_natCast_mul proves qParam 1 (delta * z) = (qParam 1 z)^delta from qParam 1 z = exp(2 pi i z) and Complex.exp_nat_mul, so tprod_n (1 - eta_q n (delta tau)) is literally F evaluated at (qParam 1 tau)^delta; UpperHalfPlane.qParam_tendsto_atImInfty plus Tendsto.pow sends that to 0^delta = 0, which is where delta != 0 is used and where Nat.pos_of_mem_divisors supplies it. (3) The integer exponent is Filter.Tendsto.zpow0 at the limit 1, whose side condition (a != 0 or 0 <= m) is discharged on the LEFT by one_ne_zero - this is why negative exponents need no hypothesis: the limit is 1, not 0. Finally tendsto_finsetProd multiplies the divisors and the empty/constant product of ones is 1. THREE COMPANION DECLARATIONS, reported rather than hidden. (a) qParam_one_natCast_mul - the dilated q-parameter is a q-power, qParam 1 (delta z) = (qParam 1 z)^delta for delta : Nat. Two lines; it is the only place the dilation interacts with the q-expansion. (b) tendsto_tprod_one_sub_eta_q_natCast_mul - the PER-FACTOR generalisation of the Mathlib lemma: for delta != 0, tprod_n (1 - eta_q n (delta tau)) -> 1 along atImInfty, with the exponent 24 removed and the dilation added. This is the reusable piece. (c) tendsto_etaQuotientH_div_qpow - the packaged B11+B12 corollary, f/q^{ord_infty} -> 1, carrying the hypothesis N != 0 inherited from F3.1-A3 (the cusp-order formula at d = N), NOT from the analysis. SCOPE - read before citing. The cusp infinity ONLY. Nothing here touches Gamma0(N), the slash action, the eta multiplier system, or any other cusp c/d; the other cusps are exactly what needs the multiplier and that is what F32-OBSTRUCTED records. F32-A1 (eta_T_transform) is still a sorry and the Dedekind-sum obstruction is untouched. The sorry count of EtaQuotientModularity.lean is unchanged at 19 occurrences / 13 sorry-carrying declarations, all in the F3.2 block. PLACEMENT, stated loudly (same deviation, same reason, as F31-B1..B11). The brief named Lean/SocrateAI/ModularForms/EtaQuotient.lean; that file is the ARITHMETIC layer whose import cone is deliberately Nat.divisors + Nat.totient only, while ModularForm.eta_q, Function.Periodic.qParam and UpperHalfPlane.atImInfty sit behind Mathlib.NumberTheory.ModularForms.DedekindEta / Discriminant. All four declarations are in EtaQuotientModularity.lean instead, in a new F3.1-B12 block placed immediately after the B11 material and before etaQuotient_pow_24. No import was added to either file. AXIOM FOOTPRINT [propext, Classical.choice, Quot.sound] with NO sorryAx, for all four new declarations (qParam_one_natCast_mul, tendsto_tprod_one_sub_eta_q_natCast_mul, tendsto_etaQuotient_tprod_factor, tendsto_etaQuotientH_div_qpow), each guarded by '#guard_msgs in #print axioms' in FinalCheck.lean. FOUR STATEMENT PINS (section B12Pins in FinalCheck.lean) write the propositions out longhand: PIN 1 the node verbatim with the bare Nat -> Int exponent vector, Filter.Tendsto / UpperHalfPlane.atImInfty / nhds 1 spelled out and the dilation (delta : C) * tau present inside eta_q; PIN 2 the analytic order statement with etaQuotient unfolded to the bare product of ModularForm.eta values, so nothing hides behind our abbreviation; PIN 3 the MATHLIB CROSS-CHECK run in the strong direction - Mathlib's own tendsto_atImInfty_tprod_one_sub_eta_q_pow (exponent 24, no dilation) is REPROVED from our generalisation using only Multipliable.tprod_pow to move the 24 across the tprod; PIN 4 the Delta cross-check against the literature - at N = 1, r == 24 the corollary gives Delta(tau)/exp(2 pi i tau * 1) -> 1, i.e. ord_infty(Delta) = 1, the classical value, which strengthens Mathlib's discriminant_isZeroAtImInfty from 'zero at i infinity' to 'zero to order exactly one'. NON-VACUITY CHECKED, not assumed: three perturbations fed the real proof term all fail with 'error: Type mismatch' - (i) nhds 0 in place of nhds 1 (atImInfty is NeBot so limits are unique), (ii) 2 * ord_infty in place of ord_infty in the divided q-power, (iii) claiming the dilated q-parameter equals the undilated one. Recorded in scratch/B12perturb.lean, which keeps the failing forms as comments and the node itself as live code. Final line of lake build: 'Build completed successfully (3475 jobs).'", "lean_name": "SocrateAI.ModularForms.tendsto_etaQuotient_tprod_factor", "lean_file": "Lean/SocrateAI/ModularForms/EtaQuotientModularity.lean", "status": "proved", "depends_on": ["F31-B11", "F31-A3", "F31-B5"], "paper_claim": null}
# --- F3.1-B13: the cusp INFINITY, in Mathlib's own meromorphicOrderAt language. ---
{"id": "F31-B13", "kind": "math", "statement_nl": "PROVED. THE ORDER OF VANISHING OF AN ETA QUOTIENT AT THE CUSP INFINITY, IN MATHLIB'S OWN ORDER-OF-VANISHING LANGUAGE. For every N, every r : N -> Z and every m : Z with 24*m = sum_{delta | N} delta * r_delta, meromorphicOrderAt (UpperHalfPlane.cuspFunction 1 (etaQuotientH N r)) 0 = m; and if etaQuotientCuspOrder N r N = (m : Q) (equivalently, by ligozatCongr1_iff (F31-A7), if Ligozat's first congruence holds) then that m is Ligozat's cusp-order value at the cusp denominator d = N. meromorphicOrderAt is Mathlib (Analysis/Meromorphic/Order.lean), cuspFunction is Mathlib (NumberTheory/ModularForms/QExpansion.lean), and width 1 is Mathlib's strictWidthInfty_Gamma0; no SocrateAI notion of 'order at a cusp' is introduced. PROOF: rewrite F31-B11's split in the local parameter q = qParam 1 tau, where the hypothesis 24 m = sum delta r_delta turns the leading exponential into the INTEGER power q^m (Complex.exp_int_mul) and the tail becomes etaQuotientTail N r q = prod_delta (prod'_n (1 - (q^delta)^(n+1)))^{r_delta}; that tail is analytic at 0 (Mathlib's differentiableOn_tprod_one_sub_pow, composed with q -> q^delta, then AnalyticAt.fun_zpow whose nonvanishing side condition is the value 1, which is what admits NEGATIVE exponents) and equals 1 at q = 0. cuspFunction_etaQuotientH computes Mathlib's cusp function on the punctured disc via invQParam / qParam_right_inv; meromorphicOrderAt_eq_int_iff, whose criterion is on a PUNCTURED neighbourhood, then gives the order without ever touching the junk value at q = 0 and without any holomorphy or positivity hypothesis (the order may be negative). SCOPE (LL-1): this is the cusp INFINITY only. Every other cusp needs the eta multiplier system for a general gamma in Gamma0(N) (Dedekind sums, absent from Mathlib) - see F31-OBSTRUCTED. EVIDENCE: axiom footprint [propext, Classical.choice, Quot.sound], no sorryAx, ten #guard_msgs #print axioms guards plus three statement pins in FinalCheck.lean; external literature pin meromorphicOrderAt_cuspFunction_discriminant gives ord_infty(Delta) = 1, the classical value, which Mathlib states independently as discriminant_qExpansion_order in a module outside this workspace's built cone. Non-vacuity checked: asserting the value 2 for Delta, and dropping the factor 24 from the hypothesis, both fail to compile.", "lean_name": "SocrateAI.ModularForms.meromorphicOrderAt_cuspFunction_eq_cuspOrder_infty", "lean_file": "Lean/SocrateAI/ModularForms/EtaQuotientCuspOrder.lean", "status": "proved", "depends_on": ["F31-A2", "F31-A3", "F31-A7", "F31-B5", "F31-B11", "F31-B12"], "paper_claim": null}
# --- F3.1-OBSTRUCTED: the general cusp c/d.  An honest negative; see the file docstring. ---
{"id": "F31-OBSTRUCTED", "kind": "math", "statement_nl": "THE NAMED OBSTRUCTION, and a deliverable in its own right (an honest negative). The claim that etaQuotientCuspOrder N r d IS the analytic order of vanishing of prod_delta eta(delta z)^{r_delta} at a general cusp c/d (Ligozat; Ono, Web of Modularity, Thm 1.65) is NOT proved, NOT assumed, and deliberately NOT STATED anywhere in this development; stating it would be the LL-1 failure of a green build of the wrong theorem. RE-VERIFIED AGAINST MATHLIB 905b95818eb32af7874a58b427f50c1711a5e96c, and ONE OF THE TWO BLOCKERS THIS NODE WAS HANDED IS WRONG. Blocker (1), CONFIRMED: the classical proof moves c/d to infinity by some gamma in SL(2,Z) and needs the eta multiplier system for a general gamma, classically written with Dedekind sums; grep -rl over Mathlib returns 0 files for each of DedekindSum, dedekindSum, etaMultiplier, eta_multiplier, Ligozat, EtaQuotient. Mathlib has the S-transformation (eta_comp_eq_csqrt_I_inv) and we have the T-transformation (F31-B2/B3), but the multiplier is a cocycle, so generating SL(2,Z) does not hand over the multiplier of an arbitrary word without the Dedekind-sum bookkeeping - the same wall F32-OBSTRUCTED meets from the other side. Blocker (2), REFUTED: the claim 'Mathlib has no notion of order of vanishing at a cusp at all' rested on orderAt / vanishingOrder / cuspWidth / widthAt each returning zero files. Those four greps do return zero, but the inference is a CASE ARTEFACT: grep -rl 'orderAt' returns 0 files while grep -rli 'orderat' returns 19, because the declarations are analyticOrderAt and meromorphicOrderAt with a capital O. Mathlib at this commit has Analysis/Analytic/Order.lean (analyticOrderAt), Analysis/Meromorphic/Order.lean (meromorphicOrderAt, meromorphicOrderAt_eq_int_iff), NumberTheory/ModularForms/Cusps.lean (IsCusp, CuspOrbits with a Finite instance, strictWidthInfty / widthInfty and strictWidthInfty_Gamma0 N = 1) and NumberTheory/ModularForms/QExpansion.lean (UpperHalfPlane.cuspFunction, qExpansion, analyticAt_cuspFunction_zero). So the left-hand side of the equation IS stateable at the cusp infinity, and F31-B13 states and PROVES it there. WHAT IS ACTUALLY MISSING, after the correction: (a) the eta multiplier for a general gamma in Gamma0(N) - a genuine obstruction; (b) an order of vanishing at a cusp OTHER than infinity - Mathlib's width is widthInfty only, there is no widthAtCusp and no orderAtCusp, though these are constructible from conjGL + widthInfty + the slash action, so this is missing API rather than an obstruction; (c) the indexing data of the classical statement, namely that the cusps of Gamma0(N) are parametrised by d | N with multiplicity phi(gcd(d,N/d)) and that [SL(2,Z) : Gamma0(N)] = psi(N) - neither is in Mathlib (no index formula for Gamma0 anywhere) and neither is proved here; numCusps and dedekindPsi (F31-A8) carry those classical READINGS and nothing more. NET POSITION: F3.1 ships etaQuotientCuspOrder as a DEFINITION validated by the valence identity F31-A10 and the kernel-decided guards, PLUS one cusp - d = N, the cusp infinity - where it is now a theorem (F31-B13). At d != N it remains a reading, not a theorem of this development. Status blocked because the general-cusp claim is unreached; there is no lean_name because the deliverable is precisely that no such declaration exists. The record, with the greps, is the module docstring of Lean/SocrateAI/ModularForms/EtaQuotientCuspOrder.lean.", "lean_name": null, "lean_file": "Lean/SocrateAI/ModularForms/EtaQuotientCuspOrder.lean", "status": "blocked", "depends_on": ["F31-A2", "F31-B13"], "paper_claim": null}
{"id": "F32-B1", "kind": "math", "statement_nl": "HEADLINE Gamma0_generated_of_le_four. PROVED, sorry-free. STATEMENT, verbatim as landed: for N : Nat with hN : 0 < N and hN4 : N <= 4, Subgroup.closure {(-1 : SL(2,Z)), ModularGroup.T, matV N} = CongruenceSubgroup.Gamma0 N. The node's own Nat+ phrasing is landed alongside as Gamma0_generated_of_le_four_pnat (N : PNat, hN : (N : Nat) <= 4), which is the scoped signature. TWO DEVIATIONS FROM THE SCOPED STATEMENT, both stated loudly and neither a weakening. (1) The scoped third generator was written '!![1,0;-(N:Z),1]', which is a Matrix and not an element of SL(2,Z), so the set as written does not typecheck; the landed generator is matV N (F3.2-A8), and matV_coe : (matV N : Matrix (Fin 2) (Fin 2) Z) = !![1,0;-(N:Z),1] is definitional (rfl). FinalCheck PIN 3 pins that identification. (2) The scoped right-hand side was written '(CongruenceSubgroup.Gamma0 N).toSubgroup'; Mathlib's Gamma0 N IS a Subgroup SL(2,Z) already (CongruenceSubgroups.lean), so there is no .toSubgroup and the landed equality is between two Subgroup SL(2,Z). FinalCheck PIN 4 re-pins the right-hand side as the raw condition (N : Z) | g 1 0, not as the Gamma0 abbreviation. WHAT WAS PROVED, IN ENGLISH (LL-1). For each of the four levels N = 1, 2, 3, 4, the subgroup of SL(2,Z) generated by the three matrices -I, T = !![1,1;0,1] and V = !![1,0;-N,1] is EXACTLY Gamma0(N), the matrices whose lower-left entry is divisible by N. Both inclusions are proved. THE EASY INCLUSION (closure_gamma0Gens_le) holds for EVERY N and is three one-line membership checks. THE HARD INCLUSION is a Euclidean descent on the lower-left entry c, run entirely inside <T, V>: T^n . gamma replaces a by A := a + n c and fixes c (T_zpow_mul_zero_zero), V^m . gamma replaces c by -mN a + c and fixes a (matV_zpow_mul_one_zero). Writing c = N c' (legitimate: N | c is exactly membership in Gamma0(N)), pick n by BALANCED division so 2|A| <= |c| = N|c'|, then pick m the same way so 2|c' + mA| <= |A|; the new lower-left entry is N(c' + mA), strictly smaller in absolute value provided |A| < 2|c'|. WHERE N <= 4 IS SPENT - THE ONLY PLACE. For N <= 3, 2|A| <= 3|c'| < 4|c'| gives |A| < 2|c'| outright. For N = 4 the estimate only gives |A| <= 2|c'|, and the boundary case 2|A| = |c| is killed by ARITHMETIC rather than analysis: there A | c, and IsCoprime A c (a restatement of det gamma = 1, sl_det_entries) forces A to be a unit, hence |c| = 2, impossible when 4 | c and c is nonzero. At N = 5 the estimate FAILS - descent_bound_fails_at_five records the counterexample (A, c') = (5, 2): 2*5 <= 5*2 but 5 >= 2*2. An adversarial rerun of the entire block with 'N <= 5' substituted for 'N <= 4' was performed and fails at exactly the hkey inequality inside gamma0_descent and at NO other step, so the hypothesis is load-bearing rather than decorative. THE DEGENERATE BRANCH, stated honestly. A = 0 makes the V-step useless. But A = 0 forces c | a, hence |c| = 1 by coprimality, hence N = 1 (since N | c); at level one S = (T V_1 T)^{-1} lies in the closure (T_mul_matV_one_mul_T, S_mem_closure_gens_one) and S T^n gamma has lower-left entry A = 0. So S is used, but ONLY at N = 1, where it belongs to Gamma0(1). THE BASE CASE. c = 0 plus det = 1 forces a = d = +-1, so gamma = T^b or gamma = (-I) T^{-b} (eq_T_zpow_of_lower_left_zero, eq_neg_T_zpow_of_lower_left_zero). MATHLIB INPUTS ACTUALLY USED (LL-11 - the hard-looking step was three library lemmas). Int.bmod with Int.le_bmod, Int.bmod_lt and Int.dvd_self_sub_bmod give BALANCED remainders (exists_balanced_add); the ordinary Int.emod bound |r| < |y| is NOT strong enough and would stop the descent at N <= 2. ModularGroup.coe_T_zpow gives T^n in closed form; conj_zpow plus ModularGroup.S_inv transport it to V^m through matV_eq_conj : V = S T^N S^{-1} (matV_zpow_coe), so no fresh zpow induction was written. IsCoprime.isUnit_of_dvd and Int.isUnit_iff do the N = 4 boundary case. Mathlib's SpecialLinearGroup.SL2Z_generators is NOT used in the proof; it is only the external check behind guard 1. SCOPE - READ BEFORE CITING. This is a statement about Gamma0(N) as an abstract subgroup of SL(2,Z). It says NOTHING about eta quotients, and it is FALSE as stated for general N (already Gamma0(5) needs a fourth generator). It does NOT close F3.2-OBSTRUCTED: it supplies the generation half only, and the character chi(d) bookkeeping of full Ligozat is still missing. What it does supply is that for N <= 4 the multiplier w of F3.2-A5, being a HOMOMORPHISM, is determined by w(-I) (etaMultiplierVal_neg_one), w(T) (F3.2-A6) and w(V) (F3.2-A8) - all three already computed - with no eta multiplier system and no Dedekind sums. FOUR LL-1 GUARDS. GUARD 1 gamma0Gens_one_top: at N = 1 the theorem specialises to closure = top, i.e. SL(2,Z) = <-I, T, V_1>, which is the S = (T V_1 T)^{-1} rewriting of Mathlib's SL2Z_generators - a wrong V would break it. GUARD 2 S_not_mem_closure_gens_two and closure_gamma0Gens_two_ne_top: S is not in Gamma0(2), so at N = 2 the closure is a PROPER subgroup - the theorem has not silently degenerated into 'closure = top'. GUARD 3 descent_bound_fails_at_five: the counterexample that pins where N <= 4 is spent. GUARD 4 testGamma0Four_mem_closure: the concrete element !![3,1;8,3] of Gamma0(4) is a word in the generators. FOUR STATEMENT PINS (section F32B1Pin in FinalCheck.lean): the three generators pinned entrywise as raw 2x2 integer matrices, and the node longhand as 'g in closure {...} <-> (N : Z) | g 1 0'. AXIOM FOOTPRINT [propext, Classical.choice, Quot.sound], NO sorryAx, for all nineteen declarations guarded by '#guard_msgs in #print axioms' in FinalCheck.lean: exists_balanced_add, sl_det_entries, matV_eq_conj, matV_zpow_coe, T_zpow_mul_zero_zero, matV_zpow_mul_one_zero, S_mul_one_zero, closure_gamma0Gens_le, T_mul_matV_one_mul_T, S_mem_closure_gens_one, gamma0_descent, mem_closure_gamma0Gens_aux, Gamma0_generated_of_le_four, Gamma0_generated_of_le_four_pnat, gamma0Gens_one_top, S_not_mem_closure_gens_two, closure_gamma0Gens_two_ne_top, descent_bound_fails_at_five, testGamma0Four_mem_closure. FILE PLACEMENT, a deviation from the brief: the brief said EtaQuotient.lean, but that file has a deliberately restricted import cone (Nat.divisors + Nat.totient only, no SL(2,Z), no Mathlib modular-forms) and contained no sorry to replace. The block was landed in EtaQuotientModularity.lean, immediately before the F3.2-OBSTRUCTED section, where matV, T_mem_Gamma0, neg_one_mem_Gamma0 and dvd_lower_left_of_mem_Gamma0 already live and where downstream F3.2 work can use it without an import cycle. Final line of lake build: 'Build completed successfully (3476 jobs).'", "lean_name": "SocrateAI.ModularForms.Gamma0_generated_of_le_four", "lean_file": "Lean/SocrateAI/ModularForms/EtaQuotientModularity.lean", "status": "proved", "depends_on": [], "paper_claim": null}
# --- F3.2-B2: FULL LIGOZAT for N <= 4.  Generation (B1) replaces evaluation of the multiplier. ---
{"id": "F32-B2", "kind": "math", "statement_nl": "HEADLINE ligozat_of_le_four. PROVED, sorry-free. FULL LIGOZAT FOR N <= 4. STATEMENT, verbatim as landed: for N : Nat with 0 < N and N <= 4, r : Nat -> Int, k : Int with sum over delta in N.divisors of r delta = 2*k, h1 : LigozatCongr1 N r, h2 : LigozatCongr2 N r, and ANY monoid hom w : Gamma0 N ->* Cx with w <T, T_mem_Gamma0 N> = 1, w <matV N, matV_mem_Gamma0 N> = 1 and w <-1, neg_one_mem_Gamma0 N> = (-1 : Cx)^k: for every gamma : Gamma0 N and every z : H, etaQuotientH N r (gamma . z) = (w gamma : C) * (denom gamma z)^k * etaQuotientH N r z. The word UNIQUE in the node scoping is a THEOREM, landed separately as etaMultiplierHom_eq_of_le_four : any such w EQUALS the character etaMultiplierHom r hk produced by F32-A5. The Nat+ phrasing of the node is landed as ligozat_of_le_four_pnat. WHAT WAS PROVED, IN ENGLISH (LL-1). F32-A5 produced, for every N and every r of even weight-sum and with NO congruence conditions, a character w : Gamma0 N ->* Cx of order dividing 24 with f(gamma z) = w(gamma)(cz+d)^k f(z); what A5 could not do is SAY WHAT w IS. This node says it, for N <= 4, by pure group theory and with no new analysis: Ligozat congruence (i) is exactly w T = 1 (F32-A6), congruence (ii) is exactly w V = 1 (F32-A8), w(-I) = (-1)^k holds unconditionally (F32-A9 / etaMultiplierVal_neg_one), and for N <= 4 the three matrices -I, T = !![1,1;0,1], V = !![1,0;-N,1] GENERATE Gamma0(N) (F32-B1). A homomorphism is determined by its values on a generating set (Mathlib's MonoidHom.eq_of_eqOn_dense), so w is THE unique character with those three values. THE GENERATION IS TRANSPORTED INTO THE SUBTYPE, which is where a character of Gamma0(N) actually lives: closure_gamma0GensSub_eq_top_of_gen turns B1's equation inside SL(2,Z) into closure {gens} = TOP inside the group Gamma0 N, via Subgroup.map_subtype_inj (the subtype inclusion is injective, so map reflects equality), MonoidHom.map_closure and Subgroup.range_subtype. A STATEMENT CORRECTION, REPORTED LOUDLY, NOT BURIED. The sorry this node replaced carried the statement 'f(gamma z) = (denom gamma z)^k f(z) for all gamma in Gamma0 N, given (i), (ii) and generation'. That statement is FALSE. At gamma = -I, which lies in Gamma0(N) and in the closure of the generators, the left side is f(z) (-I acts trivially on H) and the right side is (-1)^k f(z); since f never vanishes (F31-B7) the two agree iff k is EVEN, and Ligozat's congruences do not force k even. The counterexample is landed and proved, not asserted: ligozatOddExp is r_1 = -3, r_3 = 9 at N = 3, with sum r_delta = 6 = 2*3 so k = 3 is ODD, sum delta*r_delta = 24 (congruence (i) holds) and sum (3/delta)*r_delta = 0 (congruence (ii) holds), N = 3 <= 4 so generation is a theorem (ligozatOdd_hgen), and not_multiplier_trivial_odd proves the conclusion FAILS. Classically this is the nebentypus: eta(z)^-3 eta(3z)^9 is a weight-3 form on Gamma0(3) WITH the quadratic character. The hypothesis-shaped multiplier_trivial_of_congr is therefore landed with ONE HYPOTHESIS ADDED, Even k, and the counterexample is the proof that the addition is load-bearing rather than defensive. THE EVEN-WEIGHT PACKAGE, which is the node's 'for k even this yields a term of ModularForm'. etaMultiplierHom_eq_one_of_le_four: for even k the character is trivial (the constant hom has the same three generator values). etaQuotientH_transform_of_le_four: f(gamma z) = (denom gamma z)^k f(z) on all of Gamma0(N). etaQuotientH_slash_of_le_four: slash invariance in Mathlib's own form, f |[k] g = f for every g in the image of Gamma0(N) in GL(2,R). mdiff_etaQuotientH: holomorphy in Mathlib's manifold sense (F31-B8 transported by UpperHalfPlane.mdifferentiable_iff). isBoundedAt_of_bdd_SL2Z: Ligozat condition (iii), taken as the node's hypothesis hbd in Mathlib's IsBoundedAtImInfty form, converted to boundedness at every cusp of Gamma0(N) via IsCusp.mono and OnePoint.isBoundedAt_iff_forall_SL2Z. etaQuotientModularForm: the term of ModularForm (Gamma0 N) k itself. WHY hbd IS A HYPOTHESIS AND NOT A LEMMA, stated so it cannot be mistaken for an oversight: converting the arithmetic predicate LigozatHolomorphic (nonnegativity of etaQuotientCuspOrder at every cusp) into boundedness requires knowing that etaQuotientCuspOrder IS the order of vanishing at a general cusp, which is exactly F31-OBSTRUCTED. Only the cusp infinity is available (F31-B13). The node scoped hbd as a hypothesis for that reason and it stays one. SCOPE AND WHAT IS STILL OPEN. Nothing here is proved for N >= 5. F32-B1's descent fails at N = 5 (descent_bound_fails_at_five is the recorded counterexample) and for general N the reduction of Gamma0(N) to three generators is FALSE. The Dedekind-sum obstruction (F32-OBSTRUCTED) is NOT overcome by this node; it is AVOIDED, for four levels, by replacing evaluation of the multiplier with generation of the group. No Dedekind sum, no eta multiplier system, and no Kronecker character chi(d) appears anywhere in the proof. LL-1 GUARDS, both landed and both in FinalCheck.lean. GUARD 1, agreement with Mathlib: ligozat_level_one_24_guard is the B2 route at N = 1, r = 24, k = 12, where the eta quotient IS Delta; the statement it produces is verbatim etaQuotientH_level_one_24_transform, which was proved from Mathlib's own discriminant_S_invariant / discriminant_T_invariant and shares no step with this block. GUARD 2, the honest negative: not_multiplier_trivial_odd, described above. FinalCheck also carries PIN 1 (the odd counterexample really satisfies both congruences with odd k, written longhand rather than through the predicates) and PIN 2 (the packaged object really is Mathlib's ModularForm at the image of Gamma0 N in GL(2,R), and its underlying function is definitionally the product prod_delta eta(delta z)^{r_delta}). DECLARATIONS LANDED, all sorry-free, all with axiom footprint [propext, Classical.choice, Quot.sound] (NO sorryAx), each guarded by '#guard_msgs in #print axioms' in FinalCheck.lean: gamma0GensSub, image_gamma0GensSub, gamma0Gens_eq_perm, closure_gamma0Gens_eq_of_hgen, closure_gamma0GensSub_eq_top_of_gen, closure_gamma0GensSub_eq_top, hom_ext_of_gen, hom_ext_of_le_four, etaMultiplierHom_neg_one, etaMultiplierHom_eq_of_gen, etaMultiplierHom_eq_of_le_four, ligozat_of_le_four, ligozat_of_le_four_pnat, etaMultiplierHom_eq_one_of_gen, etaMultiplierHom_eq_one_of_le_four, etaQuotientH_transform_of_gen, etaQuotientH_transform_of_le_four, multiplier_trivial_of_congr, etaQuotientH_slash_of_le_four, mdiff_etaQuotientH, Gamma0_map_le_SL, isBoundedAt_of_bdd_SL2Z, etaQuotientModularForm, etaQuotientModularForm_apply, ligozat_level_one_24_guard, ligozatOddExp_sum, ligozatOddExp_congr1, ligozatOddExp_congr2, ligozatOdd_hgen, etaMultiplierVal_ligozatOddExp_neg_one, not_multiplier_trivial_odd; plus the definition ligozatOddExp, which depends on no axioms at all. The FinalCheck tripwire that used to assert multiplier_trivial_of_congr still carried sorryAx was UPDATED, not deleted.", "lean_name": "SocrateAI.ModularForms.ligozat_of_le_four", "lean_file": "Lean/SocrateAI/ModularForms/EtaQuotientModularity.lean", "status": "proved", "depends_on": ["F32-A5", "F32-A6", "F32-A8", "F32-B1"], "paper_claim": null}
# --- F3.2-B3: the multiplier IS Ligozat's Kronecker character, for N <= 4.  B2 pinned the
# character by three generator values; B3 says which function of d = gamma_{11} it is.  Needs a
# Kronecker symbol, which Mathlib does not have (jacobiSym disagrees at the prime 2), and one
# reciprocity fact, (-3/p), proved elementarily rather than via Gauss sums. ---
{"id": "F32-B3", "kind": "math", "statement_nl": "HEADLINE multiplier_eq_kronecker_of_le_four. PROVED, sorry-free. THE MULTIPLIER IS LIGOZAT'S KRONECKER CHARACTER, FOR N <= 4. STATEMENT, verbatim as landed: for N : Nat with 0 < N and N <= 4, r : Nat -> Int, k : Int with sum over delta in N.divisors of r delta = 2*k, h1 : LigozatCongr1 N r, h2 : LigozatCongr2 N r, and every gamma : Gamma0 N: (etaMultiplierHom r hk gamma : C) = kroneckerSym (ligozatKroneckerNum N r k) (gamma 1 1), where ligozatKroneckerNum N r k = (-1)^|k| * prod over delta | N of delta^|r delta| and kroneckerSym is the Kronecker symbol. The transformation law in the literature's own shape is landed separately as ligozat_kronecker_transform_of_le_four: f(gamma z) = chi(d) * (c z + d)^k * f(z) for every gamma in Gamma0(N) and every z in H, with chi(d) the Kronecker symbol above. WHAT WAS PROVED, IN ENGLISH (LL-1). F32-B2 pinned the multiplier w by its three generator values w(T)=1, w(V)=1, w(-I)=(-1)^k and proved uniqueness; it never said what w is as a function of d = gamma_{11}. This node says it: w(gamma) = ((-1)^k prod delta^{r_delta} / d), the Kronecker symbol, which is exactly the character Ligozat's criterion attaches to the eta quotient. The proof is: both sides are homomorphisms Gamma0(N) -> Cx (the right-hand side because gamma |-> gamma_{11} mod N is Mathlib's own Gamma0Map and a MulChar on ZMod N pulls back along it), so B2's uniqueness applies once the value at -I matches; the work is the arithmetic that identifies the Kronecker symbol, level by level, with a Dirichlet character mod N. MATHLIB DOES NOT HAVE THE KRONECKER SYMBOL, AND jacobiSym IS NOT IT. Mathlib has jacobiSym a b for b : Nat, defined as the product of legendreSym p a over the prime factors of b. At p = 2 that is NOT the Kronecker convention: jacobiSym (-3) 2 = 1 whereas the Kronecker value (-3/2) = chi8(-3) = -1. This is load-bearing, not pedantic: Gamma0(3) contains matrices with EVEN d (for instance !![-1,-1;3,2], whose d is 2) and with NEGATIVE d (-I), so the honest statement needs the genuine Kronecker symbol. kroneckerPrime / kroneckerSym are landed as that symbol, built on Mathlib's legendreSym, ZMod.chi8 and Nat.primeFactorsList: at an odd prime kroneckerPrime a p IS legendreSym p a definitionally (pinned by rfl in FinalCheck), at p = 2 it is ZMod.chi8 a (also pinned by rfl), and kroneckerSym a d is the standard multiplicative extension (a/sign d) * prod over p | |d| of (a/p), with the classical convention (a/0) = 1 for a = +-1 and 0 otherwise. THE ONE PIECE OF RECIPROCITY, PROVED ELEMENTARILY. The only nontrivial evaluation needed is (-3/p) = chi_{-3}(p) for odd primes p != 3. It is NOT taken from Mathlib's quadratic reciprocity (that file sits behind the Gauss-sum / cyclotomic / Dedekind-domain cone, ~300 unbuilt modules in the shared pool). isSquare_neg_three_iff proves from scratch that -3 is a square mod p iff p = 1 mod 3: x^2 = -3 and z^2+z+1 = 0 are exchanged by z = (x-1)/2, and z^2+z+1 = 0 says exactly that z has order 3 in (Z/p)x, which happens iff 3 | p-1. The backward direction uses only that (Z/p)x is cyclic. THE LEVEL-BY-LEVEL ARITHMETIC, which is where N <= 4 is used a second time (the first is B1's generation). N = 1: congruence (i) forces 12 | k, so k is even, the numerator is 1 and the character is trivial. N = 2: (i)+(ii) force 4 | k and r_2 even, so the numerator is a perfect square coprime to the odd d and the character is trivial. N = 3: (i) with the weight relation gives 12 | k + r_3, so r_3 = k mod 2; for even k the numerator is 3^{even}, a square, and the character is trivial, and for ODD k it is -3 times a square and the character is (-3/.), the quadratic character mod 3. N = 4: both congruences force every r_delta even, so the numerator is +-(square) with d odd: trivial for even k, and (-1/.) = chi4 for odd k. THE |r_delta| CONVENTION IS NOT A WEAKENING, AND THIS IS PROVED. Ligozat's numerator (-1)^k prod delta^{r_delta} is a RATIONAL number when some r_delta < 0, and a Kronecker symbol takes an integer numerator; ligozatKroneckerNum therefore uses |k| and |r_delta|. kroneckerSym_ligozat_eq_prod and multiplier_eq_ligozat_character_of_le_four prove that this changes nothing, by landing the result in Ligozat's own completely-multiplicative form with GENUINE INTEGER exponents: w(gamma) = (-1/d)^k * prod over delta | N of (delta/d)^{r_delta} (zpow), valid because the symbol takes values +-1 on arguments coprime to d and +-1 is its own inverse. TWO VALIDATIONS, BOTH LANDED AS THEOREMS (LL-1). VALIDATION 1, the node's own example: ligozat_level_four_weight_five proves that for eta(z)^4 eta(2z)^2 eta(4z)^4 -- level 4, weight 5, both congruences holding with sum delta r_delta = sum (4/delta) r_delta = 24 -- the character produced is literally kroneckerSym (-4), i.e. (-4/d), which is the character the literature attaches to this form. VALIDATION 2, odd weight WITH A NEGATIVE EXPONENT: ligozat_level_three_weight_three proves that for eta(z)^{-3} eta(3z)^9 -- the same level-3 example F32-B2 used to show the multiplier is not trivial -- the character is kroneckerSym (-3), the classical nebentypus chi_{-3}. B2 could only say 'not 1'; B3 says which character. SCOPE AND WHAT IS STILL OPEN. Nothing here is proved for N >= 5. The N <= 4 hypothesis is used twice: through B1 for generation, and in the finite case analysis above. The Dedekind-sum obstruction (F32-OBSTRUCTED) is NOT overcome; it is still avoided, for four levels. No Dedekind sum and no eta multiplier system appears anywhere in the proof. DECLARATIONS LANDED, all sorry-free, all with axiom footprint [propext, Classical.choice, Quot.sound] (NO sorryAx), each guarded by '#guard_msgs in #print axioms' in FinalCheck.lean: natCast_ne_zero_of_ne, cube_root_of_isSquare_neg_three, isSquare_neg_three_of_mod, isSquare_neg_three_iff, kroneckerPrime, kroneckerSym, kroneckerPrime_mul, kroneckerPrime_one, kroneckerPrime_trichotomy, kroneckerPrime_ne_zero, kroneckerPrime_sq, kroneckerSym_one_left, kroneckerSym_mul_left, kroneckerSym_sq_of_gcd, prod_map_mulChar, kroneckerSym_eq_mulChar, legendreSym_neg_three, kroneckerSym_neg_one, kroneckerSym_neg_three, kroneckerSym_neg_four, charGamma0, charGamma0_apply, coe_T_one_one, matV_one_one, neg_one_one_one, multiplier_eq_intChar_of_le_four, ligozatKroneckerNum, gamma0_not_dvd, gcd_pow_of_not_dvd, mulChar_one_apply_of_isUnit, isUnit_gamma0_entry, multiplier_eq_kronecker_one, multiplier_eq_kronecker_two, multiplier_eq_kronecker_three, multiplier_eq_kronecker_four, multiplier_eq_kronecker_of_le_four, ligozatFourFive, ligozatFourFive_sum, ligozatFourFive_congr1, ligozatFourFive_congr2, ligozatFourFive_num, ligozat_level_four_weight_five, kroneckerSym_trichotomy, kroneckerSym_ne_zero_of_gcd, kroneckerSym_pow_left, kroneckerSym_prod_left, zpow_eq_pow_natAbs, kroneckerSym_ligozat_eq_prod, gamma0_gcd_eq_one, multiplier_eq_ligozat_character_of_le_four, ligozatOddExp_num, ligozat_level_three_weight_three, ligozat_kronecker_transform_of_le_four. FinalCheck also carries six STATEMENT pins: PIN 1 (kroneckerPrime a 2 = ZMod.chi8 a, by rfl -- the Kronecker convention at 2, not the Jacobi one), PIN 2 (kroneckerPrime a 5 = legendreSym 5 a, by rfl), PIN 3 (the classical table of (-3/.) at d = -1, 2, 5, 7, including the two denominators a Jacobi symbol cannot see), PIN 4 (the table of (-4/.) = chi4 at d = -1, 3, 5), PIN 5 (the level-4 exponent vector satisfies both congruences, longhand, with k = 5 ODD), PIN 6 (the two numerators -1024 = (-4)*16^2 and -19683 = (-3)*81^2, longhand). FILE NOTE: the scoping message named EtaQuotient.lean, which is the ARITHMETIC layer and by design imports only Nat.divisors / Nat.totient (no eta, no upper half-plane, no Gamma0). B3 is about a character of Gamma0(N) and therefore landed in Lean/SocrateAI/ModularForms/EtaQuotientModularity.lean, next to etaMultiplierHom and the B2 block it builds on; one new Mathlib import, Mathlib.NumberTheory.LegendreSymbol.Basic, was added there.", "lean_name": "SocrateAI.ModularForms.multiplier_eq_kronecker_of_le_four", "lean_file": "Lean/SocrateAI/ModularForms/EtaQuotientModularity.lean", "status": "proved", "depends_on": ["F32-B2"], "paper_claim": null}
{"id": "F32-C1", "kind": "math", "statement_nl": "HEADLINE abs_eta_smul. PROVED, sorry-free. STATEMENT, verbatim as landed: for every gamma : SL(2,Z) and every z : H, ‖ModularForm.eta ((gamma . z : H) : C)‖ = Real.sqrt ‖denom (gamma : GL (Fin 2) R) (z : C)‖ * ‖ModularForm.eta (z : C)‖. In words: the MODULUS of the Dedekind eta transformation, for the WHOLE modular group, with no multiplier, no congruence condition, no character and no choice of generators. Classically eta(gamma z) = eps(gamma) (cz+d)^{1/2} eta(z) where eps(gamma) is a 24th root of unity whose closed form is exactly where DEDEKIND SUMS enter, and Mathlib has none (greps for DedekindSum, dedekindSum, etaMultiplier return zero files at commit 905b95818e). Taking absolute values deletes eps (it has modulus 1) and deletes the branch ambiguity of the square root (the two branches differ by a sign), so nothing Dedekind-valued is needed. PROOF, and it is NOT Subgroup.closure_induction over the S,T generators: raise to the 24th power FIRST, where the multiplier is already gone, because eta^24 = Delta is Mathlib's ModularForm.discriminant, modular of weight 12 for the FULL modular group (CuspForm.discriminant, built from discriminant_S_invariant and discriminant_T_invariant). The delta = 1 case of F3.2-A4's eta_pow24_natScale_smul is verbatim eta(gamma z)^24 = (cz+d)^12 eta(z)^24; norm_mul and norm_pow turn that into |eta(gamma z)|^24 = |cz+d|^12 |eta(z)|^24; Real.sq_sqrt evaluates (sqrt|cz+d|)^24 = |cz+d|^12; and pow_left_inj₀ (x -> x^24 is injective on [0, infinity)) concludes, both sides being norms. Mathlib's eta_comp_eq_csqrt_I_inv is used only through Mathlib's own discriminant_S_invariant; we did not reprove the S-transformation. Three named lemmas, no new machinery (LL-11). SCOPE, so it cannot be misread (LL-1): this is a statement about a NONNEGATIVE REAL. It does NOT determine eta(gamma z) as a complex number; the phase eps(gamma) is precisely the information the norm discards, and pinning it down for a general gamma in Gamma0(N) remains F3.2-OBSTRUCTED. What it unlocks is every question that sees only |f| -- growth, vanishing orders, log|f| -- i.e. the cusp-order analysis. COMPANIONS LANDED IN THE SAME BLOCK: norm_etaMultiplierVal (the F3.2-A5 character has modulus 1, since w^24 = 1 and the only nonnegative real 24th root of 1 is 1) and norm_etaQuotientH_smul (‖f(gamma z)‖ = ‖denom gamma z‖^k ‖f(z)‖ for every gamma in Gamma0(N) and every exponent vector of even weight-sum -- the multiplier-free modulus law for the eta quotient itself, which is the form the cusp-order analysis consumes). LL-1 GUARD, two independent routes to one proposition: norm_eta_T_smul specialises abs_eta_smul to gamma = T (Delta route, via denom_T) and norm_eta_add_one derives |eta(z+1)| = |eta(z)| from F3.1-B2's eta_add_one (q-product route, |exp(2 pi i/24)| = 1 by Complex.norm_exp_ofReal_mul_I); abs_eta_smul_T_guard asserts the two agree. The routes share no step. Five STATEMENT PINS in FinalCheck.lean: denom is c z + d longhand; the automorphy exponent is one HALF (pinned by squaring: |eta(gamma z)|^2 = |cz+d| |eta(z)|^2); the S-instance in classical coordinates |eta(-1/z)| = sqrt|z| |eta(z)|; the T cross-check; and the corollary at N=1, r = 24, k = 12 reading ‖denom‖^12. AXIOM FOOTPRINT: [propext, Classical.choice, Quot.sound] for all six declarations -- no sorryAx. DEPENDENCY NOTE, recorded because it differs from the scoped plan: the node was scoped 'built from F32-A1' on the expectation of a Subgroup.closure_induction over the S,T generators. That is NOT what was needed. F32-A1 (eta_T_transform) is NOT used by abs_eta_smul at all. The real parents are F32-A4 (eta_pow24_natScale_smul, the Delta-modularity of a dilated eta factor) for the main theorem, F32-A5 (etaMultiplierVal / etaQuotientH_transform) for the norm_etaQuotientH_smul corollary, and F31-B2 (eta_add_one) for the independent T-route of the LL-1 guard.", "lean_name": "SocrateAI.ModularForms.abs_eta_smul", "lean_file": "Lean/SocrateAI/ModularForms/EtaQuotientModularity.lean", "status": "proved", "depends_on": ["F32-A4", "F32-A5", "F31-B2"], "paper_claim": null}
{"id": "F32-C2", "kind": "math", "statement_nl": "HEADLINE etaQuotient_cusp_order. PROVED, sorry-free. STATEMENT, verbatim as landed: for every N : N, every r : N -> Z with sum_{delta | N} r delta = 2*k, and EVERY gamma : SL(2,Z), (fun z : H => ‖(etaQuotientH N r ∣[k] (gamma : GL (Fin 2) R)) z‖) =Theta[UpperHalfPlane.atImInfty] (fun z : H => Real.exp (-2 * pi * (etaQuotientRawOrder N r (gamma 1 0) : R) * z.im)), where etaQuotientRawOrder N r c = (1/24) * sum_{delta | N} gcd(c,delta)^2 * r delta / delta. In words: Ligozat's cusp-order formula as a two-sided asymptotic for |f | gamma| at i-infinity, at EVERY cusp, for the whole modular group -- no congruence condition, no Gamma0(N)-membership, no character, no generators. SCOPE CORRECTION, LOUD (LL-1): the node was scoped with the exponent written as ligozatOrder = (N / (24 * gcd(c^2,N))) * sum gcd(c,delta)^2 r delta / delta, i.e. WITH the cusp-width factor h = N/gcd(c^2,N). THAT STATEMENT IS FALSE and was not proved. Ligozat's etaQuotientCuspOrder is an order in the LOCAL uniformiser q_h = exp(2 pi i z / h), so a decay statement in Im z carries the exponent ord_Ligozat / h. The bridge is proved: etaQuotientCuspOrder_eq_width_mul_raw : for d | N, etaQuotientCuspOrder N r d = (N / gcd(d^2,N)) * etaQuotientRawOrder N r d. etaQuotient_cusp_order_ligozat restates the headline with the exponent spelled ord_Ligozat / h so the correction is visible in the statement. Ligozat's condition (iii) is unaffected: h > 0, so ordRaw >= 0 iff ord_Ligozat >= 0 (etaQuotientRawOrder_nonneg_iff). A hand-computed pin: for N=2, f = (eta(z)eta(2z))^12, cusp 0, |f | [12] S| ~ exp(-3 pi y / 2), so ordRaw = 3/4 while Ligozat's number is 3/2 and the width is 2 (rawOrder_level_two_twelve_pin, and FinalCheck PIN 3 asserts the two numbers DIFFER). PROOF, and it does NOT touch the eta multiplier system (F3.2-OBSTRUCTED is side-stepped, not circumvented, because a Theta-statement sees only |f| and the multiplier has modulus 1). (1) HERMITE NORMAL FORM, namespace Smith: for delta | N and gamma = (a,b;c,d), the integral matrix delta*gamma = (delta a, delta b; c, d) of determinant delta factors EXPLICITLY as gamma_delta * A_delta with gamma_delta = (P,-V;S,U) in SL(2,Z) and A_delta = (A,E;0,D) upper triangular, A = gcd(delta,c), D = delta/A. The Bezout data is built from Int.gcdA/gcdB for the pairs (delta,c) and (a,c), the latter coprime because det gamma = 1; bezout_raw : delta*a*U + c*V = A. Four linear_combination identities over Z (S*A = c, P*A = delta*a, S*E + U*D = d, P*E - V*D = delta*b) give, on H, delta*(gamma z) = gamma_delta * w_delta(z) with w_delta(z) = (A z + E)/D (coe_gam_smul_hpt) and denom gamma_delta (w_delta z) = (cz+d)/D (denom_gam_hpt). No choice principle: everything is a definition. (2) F3.2-C1 IN MODULUS: abs_eta_smul at gamma_delta and w_delta gives ‖eta(delta*(gamma z))‖ = sqrt(‖cz+d‖/D) * ‖eta(w_delta z)‖ (Smith.norm_eta_natMul_smul). (3) AN EXACT IDENTITY, not an estimate (norm_etaQuotientH_smul_eq): taking the product over delta | N with exponents r_delta, the sqrt‖cz+d‖ factors collect into ‖cz+d‖^{(sum r)/2} = ‖cz+d‖^k -- this is exactly where the hypothesis sum r = 2k is consumed -- and cancel against the ‖denom‖^{-k} of the slash, leaving ‖(f | [k] gamma)(z)‖ = C(gamma) * exp(-2 pi * ordRaw * Im z) * prod_delta ‖tail_delta(z)‖^{r_delta}, with C(gamma) = prod (sqrt D_delta)^{-r_delta} nonzero. The exponent comes from Im w_delta = (A_delta/D_delta) Im z together with the arithmetic identity A_delta/D_delta = gcd(c,delta)^2/delta (Smith.A_div_D_eq). (4) ONE LIMIT: Im w_delta -> infinity along atImInfty since A/D > 0, so each tail tends to 1 by F3.1-B12's tendsto_tprod_one_sub_eta_q_natCast_mul (tendsto_cuspTail); isTheta_mul_of_tendsto converts u -> C /= 0 into u*g =Theta g. WHY NO APPROACH REGION IS NEEDED, and this was the scoped difficulty: atImInfty leaves Re z unrestricted, and individually neither ‖eta(delta gamma z)‖ nor ‖cz+d‖^{-k} is Theta of a pure exponential there -- each carries a Re z-dependent factor. They cancel EXACTLY, at the level of an identity, because the sqrt‖cz+d‖ of step (2) appears once per unit of r_delta and sum r_delta = 2k. Nothing is estimated before step (4). So no Smith-style approach region, no uniform tail bound written by hand, and no Dedekind sum. GUARDS. (a) cusp_order_infty_guard: the cusp infinity by two routes sharing no step -- route A is this theorem at gamma = 1 (Hermite + abs_eta_smul + Delta), route B is norm_etaQuotientH_isTheta_infty, which never leaves the q-product (F3.1-B12 gives f/q^{ord} -> 1 and ‖q^{ord}‖ = exp(-2 pi ord Im z)); the exponents are identified by etaQuotientRawOrder_infty, gcd(0,delta) = delta. (b) EXTERNAL PIN exp_isBigO_discriminant_of_cusp_order: at N=1, r == 24, k = 12 the eta quotient IS Mathlib's Delta and this theorem returns ordRaw = 1, i.e. ‖Delta(z)‖ =Theta exp(-2 pi Im z); its =O half is Mathlib's own ModularForm.exp_isBigO_discriminant, proved there by a different argument, so the 2 pi, the 24 and the gcd^2 are pinned against an authority outside this development. (c) rawOrder_level_two_twelve_pin, the hand-computed N=2 example. Six STATEMENT PINS in FinalCheck.lean: the definition of ordRaw longhand (rfl); the slash convention (f | [k] gamma) z = f(gamma z) denom^{-k}; the honesty pin that ordRaw /= ord_Ligozat at N=2; the width bridge; the headline in longhand (filter, Theta, -2 pi, z.im); and both directions of the Mathlib discriminant pin. SCOPE, so it cannot be over-read: this is about ‖f | gamma‖, a nonnegative real. It does NOT produce the eta multiplier, does not give Ligozat's character chi, and does not by itself prove holomorphy at the cusps. What it delivers is condition (iii) in analytic form. F3.2-OBSTRUCTED is untouched.", "lean_name": "SocrateAI.ModularForms.etaQuotient_cusp_order", "lean_file": "Lean/SocrateAI/ModularForms/EtaQuotientCuspTheta.lean", "status": "proved", "depends_on": ["F32-C1"], "paper_claim": null}
# --- F3.2-C3: Ligozat at the genus-zero primes p = 5, 7, 13.  Generation of Gamma0(p) by
# {-I, T, V} plus explicit ELLIPTIC elements (coset enumeration against P^1(F_p)), and the
# multiplier evaluated on every generator, the elliptic ones by F3.2-A9's fixed-point trick. ---
{"id": "F32-C3", "kind": "math", "statement_nl": "HEADLINE Gamma0_prime_generated (generation) and ligozat_of_prime5 / _p7 / _p13 (the multiplier). PROVED, sorry-free. STATEMENT, verbatim as landed: for p in ({5,7,13} : Finset N), Subgroup.closure (gamma0GensPrime p) = Gamma0 p, where gamma0GensPrime 5 = {-1, T, matV 5, matH 2 2, matH 3 3}, gamma0GensPrime 7 = {-1, T, matV 7, matH 2 3, matH 4 5}, and gamma0GensPrime 13 = {-1, T, matV 13, matH 3 4, matH 5 5, matH 8 8, matH 9 10}, with matH j j' := !![-j', -1; j*j'+1, j]. The node's '{-1,T,V} union elliptic' shape is landed separately as gamma0GensP5_eq_union / P7 / P13. TWO DEVIATIONS FROM THE SCOPED STATEMENT, both stated loudly. (1) The scoped right-hand side was '(Gamma0 p).toSubgroup'; Mathlib's Gamma0 p IS a Subgroup SL(2,Z), so there is no .toSubgroup and the landed equality is between two Subgroup SL(2,Z). FinalCheck PIN 3 re-pins the right-hand side as the raw condition (5 : Z) | g 1 0. (2) The 'explicit elliptic elements' are named: they are the Schreier generators matH j j' whose trace j - j' is 0 or -1; elliptic_traces proves all eight traces. WHAT WAS PROVED, IN ENGLISH (LL-1). (A) GENERATION. For each of p = 5, 7, 13 the subgroup of SL(2,Z) generated by -I, T = !![1,1;0,1], V = !![1,0;-p,1] and an explicit finite list of ELLIPTIC matrices (two for p=5, two for p=7, four for p=13) is EXACTLY Gamma0(p). Both inclusions are proved. (B) THE MULTIPLIER ON THOSE GENERATORS. Under Ligozat's congruences (i) and (ii), the character w of F3.2-A5 takes the values w(T) = 1 (A6), w(V) = 1 (A8), w(-I) = (-1)^k (A9), w(e) = i^{-k} on each trace-0 elliptic generator and w(e) = omega^{-k}, omega = (-1 + sqrt 3 i)/2, on each trace -1 one (A9 at the fixed point). Since the listed elements generate, w is THE unique character with those values: etaMultiplierHom_eq_of_p5 / _p7 / _p13, and the transformation law f(gamma z) = w(gamma) (cz+d)^k f(z) holds on ALL of Gamma0(p): ligozat_of_prime5 / _p7 / _p13.  A single uniform corollary over the Finset {5,7,13}, in the node's own phrasing, is landed as ligozat_of_prime: under (i), (ii) and 12 | k the eta quotient transforms with TRIVIAL multiplier on all of Gamma0(p) for every p in {5,7,13} (12 is divisible by each of the three sharp thresholds 4, 6, 12; the per-prime statements keep the sharp one). (C) TRIVIAL MULTIPLIER. etaQuotientH_transform_p5 / _p7 / _p13: f(gamma z) = (cz+d)^k f(z) on all of Gamma0(p) provided 4 | k (p=5), 6 | k (p=7), 12 | k (p=13). THE PROOF, and why it is not B1's descent. B1's Euclidean descent provably stops at N = 5 (descent_bound_fails_at_five) and CANNOT be repaired, because Gamma0(5) is genuinely not generated by {-I, T, V}: Gamma0bar(5) = Z/2 * Z/2 * Z. The route landed here is COSET ENUMERATION. subgroup_eq_of_transversal is an elementary criterion proved from Subgroup.closure alone: if closure X = top, H <= K, 1 in R, R meet K = {1}, and for every r in R and x in X there are r', r'' in R with r x r'^{-1} in H and r x^{-1} r''^{-1} in H, then H = K. (The predicate 'g r^{-1} in H for some r in R' is carried across closure X = top by the subgroup {g : forall u, P u -> P (u g) and P (u g^{-1})}.) Gamma0_eq_of_schreier instantiates it with X = {S, T} (Mathlib's SpecialLinearGroup.SL2Z_generators) and the transversal R = {1} union {S T^j : 0 <= j < p}, whose p+1 classes are P^1(F_p). PRIMALITY IS SPENT EXACTLY ONCE: in the case r = S T^j, x = S, where S T^j S (S T^{j'})^{-1} = matH j j' needs j' = -j^{-1} mod p to exist. Every other case is a one-line identity: r = S T^{p-1}, x = T gives S T^p S^{-1} = matV p (matV_eq_conj); r = S, x = T^{-1} gives (matV p)^{-1}; x = S^{-1} is x = S times the central -I (mul_S_inv_mul); the rest are 1. So the ONLY per-prime input is a word in the generators for each matH j j', j = 1..p-1, and those words are short and uniform: matH 1 (p-1) = T^{-1} V^{-1}, matH (p-1) 1 = (-I) V T, matH j' j = (-I) (matH j j')^{-1}, and at p = 13 two products of two elliptic generators. Each is a single 'decide' on 2x2 integer matrices. THE ELLIPTIC FIXED POINTS, uniformly and without Dedekind sums. matH_smul_tauEll: if zeta is a root of the characteristic polynomial X^2 - (j - j')X + 1 of matH j j' with Im zeta > 0 and j j' + 1 > 0, then tau0 = (zeta - j)/(j j' + 1) lies in H, is fixed by matH j j', and denom (matH j j') tau0 = zeta (denom_matH_tauEll). Only two roots occur: zeta = i for trace 0 and zeta = omega for trace -1. F3.2-A9's etaMultiplierVal_of_fixed then returns w = zeta^{-k} with no further analysis. MATHLIB INPUTS ACTUALLY USED (LL-11). SpecialLinearGroup.SL2Z_generators (closure {S,T} = top), ModularGroup.S_inv / coe_S / coe_T_zpow, Subgroup.map_subtype_inj + MonoidHom.map_closure + Subgroup.range_subtype (transport of generation into the subtype), MonoidHom.eq_of_eqOn_dense (uniqueness), Complex.div_ofReal_im (the fixed point is in H). Mathlib's Subgroup.closure_mul_image_eq_top (Schreier's lemma, GroupTheory/Schreier.lean) EXISTS and was deliberately NOT used: it is phrased through IsComplement and the transversal function, both of which would have to be computed; the bespoke criterion is 45 lines and needs neither. SCOPE - READ BEFORE CITING. (1) The multiplier is NOT identified with Ligozat's Kronecker character chi(d). That is the F3.2-B3 analogue at these levels and it is not attempted; what is delivered is the character's value on a generating set, hence by uniqueness on the whole group, but not a closed formula in d = gamma_{11}. (2) Ligozat condition (iii), holomorphy at the cusps, is untouched at these levels (F3.1-OBSTRUCTED, F3.2-C2). (3) The divisibility hypotheses of (C) are NOT consequences of (i) and (ii). not_multiplier_trivial_p5 is the proof: at p = 5, r_1 = 5, r_5 = -1, k = 2, both congruences hold and k is EVEN, generation is a theorem, and the trivial-multiplier law FAILS at the elliptic generator because w = i^{-2} = -1. This is the level-5 analogue of B2's not_multiplier_trivial_odd, and it is why the statement carries 4 | k rather than Even k. (4) It is NOT proved here that the elliptic generators are NECESSARY, i.e. that {-I,T,V} generates a proper subgroup of Gamma0(5); only that this proof needs them (see the negative control below) and that B1's descent provably fails. (5) F3.2-OBSTRUCTED is AVOIDED, not overcome: for three more levels, evaluation of the general multiplier is replaced by generation plus A9. Nothing here says anything about a general N. NEGATIVE CONTROL, run and read. The entire p = 5 block was re-run verbatim with the generating set cut down to gamma0Gens 5 = {-1, T, matV 5}. It fails at exactly two goals, j = 2 and j = 3 - the two elliptic Schreier generators - and at no other step. The elliptic elements are therefore load-bearing, not decorative. GUARDS. GUARD 1, two independent routes to one proposition: closure_gamma0Gens_three_schreier proves closure (gamma0Gens 3) = Gamma0 3 by coset enumeration, and gamma0Gens_three_two_routes asserts it alongside B1's closure_gamma0Gens_eq, which proves the same statement by Euclidean descent; the two share no step. closure_gamma0Gens_two_schreier does the same at N = 2. GUARD 2, properness: S_not_mem_closure_gensP5 and closure_gamma0GensP5_ne_top - the closure is a PROPER subgroup, so the theorem has not degenerated into 'closure = top'. GUARD 3, the honest negative: not_multiplier_trivial_p5, above. GUARD 4: elliptic_traces - all eight extra generators really are elliptic (trace 0 or -1), so A9 applies to them. GUARD 5, non-vacuity: etaMultiplierHom_satisfies_p5 and _p13 - the generator-value hypotheses of the headline are simultaneously satisfiable, etaMultiplierHom itself satisfying them; without this the headline could be vacuously true. Plus testGamma0Five_mem_closure, a concrete non-generator of Gamma0(5) exhibited as a member. TEN STATEMENT PINS in FinalCheck.lean (section F32C3Pin): matH entrywise; the transversal longhand; the right-hand side as (5 : Z) | g 1 0; the '{-1,T,V} union elliptic' shape; the fixed point (i-2)/5 and its automorphy factor i (not -i) at p = 5; omega longhand plus omega^2 + omega + 1 = 0; the p = 5 headline longhand; the honesty pin that (i)+(ii)+Even k hold for the counterexample; the three divisibility thresholds 4, 6, 12 level by level so they cannot be transposed; and the uniform ligozat_of_prime quantified over the Finset. AXIOM FOOTPRINT [propext, Classical.choice, Quot.sound], NO sorryAx, for all forty-one declarations guarded by '#guard_msgs in #print axioms' in FinalCheck.lean. The guard was negative-controlled: adding sorryAx to one expected list makes the build fail. FILE PLACEMENT, a deviation from the brief: the brief said EtaQuotient.lean, which has a deliberately restricted import cone (Nat.divisors + Nat.totient only) and contains no sorry. The block was landed in the new module Lean/SocrateAI/ModularForms/EtaQuotientPrimeLevel.lean, importing EtaQuotientModularity, and wired into both SocrateAI.lean and FinalCheck.lean. Final line of lake build: 'Build completed successfully (3482 jobs).'", "lean_name": "SocrateAI.ModularForms.Gamma0_prime_generated", "lean_file": "Lean/SocrateAI/ModularForms/EtaQuotientPrimeLevel.lean", "status": "proved", "depends_on": ["F32-A5", "F32-A6", "F32-A8", "F32-A9", "F32-B1"], "paper_claim": null}
# Run 4 (2026-09-07) -- Dedekind sums, Apostol's Phi / Rademacher's Psi, the eta multiplier.
