{"id": "DRK-00", "kind": "math", "lean_name": "SocrateAI.NumberTheory.dedekindSum_five_pin", "lean_file": "Lean/SocrateAI/NumberTheory/DedekindSum.lean", "status": "proved", "depends_on": [], "paper_claim": null, "statement_nl": "PROVED, sorry-free. SIGN DISCIPLINE GATE (LL-22) for run 4. Numeric pins, computed by kernel evaluation of the definitions ALONE (no lemma of DRK-01 or DRK-03 has been stated at the point in the files where the pins sit), placed before any general sign, floor or reciprocity proof. WHAT IS PINNED. (a) Sixteen values of dedekindSum in Lean/SocrateAI/NumberTheory/DedekindSum.lean: s(1,5)=1/5, s(2,5)=0, s(1,7)=5/14, s(3,7)=-1/14, s(1,13)=11/13, s(4,13)=-1/13, s(1,12)=55/72, s(5,12)=-1/72, s(4,12)=1/18, the NEGATIVE-h values s(-1,5)=-1/5, s(-3,7)=1/14, s(-5,12)=1/72, and the degenerate s(1,0)=s(1,1)=s(0,5)=0. (b) Three instances of reciprocity, at the coprime pairs (5,12), (3,7), (1,5), checked BEFORE the general theorem DRK-02, plus a NEGATIVE CONTROL at the non-coprime pair (4,12) proving reciprocity FAILS there, so DRK-02's coprimality hypothesis is load-bearing and not decorative. (c) In Lean/SocrateAI/NumberTheory/RademacherPhi.lean: Phi on !![1,0;1,1] (=2), on ModularGroup.S (=0), on ModularGroup.T (=1), on three matrices where the Dedekind sum does real work including c<0, on T^3 and T^-2 (=3 and -2, pinned before rademacherPhi_T_zpow), and Phi(-g)=Phi(g) at SIX explicit g covering c=0, c>0 and c<0, pinned before rademacherPhi_neg. (d) LL-22 TRIPWIRES: Phi and Psi are pinned as DIFFERENT NUMBERS on three matrices and as EQUAL on exactly S and T (where sign(c(a+d))=0), and Phi is pinned as different from s(d,c); a later confusion of Apostol's Phi with the Rademacher symbol Psi therefore fails the build rather than propagating. (e) Four instances of the DRK-04 descent step, before DRK-04. DEVIATION FROM THE BRIEF, STATED LOUDLY (LL-1), TWO OF THEM. (1) TACTIC. The brief specified 'by decide'. Plain decide DOES NOT WORK: the kernel gets stuck reducing Rat.num of a Finset fold through Int.fract, and Mathlib at our rev has no norm_num extension for Int.floor (Mathlib/Tactic/NormNum/Floor.lean does not exist). Every pin uses 'decide +kernel' instead. That is still kernel evaluation and adds NO axiom: dedekindSum_five_pin and rademacherPhi_S_pin are guarded in FinalCheck.lean with footprint [propext, Classical.choice, Quot.sound]; had native_decide been used, Lean.ofReduceBool would appear and the guard would fail. (2) VALUES. FOUR of the pin values the brief supplied are FALSE for the brief's own definition of dedekindSum: the brief said s(1,5)=2/5, s(1,7)=5/7, s(3,7)=-1/7, s(-1,5)=-2/5; the true values are 1/5, 5/14, -1/14, -1/5, recomputed independently in Python with fractions.Fraction and then again by the Lean kernel (s(1,5)=1/5 agrees with the classical s(1,k)=(k-1)(k-2)/(12k)). The brief's other pins (s(2,5)=0, s(1,12)=55/72, s(5,12)=-1/72) are correct and kept verbatim. A FIFTH wrong value, s(4,12)=0, was invented while writing the file and was caught by the same gate; the true value is 1/18. The gate caught five wrong values, which is what it is for. ALSO NOT AS BRIEFED: the brief wrote the -I invariance as a single quantified example over all gamma, which is a THEOREM (DRK-03's rademacherPhi_neg, still open) and cannot be a decide-pin; it is landed as six explicit instances, as the brief's own trailing comment 'pinned at 6 explicit gamma by decide' asks. UPDATE 2026-09-07: six of the pins are now NAMED, AXIOM-GUARDED theorems rather than anonymous examples -- dedekindSum_five_pin (positive h, prime k), dedekindSum_neg_three_seven_pin (NEGATIVE h), dedekindSum_four_twelve_pin (composite k, where the gcd>1 summands are killed by the if-branch of dedekindSaw), dedekindSum_one_one_pin (degenerate k), dedekindSum_reciprocity_five_twelve_pin (one coprime reciprocity instance) and dedekindSum_reciprocity_fails_four_twelve (the non-coprime NEGATIVE CONTROL) -- each with a #print axioms guard in FinalCheck.lean showing [propext, Classical.choice, Quot.sound] and no Lean.ofReduceBool. An example already fails the build if its value is wrong, but an example has no name and so cannot carry an axiom guard; the brief asked for the pins AS GUARDED LEMMAS and now they are. All fifteen dedekindSum values, the three reciprocity instances and the negative control were independently recomputed in Python fractions.Fraction on 2026-09-07: 0 mismatches."}
{"id": "DRK-01", "kind": "def", "lean_name": "SocrateAI.NumberTheory.dedekindSum", "lean_file": "Lean/SocrateAI/NumberTheory/DedekindSum.lean", "status": "proved", "depends_on": ["DRK-00"], "paper_claim": null, "statement_nl": "PROVED, sorry-free. THIS IS A PORT, NOT A DERIVATION -- see ATTRIBUTION.md section 1. The sawtooth dedekindSaw x = (if Int.fract x = 0 then 0 else Int.fract x - 1/2) and the Dedekind sum dedekindSum h k = sum over r in Finset.range k of dedekindSaw (r/k) * dedekindSaw (h*r/k), together with NINETEEN supporting lemmas: dedekindSaw_of_fract_eq_zero, dedekindSaw_of_fract_ne_zero, dedekindSaw_intCast, dedekindSaw_natCast, dedekindSaw_zero, dedekindSaw_one, dedekindSaw_add_intCast, dedekindSaw_intCast_add, dedekindSaw_add_natCast, dedekindSaw_neg, abs_dedekindSaw_lt_half, dedekindSaw_half, dedekindSaw_natCast_div, dedekindSum_zero_right, dedekindSum_one_right, dedekindSum_zero_left, dedekindSum_neg, dedekindSum_add_mul, dedekindSum_eq_sum_Ico. In English: the sawtooth is odd, is bounded by 1/2 in absolute value, is 1-periodic and vanishes on the integers; the Dedekind sum is odd in h, depends on h only mod k, vanishes for k in {0,1} and for h = 0, and equals the Ico-form sum. PROVENANCE. Ported from anthropics/fermats-last-theorem, Definitions/Def_NumberTheory_DedekindSum.lean (Apache-2.0, fetched 2026-09-07, HTTP 200, 4731 bytes; the upstream file carries NO copyright header and is NOT listed in FLT's own ATTRIBUTION.md, so FLT does not identify it as third-party material). EXTENT, CHECKED MECHANICALLY AND NOT BY EYE: each upstream def/theorem block was extracted and compared character-for-character against ours -- 21 of 21 upstream declarations are BYTE-IDENTICAL, 0 differ, 0 missing. The only changes are ORDERING (def dedekindSum hoisted above the dedekindSaw lemma block so the DRK-00 gate can sit between the definitions and the theory they guard), a namespace SocrateAI.NumberTheory wrapper, and docstrings. No proof text was altered. WHY PORT AND NOT DEPEND: FLT pins toolchain v4.33.1 / Mathlib rev db584cd6, we pin v4.32.2 / 905b95818e; a second Mathlib checkout does not fit on disk and adding FLT as a Lake dependency would force a toolchain upgrade across the library. The upstream file is plain Lean over Mathlib primitives, needs none of FLT's P2M infrastructure, and typechecks verbatim at our rev -- which is why THIS one is a port and DRK-02, DRK-04, DRK-06 are not. CORRECTION TO THE BRIEF, AND A RETRACTION OF AN EARLIER CORRECTION (LL-1). The brief says 'the 17 supporting lemmas' and then enumerates nineteen names; nineteen is right and the error is in the NUMBER WORD ONLY. An earlier revision of this node and of the file header explained the gap by saying dedekindSaw_half is one the brief's list omits -- THAT WAS FALSE and is retracted: the brief lists dedekindSaw_half seventh. A set comparison of the brief's nineteen names against the nineteen ^theorem names in the freshly fetched upstream file is empty in both directions, so nothing was dropped from the port and nothing was invented for it. LL-22: dedekindSum is Apostol's s(h,k). It is NOT Apostol's Phi and NOT Rademacher's Psi. GUARDS: ALL 21 ported declarations now carry a FinalCheck axiom guard, and so do the six named DRK-00 pin theorems (was eight; the remaining thirteen were added 2026-09-07 so the whole port, not a sample of it, is a build dependency of the audit), plus two rfl statement pins (the sum longhand; the sawtooth longhand, which would break if the if-branch were dropped -- and dropping it would make dedekindSum_neg false). RE-VERIFIED 2026-09-07 (independent of the earlier run, commands re-run not trusted from memory): upstream re-fetched HTTP 200 / 4731 bytes / 4589 characters by python len(str); regex block-extract plus == comparison gives 21 identical, 0 differing, 0 missing; and all fifteen DRK-00 dedekindSum pin values, the three reciprocity instances and the (4,12) negative control were recomputed from scratch in Python fractions.Fraction with 0 mismatches, together with the classical s(1,k)=(k-1)(k-2)/(12k) check for k=1..24 and agreement of the range-form with the Ico-form over h in [-12,12] x k in [1,24]."}
{"id": "DRK-02", "kind": "math", "lean_name": "SocrateAI.NumberTheory.dedekindSum_add_dedekindSum", "lean_file": "Lean/SocrateAI/NumberTheory/DedekindSum.lean", "status": "proved", "depends_on": ["DRK-01"], "paper_claim": null, "statement_nl": "PROVED 2026-09-07, sorry-free. DEDEKIND RECIPROCITY. For naturals h, k with 0 < h, 0 < k and Nat.Coprime h k: dedekindSum h k + dedekindSum k h = (h/k + k/h + 1/(h*k))/12 - 1/4, as an identity in the rationals. Resolved by SocrateAI.NumberTheory.dedekindSum_add_dedekindSum in Lean/SocrateAI/NumberTheory/DedekindSum.lean; axiom footprint [propext, Classical.choice, Quot.sound], guarded in FinalCheck.lean. The INVERTED TRIPWIRE that previously asserted this node's footprint still contained sorryAx has been DELETED and replaced by that positive guard; the deletion is documented in FinalCheck.lean itself so that a vanished tripwire cannot be mistaken for a quietly removed check. PROVENANCE, TWO HALVES, DIFFERENT ANSWERS. STATEMENT: transcribed from anthropics/fermats-last-theorem, Theorems/Thm_dedekindSum_add_dedekindSum.lean (Apache-2.0, 391 bytes), including upstream's binder names and hypothesis order -- a STATEMENT-ONLY port, unchanged from before. PROOF: INDEPENDENT. It is NOT a port and NOT an adaptation of FLT's proof. FLT's proof is the single tactic p2m_exact_reverting against P2MW.S_dedekindSum_add_dedekindSum.solution; that tactic does not exist in this library and the 1286-line P2M/Sol file behind it was never read. It is also NOT Apostol's Theorem 3.11 proof, which goes through finite cotangent sums. What was used is the classical RADEMACHER-GROSSWALD LATTICE-POINT DOUBLE COUNT -- the route this node's own searcher brief recommended precisely because it avoids cotangent sums -- re-derived against Mathlib primitives. Do not cite FLT for the proof. THE ARGUMENT, so a reviewer can check it rather than rerun it. (1) sum_mod_perm: for coprime h, k the map r -> h*r mod k permutes Finset.Ico 1 k (injective by Nat.ModEq.cancel_left_of_coprime, onto by cardinality via Finset.card_image_of_injOn). This is the first place coprimality enters and is exactly what fails at (4,12). (2) dedekindSum_eq_modSum: s(h,k) = (sum over r in Ico 1 k of r*(h*r mod k))/k^2 - (k-1)/4, using dedekindSum_eq_sum_Ico, dedekindSaw_natCast_div and step (1) to kill the two linear terms. (3) double_count: sum over r in Ico 1 k of r*floor(h*r/k), read as the weight-r count of lattice points of Ico 1 k x Ico 1 h strictly below the line s*k = h*r, summed in the other order via Finset.sum_comm; the two fibre identifications are fibre_left (needs k not dividing h*r, i.e. coprimality again) and fibre_right (needs only 0 < h). (4) Squaring h*floor(k*s/h) + (k*s mod h) = k*s and summing turns sum of floor(k*s/h)^2 into s(k,h); the s(k,h) so produced CANCELS the one already in the goal, leaving a rational-function identity in h and k closed by field_simp; ring. Gauss sums over Ico 1 n are proved in Q by induction (sum_Ico_one_const, sum_Ico_one_id, sum_Ico_one_sq) so that no natural-number subtraction ever escapes. All scaffolding lemmas are private to the file. SIGN DISCIPLINE (executed BEFORE the proof, not after). Seventeen named, axiom-guarded decide-+kernel pins were landed in a new ReciprocityGate block ahead of the theorem, values computed first in Python fractions.Fraction FROM THE DEFINITIONS (not from the reciprocity formula) and only then re-derived by the Lean kernel: reciprocity at the coprime pairs (7,11), (9,25), (2,15), (4,9), (11,13), (3,8) and the degenerate (1,1); the intermediate floor sums sum r*floor(7r/11) = 219 and sum floor(7r/11) = sum floor(11s/7) = 30 = (h-1)(k-1)/2; the mod sum sum r*(7r mod 11) = 286; the individual values s(7,11) = -3/22, s(11,7) = 1/14, s(9,25) = 4/25, s(25,9) = -4/27 so that a compensating pair of errors cannot satisfy a reciprocity pin; and TWO NEW NEGATIVE CONTROLS at (6,9) and (10,15) alongside the pre-existing (4,12), all three proving reciprocity FALSE off coprimality. 21 kernel checks, 0 disagreements, 0 pin values had to be adjusted. Separately, the whole proof route (all seven intermediate relations, not just the final identity) was verified in Python over all 399 coprime pairs with h, k <= 25 before a line of Lean was written: 0 mismatches. HYPOTHESES ARE ALL LOAD-BEARING: hhk in mod_pos_of_coprime and fibre_left; hk and hh as the non-vanishing of (k : Q) and (h : Q) in the closing field_simp. SCOPE, STATED PLAINLY (LL-1): this is the h, k : N statement, so negative h is out of scope -- that is the reference's own scope (FLT and Apostol both restrict to positive coprime integers), so it is a MATCH and not a weakening. DRK-04 states its descent over dedekindSum d c with d : Z possibly negative or >= c; DRK-02 does not directly serve that, and the bridge is dedekindSum_add_mul (reduce d mod c) plus dedekindSum_neg (odd in h), both already sorry-free in DRK-01. That bridge is unwritten work and is NOT covered by this node. UNBLOCKS: DRK-04, hence DRK-06, hence ETA-01."}
{"id": "DRK-03", "kind": "math", "lean_name": "SocrateAI.NumberTheory.rademacherPhi_of_pos", "lean_file": "Lean/SocrateAI/NumberTheory/RademacherPhi.lean", "status": "proved", "depends_on": ["DRK-00", "DRK-01"], "paper_claim": null, "statement_nl": "PROVED, sorry-free (2026-09-07). Resolving lean_name SocrateAI.NumberTheory.rademacherPhi_of_pos; the node's other two theorems are SocrateAI.NumberTheory.rademacherPhi_neg and SocrateAI.NumberTheory.rademacherPhi_T_zpow, both also sorry-free, in the same file. WHAT IS PROVED. The two DEFINITIONS: rademacherPhi (Apostol's Phi) is defined on ALL of SL(2,Z): if c = 0 then b/d, else (a+d)/c - 12*sign(c)*dedekindSum d |c|. rademacherPsi (the RADEMACHER SYMBOL) is defined separately as rademacherPhi g - 3*sign(c*(a+d)). LL-22 IS THE WHOLE POINT OF THIS NODE: Phi and Psi are DIFFERENT FUNCTIONS, they get different names, and DRK-00's tripwires pin them as different numbers on three matrices and as equal on exactly S and T. rademacherPhi_ne_rademacherPsi is landed as a sorry-free theorem, and FinalCheck.lean carries a rfl pin of the -3*sign(c(a+d)) offset so it cannot drift. THE THREE THEOREMS. (a) rademacherPhi_of_pos: for 0 < c, Phi g = (a+d)/c - 12*dedekindSum d c.toNat, i.e. our named Phi agrees with the expression FLT writes INLINE in Thm_rademacher_phi_step.lean and Thm_ModularForm_eta_specialLinearGroup_smul.lean. This is the BRIDGE LEMMA and it is now closed, so quoting an FLT statement against our Phi is justified in Lean (subject to Int.toNat_of_nonneg for the denominator cast, which is the only textual difference from FLT). Proof: if_neg hc.ne', Int.sign_eq_one_of_pos hc, c.natAbs = c.toNat by omega, push_cast; ring. (b) rademacherPhi_neg: Phi(-g) = Phi(g), so Phi descends to PSL(2,Z). This is what LICENSES the c<0 reduction. Proof: helper SL2_neg_apply (from Mathlib's SpecialLinearGroup.coe_neg) gives the entries of -g; the c=0 branch is (-b)/(-d)=b/d by neg_div_neg_eq; the c/=0 branch uses Int.sign_neg, Int.natAbs_neg and our dedekindSum_neg, whose two sign flips cancel, then field_simp/ring with c /= 0. (c) rademacherPhi_T_zpow: Phi(T^n) = n, the normalisation that fixes Phi's additive constant. Proof: Mathlib's ModularGroup.coe_T_zpow gives !![1,n;0,1], so the c=0 branch returns n/1. Unconditional in n. COVERAGE. The three together determine Phi everywhere and non-circularly: c>0 by of_pos; c<0 by neg then of_pos on -g; c=0 forces ad=1 so g = +-T^n, covered by T_zpow plus neg. SIGN DISCIPLINE (LL-22, brief's '6+ decide pins as guarded lemmas'). ELEVEN named, axiom-guarded pins sit in RademacherPhi.lean ABOVE the three proofs, so no pin can be discharged by the theorem it pins: three instances of of_pos (c = 5, 12, 1, on pin matrices pinMatC5/pinMatC12/pinMatC1), a NEGATIVE CONTROL rademacherPhi_of_pos_fails_c_neg showing the of_pos identity is FALSE at c = -4 (Phi = -3 but the RHS is -3/2, since (-4).toNat = 0) so the hypothesis 0 < c is load-bearing, three instances of neg (c>0, c<0, c=0 with b=5), the c=0 value pin Phi !![1,5;0,1] = 5, and three instances of T_zpow (n = 0, 4, -5). All eleven are 'decide +kernel' -- no native_decide, no Lean.ofReduceBool -- and every value was recomputed independently in Python (fractions.Fraction, re-implementing dedekindSaw/dedekindSum/Phi from the mathematical definitions) BEFORE the Lean statements were written; the two agree on all eleven. AXIOM GUARDS. FinalCheck.lean carries positive #guard_msgs #print axioms guards, footprint [propext, Classical.choice, Quot.sound], for rademacherPhi_of_pos, rademacherPhi_neg, rademacherPhi_T_zpow, the helper SL2_neg_apply, and all eleven pins. The three INVERTED tripwires that previously asserted these still carried sorryAx have been deleted and replaced by those positive guards, with a receipt comment in FinalCheck.lean recording the deletion (same convention as DRK-02). NOT CLOSED BY THIS NODE: DRK-04 (rademacher_phi_step) is still sorry in the same file, and its inverted tripwire is untouched. PROVENANCE (ATTRIBUTION.md section 2): INDEPENDENT, not ported, not adapted. FLT has NO Phi at all -- it never names the expression, never treats c <= 0, and has nothing resembling Psi; it does not state any of these three lemmas, so there was no upstream proof to follow. The proofs are Lean core / Mathlib primitives (Int.sign_eq_one_of_pos, Int.sign_neg, Int.natAbs_neg, ModularGroup.coe_T_zpow, SpecialLinearGroup.coe_neg) plus our own dedekindSum_neg. NO FLT ATTRIBUTION ENTRY IS CLAIMED OR OWED FOR THEM. (The dedekindSaw/dedekindSum DEFINITIONS they sit on top of ARE a port and ARE attributed -- that is DRK-01's entry at ATTRIBUTION.md, not this node's.)"}
{"id": "DRK-04", "kind": "math", "lean_name": "SocrateAI.NumberTheory.rademacher_phi_step", "lean_file": "Lean/SocrateAI/NumberTheory/RademacherPhi.lean", "status": "proved", "depends_on": ["DRK-02", "DRK-03"], "paper_claim": null, "statement_nl": "PROVED 2026-09-07, sorry-free. THE EUCLIDEAN-DESCENT COCYCLE STEP FOR Phi. For naturals c, r with 0 < c, 0 < r and integers a, b, d, q satisfying r = q*c - d and a*d - b*c = 1: (a+d)/c - 12*dedekindSum d c = (q*a - b + c)/r - 12*dedekindSum c r + q - 3. In English: replacing gamma = !![a,b;c,d] by the matrix whose lower-left entry is the NEXT REMAINDER r = q*c - d of the Euclidean algorithm changes (a+d)/c - 12 s(d,c) by exactly q - 3. This is the arithmetic engine of DRK-06: it turns the analytic identification of the eta multiplier into a strong induction on c, base case c = 1. RESOLVED BY SocrateAI.NumberTheory.rademacher_phi_step in Lean/SocrateAI/NumberTheory/RademacherPhi.lean; axiom footprint [propext, Classical.choice, Quot.sound], guarded POSITIVELY in FinalCheck.lean. The INVERTED TRIPWIRE that previously asserted this node's footprint still contained sorryAx has been DELETED and replaced by that positive guard; the deletion is documented in FinalCheck.lean itself (same convention as DRK-02 and DRK-03) so that a vanished tripwire cannot be mistaken for a quietly removed check. STATEMENT UNCHANGED BY THE PROOF, VERIFIED NOT ASSERTED: the theorem text is character-identical (256 chars, python len(str)) to the pre-proof text, which the comparator had already checked verbatim against upstream (242 chars both after whitespace normalisation). NOTHING WAS WEAKENED: no hypothesis added (in particular NO coprimality hypothesis was bolted on -- coprimality is DERIVED from hdet and hrd by an explicit Bezout combination), none dropped, none strengthened, and the conclusion is untouched. PROVENANCE, TWO HALVES, DIFFERENT ANSWERS. STATEMENT: STATEMENT-ONLY port, verbatim from anthropics/fermats-last-theorem, Theorems/Thm_rademacher_phi_step.lean (Apache-2.0, 429 bytes, fetched 2026-09-07 HTTP 200), with upstream's binder names, hypothesis order and shape preserved. Attributed at ATTRIBUTION.md section 2. PROOF: INDEPENDENT. It is NOT a port and NOT an adaptation of FLT's proof. Upstream's proof is the single tactic p2m_exact_reverting against P2MW.S_rademacher_phi_step.solution, a 1287-line P2M/Sol file; that tactic does not exist in this library and that file was never read. DO NOT CITE FLT FOR THE PROOF. THE ARGUMENT, so a reviewer can check it rather than rerun it, in four steps. (1) COPRIMALITY IS DERIVED, NOT ASSUMED. hdet and hrd together exhibit a Bezout combination (-a)*r + (a*q - b)*c = a*d - b*c = 1, so IsCoprime (r : Z) (c : Z) by the anonymous constructor and Nat.Coprime r c by Mathlib's Int.isCoprime_iff_gcd_eq_one and Int.gcd_natCast_natCast. This is what lets DRK-02 apply and it is why no coprimality hypothesis appears in the statement. (2) THE LEFT SUM IS REDUCED TO A NATURAL-NUMBER ONE. hrd gives d = -(r) + q*c, so d is congruent to -r mod c; our dedekindSum_add_mul (periodicity in the first argument) and dedekindSum_neg (oddness) give s(d,c) = -s(r,c) with r a NATURAL number -- which is exactly what DRK-02 needs, since reciprocity is stated for h k : N. This is the bridge DRK-02's own node text flagged as unwritten work; it is now written and it is three rewrites. (3) RECIPROCITY. dedekindSum_add_dedekindSum r c hr hc hcop gives s(r,c) + s(c,r) = (r/c + c/r + 1/(r*c))/12 - 1/4. Substituting, the s(c,r) terms CANCEL between the two sides of the goal -- note the argument order, s(d,c) on the left but s(c,r) on the right, and it is precisely this swap that reciprocity supplies. (4) FIELD ALGEBRA. What is left is the private lemma phi_step_algebra: for C, R nonzero rationals with R = Q*C - D and A*D - B*C = 1, (A+D)/C + (R/C + C/R + 1/(R*C)) - 3 = (Q*A - B + C)/R + Q - 3. Proved by eliminating D with the Euclidean step (subst) and then B with the determinant (B = (A*(Q*C-R)-1)/C, subst), after which the goal is an identity in A, C, Q, R alone and field_simp; ring closes it with nothing to guess. Its content is A*R + 1 = C*(Q*A - B). dedekindSum_one_right, which the searcher brief also offered, turned out NOT to be needed: the c = 1 and r = 1 corners fall out of the same uniform argument. SIGN DISCIPLINE, EXECUTED BEFORE THE PROOF AND NOT AFTER. TWELVE named, axiom-guarded decide-+kernel instance pins plus THREE named NEGATIVE CONTROLS were landed in a new RademacherPhiStepGate block ahead of the theorem, and built green (3.3s) before a line of the proof was written. Values were computed first in PYTHON (fractions.Fraction, re-implementing dedekindSaw/dedekindSum AND both sides of the identity straight from the mathematical definitions, not from this library and NOT from the reciprocity formula) and only then re-derived by the Lean kernel: 15 kernel checks, 0 disagreements, 0 pin values had to be adjusted. The pins are chosen to hit the corners a port usually breaks in: c=1 and r=1 together (pin_c1_r1), r=1 with c>1 i.e. the descent base case (pin_c7_r1), r>c (pin_c5_r7), q=0 with d<0 (pin_c5_q0), q<0 with d<0 and b<0 (pin_c5_qneg), a<0 and b<0 (pin_c7_aneg), composite c=12 where the gcd>1 summands are killed by the if-branch of dedekindSaw (pin_c12_r7), d=11>c i.e. an UNREDUCED numerator so dedekindSum_add_mul does real work (pin_c5_dbig), c=13 (pin_c13_r5), and both sums nonzero at once (pin_c4_r5). NEGATIVE CONTROLS: rademacher_phi_step_fails_det_ne_one (det=3) and _fails_det_ne_one_2 (det=-2) prove the identity is FALSE off hdet, and _fails_hrd proves it FALSE at an r that is positive but is not the Euclidean remainder -- so BOTH hypotheses are load-bearing, not decorative. THE SAME PYTHON SWEEP, run before any Lean, enumerated EVERY (a,b,c,d,q) with 1 <= c <= 14, |d| <= 25, gcd(|d|,c)=1, |a| <= 12, b := (a*d-1)/c integral, |q| <= 8 and r = q*c - d > 0: 24769 satisfying instances, 0 COUNTEREXAMPLES, with corner coverage c=1 (10625), r=1 (1037), d<0 (19320), q<0 (6207), a<0 (12188), q=0 (1457), d>=c (3713). FOUR OF THE TWELVE PINS ARE A PROMOTION, NOT NEW WORK, AND ARE LABELLED AS SUCH: the four anonymous decide-+kernel examples that DRK-00 already carried for this node are now the named theorems rademacher_phi_step_pin_c5_r2, _c5_r7, _c3_r2, _c4_r5, because an example has no name and so cannot carry a #print axioms guard. Nothing was dropped; a comment at the old site records the move. The other eight pins and all three negative controls are new. SCOPE, STATED PLAINLY (LL-1): c : N with 0 < c makes c < 0 INEXPRESSIBLE and 0 < r excludes r = 0. That is upstream's own scoping and the right scoping for a Euclidean-descent step (the remainder is positive by construction), so it is a MATCH and not a weakening -- but it means THIS NODE DOES NOT COVER c <= 0. The c <= 0 bookkeeping lives in DRK-03 (rademacherPhi_neg reduces c<0 to c>0 via gamma -> -gamma; the c=0 branch of the definition; rademacherPhi_T_zpow; and the bridge rademacherPhi_of_pos identifying our named Phi with FLT's inline expression under 0 < c). DRK-06 must route c <= 0 through those. LL-22: dedekindSum here is Apostol's s(h,k); the expression this lemma is about is Apostol's Phi (via rademacherPhi_of_pos), NOT the Rademacher symbol Psi. ONE CORRECTION TO THIS NODE'S OWN EARLIER TEXT (LL-1): the reference 'Apostol ch. 3' overstates. Apostol ch. 3 grounds the Phi expression and the reciprocity law but does NOT contain this descent identity -- Apostol proves the eta transformation by Iseki's formula, not by Euclidean descent. The identity is the Rademacher-Grosswald cocycle Phi(AB) = Phi(A) + Phi(B) - 3*sign(c_A c_B c_AB) specialised with Phi(T^q) = q, which is where the +q and the -3 come from. Apostol validates the conventions and the ingredients, not the lemma. UNBLOCKS: DRK-06, hence ETA-01. WHAT THIS DOES NOT CLOSE: DRK-05, DRK-06, DRK-07 and ETA-01 are all STILL OPEN with their inverted tripwires untouched. DRK-04 is the arithmetic engine of DRK-06, not DRK-06."}
{"id": "DRK-05", "kind": "math", "lean_name": "SocrateAI.ModularForms.logDeriv_eta_smul_eq_logDeriv_csqrt", "lean_file": "Lean/SocrateAI/ModularForms/EtaMultiplier.lean", "status": "proved", "depends_on": ["DRK-03"], "paper_claim": null, "statement_nl": "PROVED 2026-09-08, BOTH HALVES, sorry-free. RECONSTRUCTED NODE -- the run brief was truncated mid-node at 'theorem logDeriv_eta_smul_eq_logDeriv_csqrt'; the NAME is the brief's verbatim, the STATEMENT was reconstructed, and that reconstruction is recorded here rather than papered over. WHAT IS PROVED. (a) logDeriv_eta_smul_eq_logDeriv_csqrt: for gamma in SL(2,Z) with c > 0 and z in the upper half plane, logDeriv (eta composed with mobiusC gamma) z = logDeriv (w |-> csqrt(-i*(c*w+d)) * eta w) z, where mobiusC gamma w = (a*w+b)/(c*w+d) as a self-map of C. (b) exists_eta_smul_const: there is a nonzero constant C(gamma), independent of z, with eta(gamma . z) = C(gamma) * csqrt(-i*(c*z+d)) * eta z for every z. (a) plus connectedness of upperHalfPlaneSet gives (b) via logDeriv_eqOn_iff. HOW: the E2-period route MATHLIB_PR.md recommends, NOT FLT's closed-form-first route. ModularForm.logDeriv_eta_eq_E2 turns each side into E2; EisensteinSeries.E2_slash_action gamma supplies the weight-2 defect D2 gamma z = 2*pi*i*c/denom; riemannZeta_two gives zeta(2) = pi^2/6; and i^2 = -1 turns the SUBTRACTED defect into the ADDED c/(2(cz+d)) that Complex.deriv_sqrt produces on the square-root side. NOTE: this is NOT literally Mathlib's S-case proof with S replaced by gamma, as the earlier version of this node guessed -- Mathlib's S-case leans on ModularGroup.denom_S (denom S z = z) and on the BARE sqrt, and neither survives generalisation; what survives is the shape. Relative to Mathlib it is a strict generalisation of ModularForm.logDeriv_eta_comp_eq_logDeriv_csqrt_eta and eta_comp_eqOn_const_mul_csqrt_eta (Mathlib/NumberTheory/ModularForms/Discriminant.lean:75,94), which cover gamma = ModularGroup.S only. SIGN GATE: twenty-five norm_num pins and two negative controls precede the proof in the file (drk05_pin_slit_*, drk05_pin_slit_pos_*, drk05_pin_defect_*, drk05_neg_control_slit_cneg, drk05_neg_control_plus_I), all proved from Mathlib primitives alone so a pin cannot be discharged by the argument it exists to check; all 27 carry FinalCheck axiom guards. Every right-hand side was computed independently BEFORE any Lean proof existed, twice: mpmath at 50 dps and exact fractions.Fraction, agreeing to the last digit. The same sweep verified the full DRK-05(a) identity numerically at 16 (gamma, z) pairs against the closed form logDeriv eta z + c/(2(cz+d)), agreement <= 3e-51 except at c = 12, 16 where the residual is eta-product truncation at gamma z. HONESTY (LL-1) -- WHAT THIS IS NOT: DRK-05 is the ANALYTIC HALF ONLY. It proves the multiplier is a CONSTANT; it says NOTHING about its VALUE. DRK-05(b) is STRICTLY WEAKER than FLT's eta_specialLinearGroup_smul (= eta_specialLinearGroup_smul_flt, DRK-06): the reference gives the multiplier as exp(pi*i/12*((a+d)/c - 12*s(d,c))) and DRK-05(b) replaces that value by an unnamed existential. The reference implies DRK-05(b) in one line; the converse is all of DRK-06. No Dedekind sum, no Phi and no Psi appears anywhere in DRK-05, so LL-22 cannot bite here. DRK-05 does NOT close FLT item (3), does NOT remove F3.2-OBSTRUCTED, and does NOT unblock ETA-01. It also inherits the reference's scope gap: both statements carry 0 < gamma 1 0, so c = 0 and c < 0 (which Gamma0(N) contains) are untouched and still route through DRK-03. NAME DRIFT, recorded: the brief writes logDeriv_eta_smul_eq_logDeriv_csqrt_eta and exists_eta_smul_eq_const_mul_csqrt; what is landed, guarded and named here is logDeriv_eta_smul_eq_logDeriv_csqrt (no trailing _eta) and exists_eta_smul_const. PROVENANCE: INDEPENDENT. No FLT text was used; FLT has no logDeriv statement at all, only the closed form."}
{"id": "DRK-06", "kind": "math", "lean_name": "SocrateAI.ModularForms.eta_smul_eq_exp_rademacherPhi", "lean_file": "Lean/SocrateAI/ModularForms/EtaMultiplier.lean", "status": "proved", "depends_on": ["DRK-03", "DRK-04"], "paper_claim": null, "statement_nl": "PROVED 2026-09-08, SORRY-FREE, BOTH PHRASINGS. THE THEOREM THE WHOLE RUN EXISTS TO REACH. NODE ID RECONSTRUCTED: there is no DRK-06 in the run brief (the brief was truncated inside DRK-05), but DRK-04's own statement_nl refers to 'the arithmetic engine of DRK-06', so the node is reconstructed under that id. STATEMENT AS LANDED: for gamma in SL(2,Z) with c := gamma 1 0 > 0 and z in the upper half plane, eta(gamma . z) = exp(pi*i/12 * Phi(gamma)) * csqrt(-i*(c*z+d)) * eta z, where Phi = rademacherPhi is APOSTOL'S Phi and NOT the Rademacher symbol Psi (LL-22). LANDED TWICE, ON PURPOSE, AND BOTH ARE NOW PROVED. (1) eta_smul_eq_exp_rademacherPhi -- through our named rademacherPhi; this is the resolving lean_name and the one that is proved from scratch. (2) eta_specialLinearGroup_smul_flt -- the Dedekind sum written INLINE exactly as FLT writes it, with c.toNat as the second argument and no Phi anywhere, so a comparator can check our statement against upstream character-for-character. It is now ONE rw off (1) via rademacherPhi_of_pos_toNat (DRK-03, added 2026-09-08), which closes the (c : Z) vs (c.toNat : N) cast gap the DRK-06 comparator flagged as its residual (a). PROVENANCE: STATEMENT from anthropics/fermats-last-theorem, Theorems/Thm_ModularForm_eta_specialLinearGroup_smul.lean (Apache-2.0, 1024 bytes, fetched 2026-09-07). PROOF INDEPENDENT (ADAPTED, NOT PORTED): upstream's proof is p2m_exact_reverting against P2MW.S_ModularForm_eta_specialLinearGroup_smul.solution, a 9054-byte P2M/Sol file; that tactic does not exist in this library and that file was never read. OUR PROOF: strong induction on c = gamma 1 0. Euclidean step r = q*c - d with 0 <= r < c (Int.emod); r = 0 forces c | d hence c | 1 hence c = 1. BASE c = 1: gamma = T^a . S . T^d literally, so eta(gamma z) is our eta_add_int (F3.1-B3) twice around Mathlib's eta_comp_eq_csqrt_I_inv, and Phi(gamma) = a + d because s(d,1) = 0 (dedekindSum_one_right, DRK-01). STEP 0 < r < c: gamma = gamma' . S . T^q with gamma' = [[q*a-b, a],[r, c]], induction hypothesis at gamma', our rademacher_phi_step (DRK-04) giving Phi(gamma) = Phi(gamma') + q - 3, and the branch identity sqrt(A)*(sqrt(-i)*sqrt(w)) = sqrt(-i)*sqrt(-i(cz+d)) with sqrt(-i) = exp(-pi i/4) = exp(pi i (-3)/12) supplying exactly the -3. The branch bookkeeping rests on csqrt_mul_of_re_mul_pos (sqrt u * sqrt v = sqrt(uv) whenever Re(sqrt u * sqrt v) > 0), proved here from our own csqrt_sq (F3.2-A7) plus Complex.cpow_inv_two_re; Mathlib at our pinned revision carries no multiplicativity lemma for Complex.sqrt. DRK-05 (exists_eta_smul_const) IS NOT USED: the induction produces the constant and its value together, so the analytic half is subsumed rather than invoked. The DAG edge to DRK-05 has been REPLACED by an edge to DRK-03, which is genuinely required (rademacherPhi_of_pos / _toNat is what makes the Phi phrasing equal FLT's). SIGN GATE (came first, LL-22): eight decide+kernel descent pins Phi(gamma) = Phi(gamma') + q - 3 at c in {2,3,4,5,7,12,13} including q = 0 and negative d; six decide+kernel base pins Phi = a + d at c = 1; two branch pins fixing the sign of Im sqrt(-i) < 0 < Im sqrt(+i); three negative controls (shift -2 fails, shift 0 fails, exp(+pi i/4) is not sqrt(-i)). All values were computed independently in Python (fractions.Fraction for Phi; cmath for the analytic law at 8 matrices x 2 points and the branch identity at 6 matrices x 2 points, ratios 1 +- 1e-13) BEFORE any Lean proof of this node existed. SCOPE, LOUDLY (LL-1): PROVED FOR c > 0 ONLY. That is FLT's own scope, so it is not a weakening of the reference -- but it is NOT the full eta transformation law on all of SL(2,Z). c = 0 is eta_add_int + rademacherPhi_T_zpow; c < 0 reduces by gamma -> -gamma (rademacherPhi_neg); NEITHER is written down. DRK-06 DOES NOT CLOSE ETA-01 OR REMOVE F3.2-OBSTRUCTED. Still needed for ETA-01: the c <= 0 cases, the conjugated matrices gamma_delta for each delta | N, and the product over delta of eps(gamma_delta)^{r_delta} = 1 under Ligozat's congruences (DRK-07 plus counting). ligozat_general is still sorry. GUARDS: FinalCheck.lean carries positive #print axioms guards ([propext, Classical.choice, Quot.sound]) on both phrasings, on all three induction lemmas, on the eleven csqrt branch lemmas, on the ten bookkeeping lemmas, and on all sixteen pins and three negative controls; the two inverted sorryAx tripwires that pinned this node as open have been DELETED and the deletion is receipted in a comment there."}
{"id": "DRK-07", "kind": "math", "lean_name": null, "lean_file": "Lean/SocrateAI/ModularForms/EtaMultiplier.lean", "status": "open", "depends_on": ["DRK-06"], "paper_claim": null, "statement_nl": "OPEN (two sorry bodies). RECONSTRUCTED NODE (see DRK-05: the brief was truncated). PACKAGING the eta multiplier as a function of gamma alone. PROVED, sorry-free: the DEFINITION etaMultiplierPhi gamma = exp(pi*i/12 * rademacherPhi gamma), guarded in FinalCheck with a clean axiom footprint. OPEN: (a) etaMultiplierPhi_pow24 -- etaMultiplierPhi gamma is a 24th root of unity. This needs the INTEGRALITY of Phi (that Phi gamma is an integer for every gamma in SL(2,Z)), a corollary of DRK-04 that is NOT separately stated anywhere in this library yet; a searcher taking this node should state it first, as 'exists n : Z, rademacherPhi gamma = n'. (b) etaMultiplierPhi_mul_cocycle -- multiplicativity up to the square-root cocycle, which is what makes the multiplier a multiplier SYSTEM rather than a formula. Landed deliberately in the WEAK form 'there exists an eighth root of unity zeta with eps(g*d) = zeta * eps(g) * eps(d)', because the precise cocycle sign is exactly what the Rademacher symbol Psi (not Phi) is designed to track -- Rademacher's cocycle is Phi(g*d) = Phi(g) + Phi(d) - 3*sign(c_g * c_d * c_{gd}), and that -3 IS the Phi-versus-Psi discrepancy of LL-22. Pinning the sign wrongly here is the LL-22 failure mode, so it is left unpinned rather than pinned wrong. PROVENANCE: INDEPENDENT, no FLT counterpart."}
{"id": "DRK-08", "kind": "math", "lean_name": "SocrateAI.ModularForms.etaMultiplierVal_neg", "lean_file": "Lean/SocrateAI/ModularForms/EtaMultiplierNeg.lean", "status": "proved", "depends_on": ["F32-A5", "F32-A9"], "paper_claim": null, "statement_nl": "PROVED 2026-09-08, sorry-free, BOTH declarations. PROVENANCE: INDEPENDENT -- comparator verdict NO_REFERENCE, not MATCH: the full FLT tree (GitHub trees API, recursive, 45999 paths) filtered on ModularForm_eta|_eta_|etaMult|rademacher|dedekindSum contains nothing of either shape, and FLT's own general-Gamma0(N) eta-quotient result (etaProductEleven_transform, N = 11, weight 2) reaches all of Gamma0(11) by Delta + 12th power + connectedness + coset enumeration and performs NO c-sign reduction at all (zero hits for lt_trichotomy|Int.sign|natAbs|lt_or_gt in its 39366-byte solution). NO ATTRIBUTION.md port entry is owed; ATTRIBUTION.md section 5 (EtaMultiplierNeg.lean) records every declaration in the file as INDEPENDENT. (1) Resolving lean_name SocrateAI.ModularForms.etaMultiplierVal_neg: for r : EtaExp with sum_{delta | N} r delta = 2k and gamma in Gamma0 N, etaMultiplierVal N r k (-gamma) = (-1)^k * etaMultiplierVal N r k gamma. Proof: -gamma = (-1)*gamma, then etaMultiplierVal_mul (F32-A5, run 3) and etaMultiplierVal_neg_one (F32-A9, run 3, w(-I) = (-1)^{-k} = (-1)^k). hgamma is load-bearing. N = 0 degenerate case is fine (divisors 0 = empty forces k = 0). (2) Second declaration SocrateAI.ModularForms.exists_pos_lower_left_or_T_zpow: every gamma in Gamma0 N is +-gamma' with gamma' in Gamma0 N and 0 < gamma' 1 0, or else +-T^n. Proof: lt_trichotomy on gamma 1 0; c < 0 takes gamma' = -gamma (in Gamma0 N via neg_one_mem_Gamma0 + mul_mem); c = 0 forces a*d = 1 by sl_det_entries, then run-3 eq_T_zpow_of_lower_left_zero and eq_neg_T_zpow_of_lower_left_zero. LL-25 TRAP RECORDED IN THE FILE: Mathlib's ModularGroup.exists_eq_T_zpow_of_c_eq_zero (NumberTheory/Modular.lean:328) is ACTION-level (exists n, forall z, g . z = T^n . z), i.e. PSL-level; its matrix-level facts live only inside its proof as suffices steps and are not exported. Using it would silently weaken part 2 to the Moebius action and destroy the point of part 1 (w(-gamma) != w(gamma) at odd k). DEPENDS_ON CORRECTED: the node brief said depends_on = [DRK-06]; that is WRONG. Neither declaration uses DRK-03, DRK-04, DRK-05, DRK-06, dedekindSum, rademacherPhi, Complex.sqrt or any analysis. The import list of EtaMultiplierNeg.lean is the receipt: it imports SocrateAI.ModularForms.EtaQuotientModularity and nothing else (it deliberately does not import RademacherPhi, which is why the pin matrices are redeclared locally). DRK-08 was unblocked from the start and provable in parallel with DRK-05/DRK-06. The two deps recorded here are the run-3 nodes that OWN the tools: F32-A5 (etaMultiplierVal_mul via etaQuotient_multiplier) and F32-A9 (etaMultiplierVal_neg_one via multiplier_elliptic). BUILT_FROM CORRECTED: three items listed in the brief are NOT used -- rademacherPhi_neg (DRK-03; it licenses the c<0 reduction at the eta/Phi level, a different theorem), Complex.mem_slitPlane_iff (present only because of the false docstring below), and etaMultiplierVal_T_eq_one (unused, AND it carries an extra hypothesis h24 : LigozatCongr1 N r that neither DRK-08 statement has -- flagged because the ASSEMBLED reduction 'w(gamma) for all gamma in Gamma0 N' does need w(T^n) = 1, hence does need LigozatCongr1; DRK-08 itself is unconditional, the assembly is not). DEFECT IN THE BRIEF'S DOCSTRING, CORRECTED, NOT COPIED: the claim '-I(cz+d) leaves slitPlane when c < 0' is FALSE. Complex.slitPlane = {z | 0 < z.re or z.im != 0} (Analysis/Complex/Basic.lean:637); for c < 0 the re-disjunct fails but the im-disjunct holds off the single line Re z = -d/c. Computed counterexample: c = -1, d = 0, z = 0.3+1.1i gives -i(cz+d) = -1.1+0.3i, which IS in slitPlane. The true statement, and the one DRK05Aux.slit_mem (EtaMultiplier.lean:466) actually makes, is about the open RIGHT HALF-PLANE: Re(-i(cz+d)) = c*Im z is negative exactly when c is. SCOPE, LOUDLY (LL-1): DRK-08 does NOT extend DRK-06 to c <= 0 and must not be reported as 'DRK-06 now holds for all gamma'. The single-eta closed form eta(gamma z) = exp(pi i Phi/12)*sqrt(-i(cz+d))*eta(z) is FALSE for c < 0, off by a factor of i -- checked numerically (400-term eta product, python3 cmath, independent of this library) at gamma = -S, z = 0.3+1.1i: ratio = -i for c = -1 and +1 for c = +1. DRK-08 is phrased at the eta-QUOTIENT multiplier level precisely because the per-eta defect i collapses there to i^{2k} = (-1)^k, which is exactly part 1's factor -- an independent cross-check of the (-1)^k, since part 1 derives it from etaMultiplierVal_neg_one instead. GUARDS (LL-2/LL-7): 29 #print axioms guards in FinalCheck.lean, all [propext, Classical.choice, Quot.sound]. Thirteen pins (drk08_pin_*, computed independently in python3 integer matrix arithmetic before the Lean statements were written) and five negative controls: drk08_neg_control_cneg4_not_T_zpow (at c = -4 the SECOND disjunct of part 2 is FALSE, so the proof really produced gamma' = -gamma with c' = 4 > 0), drk08_neg_control_T5_not_pos_lower_left (at c = 0 the FIRST disjunct is FALSE), drk08_neg_control_negT3_wrong_sign (the c = 0 negative branch really has n = -(gamma 0 1), not +(gamma 0 1)), drk08_neg_control_even_k_blind ((-1)^2 = 1: at even k the factor is invisible, which is why the guard is taken at odd k), and drk08_neg_control_neg_S_ne_S (the ODD-k guard: N = 1, r = 2 constant, f = eta^2, k = 1, where w(S) = -i is already proved two independent ways in run 3, so w(-S) = i != w(S) -- a proof of part 1 that dropped the (-1)^k would fail here). Full build: 'Build completed successfully (3486 jobs).'"}
{"id": "DRK-09", "kind": "math", "lean_name": "SocrateAI.ModularForms.etaMultiplierVal_eq_exp_etaPhiSum", "lean_file": "Lean/SocrateAI/ModularForms/EtaPhiSum.lean", "status": "proved", "depends_on": ["DRK-03", "DRK-06", "F32-A3", "F32-A5", "F32-A7"], "paper_claim": null, "statement_nl": "PROVED 2026-09-08, sorry-free, ALL THREE declarations the node was scoped in: the definition SocrateAI.ModularForms.etaPhiSum, the split form etaPhiSum_eq, and the resolving lean_name etaMultiplierVal_eq_exp_etaPhiSum. STATEMENT: for gamma in Gamma0 N with 0 < gamma 1 0 and an exponent vector r : EtaExp with sum over delta dividing N of r delta = 2*k, the eta-quotient multiplier is w(gamma) = (-I)^k * exp(pi*I/12 * etaPhiSum N r gamma), where etaPhiSum N r gamma = sum over delta | N of r delta * ((a+d)*delta/c - 12*dedekindSum d (c/delta).toNat). PROOF ROUTE (independent, against OUR architecture): for each delta | N, run 3's divisor_smul_comm_explicit rewrites delta*(gamma z) as gamma_delta*(delta z) with gamma_delta = divisorConj = !![a, b*delta; c/delta, d]; DRK-06 (eta_smul_eq_exp_rademacherPhi) evaluates that single-eta multiplier; rademacherPhi_divisorConj (new, in this file) identifies Phi(gamma_delta) with the delta-summand of etaPhiSum; the sqrt factors are the SAME number for every delta (denom_divisorConj, F3.2-A3) so prod_zpow_const collects them into sqrt(-i(cz+d))^(2k) and csqrt_zpow_two_mul (F3.2-A7) turns that into (-i)^k (cz+d)^k with no residual branch choice. That last step is where hk is load-bearing and it has NO half-integral analogue. PROVENANCE: INDEPENDENT re-derivation -- no FLT text, tactic or proof strategy used, no FLT solution file read while writing, and EtaPhiSum.lean contains zero occurrences of 'p2m'. NO ATTRIBUTION.md port entry is owed for the proofs; ATTRIBUTION.md section 7 records the file declaration by declaration as independently re-derived. METADATA CORRECTION 1 OF 2, LOUD (LL-1): the node brief's statement_nl said 'No FLT counterpart'. THAT IS FALSE AND IS RETRACTED. Verified by receipt, not memory (fetched 2026-09-08, HTTP 200): P2M/Sol/S_ModularCurve_sharpUnitInvariant.lean (9342 bytes) contains, in namespace DedekindEtaLaw, def phi (gamma : SL(2,Z)) : Q := ((a+d):Q)/((c.toNat:N):Q) - 12*dedekindSum d c.toNat at line 22, and at lines 163-165 forms phi gamma - phi gamma' for gamma' = gamma_l with C' = c/l. That DIFFERENCE IS etaPhiSum in the two-divisor case N = l prime, r = (m, -m), weight k = 0. Theorems/Thm_rademacher_phi_level_congruence.lean (551 bytes) is the prime-level, two-divisor form of the arithmetic 24 | etaPhiSum that DRK-09 does not attempt. ModularForm.etaProductEleven_transform is an N = 11 instance. ATTRIBUTION.md section 6 had already warned that the 'no counterpart' claims rested on a name filter (ModularForm_eta|_eta_|etaMult|rademacher|dedekindSum) that sharpUnit / etaProductEleven / EtaQuotient do not match; this is that caveat coming true. WHY DRK-09 IS STILL A GENERALISATION: upstream is N = l prime (two divisors), r = (m,-m), weight 0. DRK-09 is arbitrary N, arbitrary r, arbitrary integer weight k. At weight 0 the sqrt factors cancel in a ratio -- upstream does exactly that, 'rw [<- Complex.exp_sub, ...]' at line 176 of the solution file -- so FLT never performs the (sqrt(-i(cz+d)))^(2k) = (-i)^k(cz+d)^k collection, which is DRK-09's real new content. METADATA CORRECTION 2 OF 2, LOUD (LL-1): the node's docstring said 'This is the theorem that deletes F3.2-OBSTRUCTED'. THAT WORD IS WRONG and is not reproduced in the Lean file. F3.2-OBSTRUCTED is the hgen hypothesis of multiplier_trivial_of_congr (EtaQuotientModularity.lean:3420). DRK-09 REPLACES hgen with an explicit Dedekind-sum evaluation; it does not discharge it. STILL OPEN, and NOT claimed: (a) c <= 0. c < 0 reduces by DRK-08 (etaMultiplierVal_neg + exists_pos_lower_left_or_T_zpow); c = 0 is gamma = +-T^n and is GENUINELY NOT COVERED -- etaMultiplierVal_c_zero_formula_fails PROVES the formula is FALSE there (N = 1, r == 2, k = 1, gamma = T: truth w(T) = e^{pi i/6} from run 3's etaQuotientH_T_smul and denom_T, formula gives -i, and the real parts sqrt(3)/2 vs 0 separate them). The comparator's trap is recorded in the file: at N = 1, r == 24, k = 12 the formula ACCIDENTALLY succeeds at c = 0, so a one-instance check would have missed this. (b) the arithmetic 24 | etaPhiSum N r gamma from LigozatCongr1 and LigozatCongr2 -- the actual hard node, upstream only at prime level. ETA-01 therefore REMAINS OPEN and DRK-09 must not be reported as closing it. SCOPE (LL-1): hk restricts to INTEGRAL weight (even sum of r delta); half-integral weight is excluded, forced by etaMultiplierVal's own signature. etaPhiSum is a total def using Int.ediv, so off Gamma0(N) (delta not dividing c) it silently rounds and is meaningless; every consumer must carry hgamma. DEVIATIONS FROM THE NODE TEXT, both stated loudly in the file header: (i) etaPhiSum is a plain def, not 'noncomputable def', because it IS computable and because the fifteen decide+kernel pins and four kernel negative controls -- the whole sign-discipline gate -- are impossible otherwise; no mathematical change. (ii) etaPhiSum_eq's hgamma and hc are UNUSED; etaPhiSum_eq_unconditional is proved first and the node's exact phrasing derived from it, so the node statement is landed verbatim AND the strictly stronger fact is available for the c <= 0 assembly. This is a STRENGTHENING, not a weakening. GATE (LL-2/LL-7): 58 #print axioms guards in FinalCheck.lean, every one [propext, Classical.choice, Quot.sound] except the thirteen pure exponent-vector defs, which depend on no axioms at all. FIFTEEN decide+kernel pins of etaPhiSum at explicit (N, r, gamma) with N in {2,4,5,6,7,9,11,12,13} and values 0, -24, 24, 11, 28, -18, 12, 18, 5, -3, 6, -8 -- including ODD values and values not divisible by 24, and including the pair (N=6, r=(1,1,1,1)) at two different gamma giving 0 and 24, which is what shows etaPhiSum is not constant in gamma. Every value was computed independently in python3 (fractions.Fraction; ((x)) and s(h,k) re-implemented from the mathematical definition and first checked against all nine decide+kernel pins of DedekindSum.lean) BEFORE the Lean statements were written. Eleven of the fifteen were additionally checked against a 4000-term eta-product evaluation of w(gamma) = f(gamma i)/((c i + d)^k f(i)); worst relative error 3.3e-14, and the sweep includes ODD k (N = 12, k = 1, w = e^{5 pi i/12}) and non-real w (N = 7, w = i; N = 13, w = e^{-2 pi i/3}), so it is not a sweep over trivial multipliers. FOUR kernel negative controls separate etaPhiSum from the three one-character mutants that the numerical sweep rejects with relative error of order 1: etaPhiSumSignFlip (+12*s instead of -12*s), etaPhiSumNoDelta ((a+d)/c instead of (a+d)*delta/c) and etaPhiSumWrongModulus (s(d,c) instead of s(d,c/delta)), each separated at BOTH N = 12 and N = 7. BONUS, and an independent consistency check on the whole formula: comparing DRK-09 at (N,r,k) = (1,24,12) with run 3's etaMultiplierVal_level_one_24 (the multiplier of Delta is 1, proved from CuspForm.discriminant with no Dedekind sums anywhere) forces exp(2 pi i Phi(gamma)) = 1, i.e. Phi(gamma) in Z (rademacherPhi_eq_intCast_of_pos for c > 0, rademacherPhi_eq_intCast on all of SL(2,Z)). That was the explicitly-named missing ingredient of DRK-07.a -- EtaMultiplier.lean:1235 says 'Needs Phi gamma in Z ... which is NOT yet stated anywhere in this library' -- and etaMultiplierPhi_pow24_of_intCast discharges DRK-07.a's statement under a new name. The sorry at EtaMultiplier.lean:1234 is deliberately NOT touched by this run, so its inverted FinalCheck tripwire still fires: it is now STALE, not wrong. The exponent 24, the weight k = 12 and the prefactor (-I)^12 = 1 all have to be exactly right for the integrality to come out, so this doubles as a fourth negative control on DRK-09 itself. Full build: 'Build completed successfully (3487 jobs).'"}
{"id": "DRK-10", "kind": "math", "lean_name": "SocrateAI.NumberTheory.dedekindSum_jacobiSym_mod_eight", "lean_file": "Lean/SocrateAI/NumberTheory/DedekindSumJacobi.lean", "status": "proved", "depends_on": ["DRK-01", "DRK-02", "F32-B3"], "paper_claim": null, "statement_nl": "PROVED 2026-09-08, sorry-free, BOTH halves the node was scoped in. HALF 1 (the resolving lean_name): SocrateAI.NumberTheory.dedekindSum_jacobiSym_mod_eight in Lean/SocrateAI/NumberTheory/DedekindSumJacobi.lean -- for h k : N with Odd k and Nat.Coprime h k, exists t : Z with 12*k*s(h,k) = k + 1 - 2*jacobiSym h k + 8*t. HALF 2: SocrateAI.ModularForms.kroneckerSym_eq_jacobiSym_of_odd in Lean/SocrateAI/ModularForms/KroneckerJacobi.lean -- for a : Z and b : N with Odd b and 0 < b, run 3's kroneckerSym a (b:Z) = Mathlib's jacobiSym a b. Both files are new leaves; no existing file was edited except Lean/SocrateAI.lean (two imports) and Lean/SocrateAI/FinalCheck.lean (28 guards). PROVENANCE, PER DECLARATION (ATTRIBUTION.md section 8). Half 1's STATEMENT is a STATEMENT-ONLY port: upstream Theorems/Thm_dedekindSum_jacobiSym_mod_eight.lean, Apache-2.0, anthropics/fermats-last-theorem, fetched 2026-09-08 HTTP 200 449 bytes, reproduced character for character after whitespace normalisation. Half 1's PROOF is OURS: upstream's proof is 'p2m_exact_reverting @_root_.P2MW.S_dedekindSum_jacobiSym_mod_eight.solution', a tactic and a solution file that do not exist in this library; the solution file was not fetched and not read. Half 2 is INDEPENDENT end to end -- FLT works with Mathlib's jacobiSym throughout and defines no Kronecker symbol, so no port entry is owed and none is filed. PROOF ROUTE (half 1, ours): strong induction on the ODD modulus k. k=1 is 0=0. For k>=2 the numerator is first reduced mod k (dedekindSum_add_mul + jacobiSym.mod_left'); an ODD numerator h'<k descends by ONE reciprocity step -- our DRK-02 dedekindSum_add_dedekindSum, cleared of denominators to h'*A + k*B = h'^2+k^2+1-3h'k -- plus Mathlib's jacobiSym.quadratic_reciprocity, landing at the strictly smaller ODD modulus h'; an EVEN numerator is reflected to k-h' (odd, SAME modulus, dedekindSum_neg + jacobiSym.at_neg_one + chi4) and handed to the odd branch, which is NOT a second induction and is what makes the even case terminate. The mod-8 bookkeeping is isolated in two pure-integer lemmas, descent_mod_eight and reflect_mod_eight, four cases each, all eight witnesses verified in sympy (residual 0) BEFORE being written. The step '8 | h*(A-C) implies 8 | A-C' uses h odd via 8 | h^2-1, not a gcd argument. INTEGRALITY, a new public lemma: exists_intCast_eq_twelve_mul_dedekindSum (h k : N) : exists z : Z, (z:Q) = 12*k*s(h,k), with NO hypotheses at all. LOUDLY (LL-1) this is the 12k form and is STRICTLY WEAKER than FLT's Thm_exists_intCast_eq_six_mul_dedekindSum.lean (fetched 2026-09-08 HTTP 200 330 bytes, '6 * k * dedekindSum h k' for 0<k); the 6k form is NOT proved and NOT claimed. Derivation is ours: 12k*s = 12(sum r*m_r)/k - 6 sum r*eps_r - 6 sum m_r + 3k sum eps_r with eps_r = min (h*r mod k) 1, plus k | 6 sum r*m_r from m_r == h*r mod k and 6 sum_{r<k} r^2 = (k-1)k(2k-1). GATE (sign discipline, placed BEFORE every general lemma of the file): TWELVE named decide+kernel instance pins of the EXACT statement with the witness t written out -- (1,1),(0,1),(1,5),(2,5),(3,7),(5,7),(7,11),(9,25),(11,13),(2,15),(4,9),(13,5) -- including h=0, an even numerator, a numerator larger than the modulus, a prime power k=25 and a composite k=15. Every t was computed independently in python3 (fractions.Fraction, sawtooth and s(h,k) re-implemented from the mathematical definition and first checked against all eleven existing decide+kernel pins of DedekindSum.lean) BEFORE the Lean was written, and the same sweep verified the statement at 3889 pairs (k odd < 80, h < 120, gcd = 1) with ZERO violations. FOUR negative controls prove both hypotheses load-bearing: drk10_fails_k_even_one_two and drk10_fails_k_even_five_six (k even), drk10_fails_gcd_three_nine and drk10_fails_gcd_five_fifteen (gcd > 1). A consistency tripwire, drk10_general_matches_pin_seven_eleven, instantiates the GENERAL theorem at (7,11) and proves the witness it produces is the independently computed t = -4. Half 2's gate: four agreement pins ((3,1),(5,3),(2,5),(-1,7), both sides computed independently) and TWO negative controls, kronecker_ne_jacobi_at_two_neg_three and kronecker_ne_jacobi_at_two_five, which are kernel witnesses of the chi8-versus-legendreSym-2 disagreement that made run 3 build its own symbol. SCOPE, LOUDLY (LL-1), none of which is hidden: (a) ODD MODULUS ONLY, both halves. DRK-10 delivers NOTHING for the even-c branch of the Petersson multiplier and must not be read as closing the Dedekind-sum-to-character bridge. (b) The numerator is h : N, as upstream; a consumer needing s(d,c) with d < 0 must first go through dedekindSum_add_mul / dedekindSum_neg. (c) Half 2 says nothing about kroneckerSym a d for d < 0 -- that branch carries the (if a<0 and d<0 then -1) sign factor, which the positivity of (b:N) kills here; extending to d < 0 is open. (d) The node's (hpos : 0 < b) on half 2 is REDUNDANT (Odd b already forces b != 0 in N). The node's binder list is landed verbatim anyway in kroneckerSym_eq_jacobiSym_of_odd, and the hypothesis-minimal kroneckerSym_eq_jacobiSym_of_odd' plus pos_of_odd_nat are supplied alongside; downstream code should use the primed form. (e) The Apostol theorem number attached to this result in the node brief was NOT verified and is not cited anywhere in the Lean. LL-22: every declaration here is Apostol's s(h,k) (dedekindSum). None is Phi and none is Rademacher's Psi. GATE (LL-2/LL-7): 28 #print axioms guards in FinalCheck.lean, section Drk10, every one [propext, Classical.choice, Quot.sound] -- no sorryAx, no new axiom. sorry=0 admit=0 axiom=0 in both new files. Full build: 'Build completed successfully (3784 jobs).'"}
{"id": "DRK-11A", "kind": "math", "lean_name": "SocrateAI.ModularForms.exp_etaPhiSum_eq_kroneckerSym_of_le_four", "lean_file": "Lean/SocrateAI/ModularForms/EtaLigozatKronecker.lean", "status": "proved", "depends_on": ["DRK-09", "F32-B3"], "paper_claim": "Ligozat's criterion in closed Dedekind-sum form, at the levels where run 3 already identified the multiplier.", "statement_nl": "PROVED.  exp_etaPhiSum_eq_kroneckerSym_of_le_four: for 0 < N <= 4, Sum_{delta | N} r delta = 2k, Ligozat's congruences (i) and (ii), gamma in Gamma0(N) and c = gamma 1 0 > 0, (-i)^k * exp(pi*i/12 * etaPhiSum N r gamma) = kroneckerSym (ligozatKroneckerNum N r k) (gamma 1 1).  This is DRK-11's exact conclusion on a nonempty domain.  Route: DRK-09 (etaMultiplierVal_eq_exp_etaPhiSum) says the left side IS the multiplier w(gamma); run 3's F3.2-B3 (multiplier_eq_kronecker_of_le_four) says w(gamma) IS Ligozat's Kronecker symbol at N <= 4; coe_etaMultiplierHom bridges the units coercion.  NO NEW MATHEMATICS is claimed -- what it buys is that DRK-11's statement, signs and all, is provably the same proposition run 3 proved, and it is what two consistency tripwires (drk11_general_matches_pin_N3_odd_k at d = 1 with symbol +1, drk11_general_matches_pin_N3_even_d at d = 2 EVEN with symbol -1) check against values computed OUTSIDE Lean.  SCOPE, LOUDLY (LL-1): (a) N <= 4 only; N = 5, 7, 13 are NOT covered -- run 3's prime-level file characterises the multiplier as the unique character with given generator values, never as a Kronecker symbol.  (b) c > 0 only, and this is not cosmetic: drk11_neg_control_c_zero is a kernel-checked witness at gamma = T in Gamma0(3), r = (-3,9), k = 3 (hk, h1, h2 all satisfied) where the two sides are i and 1.  So this does NOT close ETA-01 and does NOT delete F3.2-OBSTRUCTED.  PROVENANCE: independent (composition of two of our own results); nothing upstream is involved.  See ATTRIBUTION.md section 9.  GATE (LL-2/LL-7): 32 #print axioms guards in FinalCheck.lean, section Drk11, every one [propext, Classical.choice, Quot.sound].  Full build: 'Build completed successfully (3785 jobs).'"}
{"id": "DRK-11", "kind": "math", "lean_name": null, "lean_file": "Lean/SocrateAI/ModularForms/EtaLigozatKronecker.lean", "status": "blocked", "depends_on": ["DRK-02", "DRK-04", "DRK-09", "DRK-10", "DRK-11A", "F32-B3"], "paper_claim": "The eta-quotient multiplier is Ligozat's Kronecker character, at general level N.", "statement_nl": "BLOCKED (statement landed, one sorry with -- OPEN:).  exp_etaPhiSum_eq_kroneckerSym: for 0 < N, Sum_{delta | N} r delta = 2k, LigozatCongr1 N r, LigozatCongr2 N r, gamma in Gamma0(N) and c = gamma 1 0 > 0, (-i)^k * exp(pi*i/12 * etaPhiSum N r gamma) = kroneckerSym (ligozatKroneckerNum N r k) (gamma 1 1).  WHAT IS PROVED IN THE FILE, and it is not nothing: (1) the ENTIRE exponential layer, whose content is that this node is EQUIVALENT to a congruence mod 24 -- drk11_iff_congr says the identity holds iff etaPhiSum N r gamma - 6k = 24n (symbol +1) or 24n + 12 (symbol -1).  That reduction (neg_I_zpow_eq_exp, drk11_lhs_eq, exp_pi_div_twelve_eq_one_iff, exp_pi_div_twelve_eq_neg_one_iff) is a real structural result and removes ALL analysis from what remains.  (2) DRK-11A: the conclusion for 0 < N <= 4.  (3) The sign-discipline gate: ELEVEN decide+kernel pins of the node's exact conclusion at explicit (N, r, k, gamma), covering k = 12, 8, 3, 2, 0 and NEGATIVE k = -3; c odd (1,3,5,7,11) and c even (2,4); d = 0, d > 0 odd, d > 0 EVEN (the chi8 branch), d < 0 odd (the sign branch), d < 0 even; negative exponents r_delta; and both symbol values +1 and -1.  Every Phi and every symbol value was computed independently in python3 (exact Fraction arithmetic; Int.fract, dedekindSaw, dedekindSum, etaPhiSum, kroneckerPrime, kroneckerSym, ligozatKroneckerNum re-implemented from the Lean SOURCE) BEFORE the Lean was written, and that re-implementation reproduces every existing decide+kernel pin of DedekindSum.lean and EtaPhiSum.lean exactly.  The same sweep verified the statement at several hundred gamma in Gamma0(N) with c > 0 for N in {1,2,3,4,5,6,7,11}: zero mismatches.  (4) FOUR negative controls: two show Ligozat's congruences are load-bearing (N = 8 with Sum delta r = -4 and Sum (8/delta) r = 52; N = 12 with both sums 56), one shows hc : 0 < c is load-bearing (gamma = T in Gamma0(3): the two sides are i and 1), one shows the (-1)^k factor of ligozatKroneckerNum is load-bearing (at d = -1 the sign-free mutant gives +1 where the truth is -1).  WHAT IS MISSING, i.e. why this is blocked and not proved.  After drk11_iff_congr the remaining content is arithmetic: etaPhiSum - 6k mod 24.  The classical route replaces each 12*s(d, c/delta) by DRK-10 (dedekindSum_jacobiSym_mod_eight), but DRK-10 is ODD-MODULUS ONLY, so every level with 2 | c/delta is untouched and no even-modulus companion exists here or upstream.  Second, DRK-10 produces the symbol (d | c/delta) with d on TOP while Ligozat's character has delta on top and gamma 1 1 below, so jacobiSym.quadratic_reciprocity has to be applied divisor-by-divisor and the resulting signs collected against hk, h1 and h2.  Neither input is attempted.  SCOPE, LOUDLY (LL-1): the node is the c > 0 SLICE of Ligozat's theorem, not Ligozat's theorem.  With hc dropped the statement is FALSE (etaPhiSum degenerates to 0 at c = 0 by etaPhiSum_of_lower_left_zero, leaving (-i)^k), so even a fully proved DRK-11 would still need DRK-08's c < 0 reduction and the c = 0 case gamma = +-T^n before ETA-01.  F3.2-OBSTRUCTED stands.  hN : 0 < N is INERT (Gamma0 0 forces c = 0, contradicting hc); it is carried because the node carries it.  PROVENANCE: INDEPENDENT.  Path-substring search over the 45950-entry FLT recursive tree (fetched 2026-09-08, HTTP 200, 17425739 B, truncated=true): ligozat 0, Ligozat 0, kroneckerSym 0, etaQuotient 0; all 34 'kronecker' paths are Kronecker's congruence for modular polynomials or Matrix.kroneckerMap, none is the Kronecker SYMBOL.  grep -ri over pinned Mathlib (905b95818e): ligozat 0, kroneckerSym 0, etaQuotient 0, dedekindSum 0, etaMultiplier 0; the 9 'rademacher' hits are Rademacher's differentiability theorem.  HONESTY CORRECTION (LL-25), made rather than omitted: 'no counterpart in any form' is too strong by ONE instance -- ModularForm.etaProductEleven_transform (fetched 2026-09-08, HTTP 200, 936 B) is the N = 11, r = (2,2), k = 2 case with TRIVIAL character, and FLT proves it on ALL of Gamma0(11) with no c > 0 restriction.  drk11_pin_N11_even_d is that instance, proved here from our own kernel evaluation.  See ATTRIBUTION.md section 9.  GATE (LL-2/LL-7): FinalCheck.lean section Drk11 carries 32 standard-footprint guards plus an INVERTED tripwire certifying that exp_etaPhiSum_eq_kroneckerSym still depends on sorryAx; discharging the sorry breaks that guard and forces the same commit to update it.  sorry = 1, admit = 0, axiom = 0 in the file.  Full build: 'Build completed successfully (3785 jobs).'  RUN-5 UPDATE (2026-09-08): unchanged and still BLOCKED, but its position in the graph has sharpened. The 'even a fully proved DRK-11 would still need DRK-08's c < 0 reduction and the c = 0 case' clause of this node is now DISCHARGED: ETA-01A (etaMultiplierVal_eq_kroneckerSym_of_pos, Lean/SocrateAI/ModularForms/EtaLigozatGeneral.lean, sorry-free) proves that the c > 0 slice IMPLIES the statement on all of Gamma0(N). DRK-11 is therefore now the ONLY open input to ETA-01. The two missing arithmetic inputs named in this node's -- OPEN: comment are unchanged. NAMED PRECISELY (run 5, verified numerically, not proved): a single sufficient input is the Petersson closed form for Phi mod 24 -- for gamma in SL(2,Z) with c > 0, Phi(gamma) = (a+d)c - bd(c^2-1) - 3c + 3 + 12*[(d|c) = -1] (mod 24) when c is ODD, and Phi(gamma) = (a+d)c - bd(c^2-1) + 3d - 3cd + 12*[(c|d) = -1] (mod 24) when c is EVEN. Both branches were checked in python3 (exact Fraction arithmetic, Phi and dedekindSum re-implemented from the Lean source) at 4857 odd-c and 1686 even-c matrices covering c = 1..24 and d = -20..20: ZERO mismatches. With that lemma the remaining work in DRK-11 is the divisor-by-divisor collection against hk, h1 and h2 -- note that the '+3' of the odd branch cancels exactly against 6k = 3*sum r_delta, which is the structural reason Ligozat's two congruences are the right hypotheses. Neither the Petersson lemma nor the collection is attempted; it is a Euclidean induction on c using DRK-04 plus quadratic reciprocity, and it is a run of its own."}
{"id": "DRK-12", "kind": "math", "lean_name": "SocrateAI.ModularForms.ModularForm.etaProductEleven_transform", "lean_file": "Lean/SocrateAI/ModularForms/EtaLigozatLevelEleven.lean", "status": "proved", "depends_on": ["F32-A5", "F32-A6", "F32-A8", "F32-B3", "F32-C3", "DRK-09"], "paper_claim": "Ligozat's criterion at level 11: eta(z)^2 eta(11z)^2 is weight 2 on Gamma0(11), a level beyond run 3's reach.", "statement_nl": "PROVED, sorry-free.  ModularForm.etaProductEleven_transform: for every gamma in Gamma0(11) and every tau in H, eta(gamma.tau)^2 * eta(11*gamma.tau)^2 = denom(gamma,tau)^2 * (eta(tau)^2 * eta(11*tau)^2).  READ THIS FIRST, LL-1: THIS DOES NOT CLOSE ETA-01 AND DOES NOT USE ligozat_general.  ligozat_general, ligozat_kronecker_transform, etaMultiplierVal_eq_kroneckerSym and etaQuotientModularFormGeneral all still inherit DRK-11's sorry; FinalCheck.lean section Eta01 still carries the four INVERTED tripwires saying so, and they still pass.  What is proved here is ONE MORE LEVEL, by generating the group -- the way run 3 got 5, 7 and 13 -- not by a general theorem.  Anyone citing this node as having removed F3.2-OBSTRUCTED is citing it wrongly.  WHY IT IS NEW RELATIVE TO RUN 3.  Run 3's F3.2-C3 route reads each non-{-I,T,V} generator value off an ELLIPTIC FIXED POINT (etaMultiplierVal_matH_diag / _matH_succ).  Gamma0bar(11) is free of rank 3 with nu_2 = nu_3 = 0 -- NO elliptic elements -- so that technique supplies nothing at p = 11: the four Schreier generators h_{2,5}, h_{3,7}, h_{4,8}, h_{6,9} have traces -3, -4, -4, -3, all hyperbolic.  Their multiplier values come from DRK-09 instead, which EVALUATES the multiplier (w(gamma) = (-i)^k exp(pi i Phi/12)) rather than constraining it.  That is the ingredient run 3 did not have, and it is what makes level 11 reachable.  ROUTE.  (1) closure_gamma0GensP11: Gamma0(11) = <-I, T, V, h25, h37, h48, h69>, the p = 11 instance of run 3's Gamma0_eq_of_schreier; the six Schreier generators that are short words (h_{1,10} = T^-1 V^-1, h_{10,1} = (-I)VT, h_{j',j} = (-I) h_{j,j'}^-1) are single decide's on 2x2 integer matrices.  S_not_mem_closure_gensP11 certifies the closure is PROPER.  (2) w(-I) = (-1)^2 = 1, w(T) = 1 by Ligozat (i), w(V) = 1 by Ligozat (ii), and w(h) = (-i)^2 exp(pi i Phi/12) = 1 at each hyperbolic generator from DRK-09 plus a decide+kernel evaluation of etaPhiSum.  hom_ext_of_closure propagates to all of Gamma0(11): etaMultiplierHom_eleven_eq_one.  (3) etaQuotientH_transform then gives the law.  WHAT ELSE IS LANDED, sorry-free.  exp_etaPhiSum_eq_kroneckerSym_eleven -- DRK-11's EXACT conclusion at N = 11, r = (2,2), k = 2, on all of Gamma0(11) with c > 0.  DRK-11 was previously known only for 0 < N <= 4 (DRK-11A), and 11 is outside that range; the proof does not go through DRK-11A.  It does NOT close DRK-11, which is quantified over all N and all r.  Also etaMultiplierVal_eq_kroneckerSym_eleven (ETA-01's conclusion at the same data, no c > 0 needed) and etaQuotientH_eleven_slash (the slash_action_eq' field of ModularForm (Gamma0 11) 2).  WHAT IS NOT DELIVERED (LL-1, loudly).  FLT's CuspForm.exists_gamma0_eleven_apply_eq_eta_sq_mul_eta_sq (Theorems/, HTTP 200, 724 B) asserts existence of an element of CuspForm (Gamma0 11) 2 -- slash-invariance AND holomorphy AND VANISHING at every cusp.  Only the first conjunct is proved here.  Vanishing is F3.1-OBSTRUCTED; etaQuotientModularFormGeneral still takes mere BOUNDEDNESS as a hypothesis, so not even the ModularForm package is reachable at this level, let alone the CuspForm one.  The DRK-12 brief's obligation name etaProductEleven_via_ligozat_general has been kept, but as the OPEN comparator: it derives the same statement through ligozat_general, carries sorryAx, and is guarded as an INVERTED tripwire.  COMPARATORS, corrected (LL-1).  The brief asked for ligozat_general_agrees_le_four / _prime as an Eq between two PROOF TERMS.  That comparator is VACUOUS -- two proofs of one Prop are equal by rfl under definitional proof irrelevance, whether or not either is correct and whether or not one still contains sorryAx -- so it is deliberately NOT written.  What is written instead: (a) drk12_matches_pin_N11_even_d -- the generation route must reproduce drk11_pin_N11_even_d, a value fixed by a Python computation at gamma = !![3,1;11,4], a matrix that appears nowhere in the generation proof; (b) drk12_le_four_routeA / routeB -- at N = 4, r = (-8,32,-8), k = 8, gamma = !![1,0;4,1], run 3's F3.2-B3 route and the DRK-09 + kernel-Phi route both land on the numeral 1, by routes sharing no step; (c) the axiom-footprint contrast in FinalCheck.lean section Drk12: 53 POSITIVE guards versus ONE inverted tripwire on the ligozat_general route.  SIGN-DISCIPLINE GATE.  Twenty pins before any general proof.  Ten decide+kernel evaluations of etaPhiSum at the ten Schreier generators h_{j,j'}, 1 <= j <= 10 (values -36, -12, -12, -12, +12, -12, +12, +12, +12, +36; both signs of Phi occur and all ten are = 12 mod 24, which is exactly (-i)^2 exp(pi i Phi/12) = 1).  Every value was computed FIRST in python3 (fractions.Fraction; Int.fract, dedekindSaw, dedekindSum, etaPhiSum re-implemented from the Lean SOURCE), and that re-implementation reproduced drk11_phi_N11, drk11_phi_N3a/b/c/d and drk11_phi_N7 exactly before any new value was written.  The same script swept 2376 matrices of Gamma0(11) with c > 0 (c in 11..88, |a|,|d| <= 60): every Phi is an integer = 12 mod 24, zero mismatches.  TWO NEGATIVE CONTROLS: kroneckerSym 121 11 = 0 != 1 (so gamma0_not_dvd's 11 does not divide gamma_11 is load-bearing -- without it Ligozat's character at level 11 is ZERO, not trivial), and the ten Phi pins are not all one constant.  PROVENANCE: INDEPENDENT.  The STATEMENT is character-for-character FLT's Theorems/Thm_ModularForm_etaProductEleven_transform.lean (fetched 2026-09-08, HTTP 200, 936 B, Apache-2.0): after collapsing whitespace, FLT is 414 chars and ours is 304, and applying six notation substitutions to FLT's text brings it to 304 with the two strings comparing == True (python3, LL-17).  That overlap is NAMED, not hidden (LL-25), in ATTRIBUTION.md section 11.  It is NOT a port: FLT discharges the theorem with p2m_exact_reverting against its own solution infrastructure, which does not exist here, and P2M/Sol/S_ModularForm_etaProductEleven_transform.lean was not fetched and not read.  FLT tree receipts (45950 entries, truncated=true): schreier 0, Schreier 1 (Artin-Schreier, unrelated), cosetReps 2 (S_ModularCurve_*, neither fetched nor used), ligozat 0, kroneckerSym 0, etaQuotient 0, etaMultiplier 0.  Pinned Mathlib 905b95818e: ligozat 0, kroneckerSym 0, etaQuotient 0, etaMultiplier 0.  GATE (LL-2/LL-7): 54 #print axioms guards in FinalCheck.lean section Drk12 -- 53 POSITIVE ([propext, Classical.choice, Quot.sound]) and 1 INVERTED ([propext, sorryAx, Classical.choice, Quot.sound]) on etaProductEleven_via_ligozat_general.  Full build: 'Build completed successfully (3767 jobs).'"}
